hadiths[600]{hadithnumber,text}:
"2401","2394 - Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Khalid ibn al-Harith informed us, he said: Shuba informed us, from Yala ibn Ata, from his father, from Abd Allah ibn Amr (may Allah be pleased with them both), that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The pleasure of the Lord, Blessed and Exalted, is in the pleasure of the father, and the anger of the Lord is in the anger of the father."" And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it marfu except Khalid ibn al-Harith from Shuba. And I heard one of our companions mention it from Sahl ibn Hammad from Shuba marfu, and I rejected it against him."
"2402","2395 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna and Sulayman ibn Ubayd Allah narrated to us, they said: Muammal ibn Ismail informed us, from Sufyan, he said: Ata ibn al-Saib and Yala ibn Ata informed us, from their father, from Abd Allah ibn Amr (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: ""The sun eclipsed in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so the Messenger of Allah prayed two rakas in four prostrations."" And this hadith is well known from the hadith of Ata ibn al-Saib from his father from Abd Allah ibn Amr. As for the hadith of Yala ibn Ata, we do not know it narrated except by Muammal from al-Thawri, so he joined them."
"2403","2396 - Umar ibn al-Khattab narrated to us, he said: Adam ibn Abi Iyas informed us, he said: Shuba informed us, from Yala ibn Ata, from his father, from Abd Allah ibn Amr (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) seeking permission for jihad, and he said: ""Are your parents alive?"" He said: Yes. He said: ""Then go and be dutiful to them."""
"2404","2397 - Yusuf ibn Musa informed us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Numayr informed us, he said: al-Hajjaj ibn Artah informed us, from Ata, from Abd Allah ibn Amr (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: ""Do you fast the day and stand the night?"" I said: Yes. He said: ""Then do not do it, for when you do that, the eyes sink and the soul wearies; fast and break fast, and stand and sleep; fast three of the month, for that is the fast of the whole year. Your eye has a right, your soul has a right, and your family has a right."" I said: O Prophet of Allah, I find strength. He said: ""If you must do, then fast the fast of the Prophet of Allah - meaning Dawud (peace be upon him) - he would fast one day and break fast one day, and would not flee when he met (the enemy)."""
"2405","2398 - And Yusuf ibn Musa informed us of it, he said: Salama ibn al-Fadl informed us, he said: Ismail ibn Muslim informed us, from Ata from Abd Allah ibn Amr (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""He would not flee at meeting,"" meaning Dawud."
"2406","2399 - And Yusuf ibn Musa informed us, he said: Jarir ibn Abd al-Hamid informed us, from Mutarrif ibn Tarif, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Abu al-Abbas, from Abd Allah ibn Amr (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Have I not been informed that you stand the night and fast the day?"" I said: Yes indeed, O Messenger of Allah, and I intend thereby only good. He said: ""Do not do it, for when you do that, the eye sinks for it and the soul wearies for it. None who fasts perpetually has fasted, but I shall guide you to the fast of the whole year: three days of every month, for that is the fast of the whole year."" He said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, I can bear it. He said: ""Then fast five of the month."" I said: O Messenger of Allah, I can bear it. He said: ""Then fast ten."" I said: I can bear it. He said: ""Then fast the fast of Dawud: he would fast one day and break fast one day, and would not flee when he met."""
"2407","2400 - Salama narrated to us, he said: Rawwad ibn al-Jarrah informed us, he said: al-Awzai informed us, from Ata, from Abd Allah ibn Amr (may Allah be pleased with them both), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: ""None who fasts perpetually has fasted."""
"2408","2401 - Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Harun informed us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ishaq informed us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Abu al-Abbas, from Abd Allah ibn Amr (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: People who exerted themselves intensely in worship were mentioned before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: ""That is the eagerness of Islam, and every sharra (fervor) has a fatra (lapse); whoever’s lapse is toward moderation is not blamed - or there is no blame upon him - and whoever’s lapse is toward sins, those are the perished."""
"2409","2402 - Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Jarir ibn Abd al-Hamid informed us, he said: Ata ibn al-Saib informed us, from his father, from Abd Allah ibn Amr (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Worship the Most Merciful, spread peace, and feed food; you shall enter the Gardens."" And this wording, we do not know it narrated except by Abd Allah ibn Amr."
"2410","2403 - Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Jarir informed us, from Ata ibn al-Saib, from his father, from Abd Allah ibn Amr (may Allah be pleased with them both), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: ""Two traits none enumerates (preserves) except he enters Paradise; they are easy, and few act upon them: a man glorifies Allah after his prayer a hundred tasbihs, and magnifies and declares His oneness."""
"2411","2404 - Yusuf said: And Mihran ibn Umar ibn Abi Umar informed us of it, from Sufyan, from Ata ibn al-Saib, from his father, from Abd Allah ibn Amr (may Allah be pleased with them both), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). It was said: And how can one not enumerate them, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Satan comes to one of you and says to him: Remember the need of such-and-such, remember the need of such-and-such, until he leaves."
"2412","2405 - And Ibrahim ibn Abd Allah informed us, he said: al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Awwal informed us, he said: I heard Abu Khalid Sulayman ibn Hayyan narrate from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid, from Ata ibn al-Saib, from his father, from Abd Allah ibn Amr (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Good is much, and few act upon it."" And we do not know that Ismail ibn Abi Khalid narrated marfu from Ata ibn al-Saib except this hadith, nor did anyone narrate it from Ismail except Abu Khalid."
"2413","2406 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Bazi narrated to us, he said: Aththam ibn Ali informed us, he said: al-Amash informed us, from Ata ibn al-Saib, from his father, from Abd Allah ibn Amr (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: ""I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) counting tasbih on his fingers."" And we do not know that al-Amash narrated marfu from Ata ibn al-Saib except this hadith, nor did anyone narrate it from al-Amash except Aththam ibn Ali."
"2414","2407 - And Yusuf ibn Musa informed us, he said: Jarir ibn Abd al-Hamid informed us, he said: Ata ibn al-Saib informed us, from his father, from Abd Allah ibn Amr (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""A man went out strutting in the Jahiliyya wearing a hulla (fine suit), so Allah, Blessed and Exalted, commanded the earth and it seized him, and he is sinking in it until the Day of Resurrection."" And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from Abd Allah ibn Amr except through this way with this chain."
"2415","2408 - Abd al-Wahid ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salama informed us, from Ata ibn al-Saib, from his father, from Abd Allah ibn Amr."
"2416","2409 - And Yusuf ibn Musa informed us of it, he said: Jarir informed us, from Ata ibn al-Saib, from his father, from Abd Allah ibn Amr (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I have come to pledge to you upon hijra (emigration), while I left my parents weeping. He said: ""Then go and make them laugh as you made them weep,"" and he refused to accept his pledge."
"2417","2410 - Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Abd al-Malik informed us, he said: Hammad ibn Salama informed us, from Ata ibn al-Saib, from his father, from Abd Allah ibn Amr (may Allah be pleased with them both), that the Jews greeted the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said within themselves: Why does Allah not punish us? He said: So it was revealed: {And when they come to you, they greet you with what Allah does not greet you with, and say within themselves: Why does Allah not punish us for what we say}. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated except from Abd Allah ibn Amr, nor do we know it narrated from Ata ibn al-Saib except by Hammad ibn Salama."
"2418","2411 - Ibrahim ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Junayd narrated to us, he said: Ismail ibn Ibrahim informed us, he said: Shuayb ibn Safwan informed us, from Ata ibn al-Saib, from his father, from Abd Allah ibn Amr (may Allah be pleased with them both), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: ""There was a kid among many sheep; its mother would suckle it and satisfy it, then it broke loose and suckled all the sheep, yet was not satiated."" He said: ""The like of this is the like of people who come after you; a man among them is given what suffices a tribe or a nation, yet is not satiated."" And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except by Abd Allah ibn Amr, nor do we know a path for it from Abd Allah except this path."
"2419","2412 - al-Qasim ibn Muhammad al-Marwazi narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Uthman informed us, he said: Abu Hamza al-Sukkari informed us, from Ata ibn al-Saib, from his father, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, marfu, he said: ""There were people among the Children of Israil whom a guest sought hospitality with, and they had a bitch about to give birth; the bitch said: I shall not bark at my family’s guest tonight. He said: So her pups howled in her belly."" And the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) struck that as an example for people who shall be at the end of time, whose foolish shall overcome their best."
"2420","2413 - Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Abd Allah informed us, he said: Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash informed us, from Abu Husayn, from al-Qasim ibn Mukhaymira, from Abd Allah ibn Amr (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the Muslim servant complains (falls ill), Allah, Blessed and Exalted, commands those who write his deeds, saying: Write for him his deeds when he was free, until I take him or free him."
"2421","2414 - Ahmad ibn Sinan narrated to us, he said: Abu Muawiya informed us, from al-Amash, from Abu Ishaq, from Wahb ibn Jabir, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"2422","2415 - And Muhammad ibn Abi Ghalib narrated it to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Maslama informed us, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Muslim informed us, from Mutarrif, from Abu Ishaq, from Wahb ibn Jabir, from Abd Allah ibn Amr (may Allah be pleased with them both), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: ""Sufficient sin for a man is to neglect whom he provides for."" And this hadith has been narrated by a group from Abu Ishaq, so we sufficed with those we mentioned among them."
"2423","2416 - And Ibrahim ibn Abd Allah informed us of it, he said: Said ibn Muhammad informed us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Abd al-Malik ibn Said ibn Abjar al-Kindi informed us, from his father, from Talha ibn Musarrif, from Khaythama, he said: We were sitting with Abd Allah ibn Amr when a steward of his came to him and said: Have you given our dependents flour? He said: No. He said: Then go and give them, for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, then he mentioned the like of it."
"2424","2417 - Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Jarir and Abu Muawiya informed us, with the wording of Abu Muawiya, from al-Amash, from Shaqiq ibn Salama, from Masruq, he said: We entered upon Abd Allah ibn Amr when he came with Muawiya to Kufa, and he mentioned the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and said: He was neither obscene nor deliberately obscene, and he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Among the best of you are the best of you in character."""
"2425","2418 - Salama ibn Shabib narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq informed us, he said: Mamar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Isa ibn Talha, from Abd Allah ibn Amr (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at Mina upon a camel; a man came to him and said: I thought shaving was before sacrifice, so I shaved before sacrificing. He said: ""Sacrifice, and there is no harm."" He said: And another came to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, I thought shaving was before stoning, so I shaved before stoning. He said: ""Stone, and there is no harm."" He said: So he was not asked that day about anything a man put forward or delayed except he said: ""Do, and there is no harm."" And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from Abd Allah ibn Amr except with this chain, and a group narrated it from al-Zuhri, so we sufficed with Mamar."
"2426","2419 - Ahmad ibn Dawud al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: Sufyan ibn Uyayna informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Isa ibn Talha, from Abd Allah ibn Amr (may Allah be pleased with them both), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"2427","2420 - And Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Waddah informed us of it, he said: Wahb ibn Jarir informed us, he said: My father informed us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salama, from Abd Allah ibn Amr (may Allah be pleased with them both), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: ""The prayer of one sitting is half the prayer of one standing."" And the hadith of Isa ibn Talha from Abd Allah ibn Amr, we do not know it narrated except by Ibn Uyayna from al-Zuhri. And the hadith of Abu Salama, we do not know it narrated except by Wahb ibn Jarir from his father from Ibn Ishaq from al-Zuhri. And Yala ibn al-Harith and Shuayb ibn Khalid have narrated it from al-Zuhri from a freed slave of Abd Allah ibn Amr from Abd Allah ibn Amr."
"2428","2421 - Abu Kurayb narrated to us, he said: Abu Muawiya informed us, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from his father, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"2429","2422 - And Amr ibn Ali informed us of it, he said: Abd al-Wahhab informed us, from Ayyub, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from his father, from Abd Allah ibn Amr (may Allah be pleased with them both), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: ""Allah, Blessed and Exalted, does not take away knowledge by snatching it away, but takes away knowledge by taking away the scholars; when no scholar remains, people take ignorant leaders, and they go astray and lead astray."""
"2430","2423 - And Azhar ibn Jamil informed us of it, he said: Aththam ibn Ali informed us, he said: Hisham ibn Urwa informed us, from his father, from Abd Allah ibn Amr (may Allah be pleased with them both), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: ""Allah does not take away knowledge by snatching it away, but takes it by taking away the scholars; when no scholar remains, people take ignorant leaders, and they are asked and give fatwa without knowledge, so they go astray and lead astray."""
"2431","2424 - And Ibrahim ibn Ziyad informed us, he said: Yahya ibn Adam informed us, he said: Qays ibn al-Rabi informed us, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from his father, from Abd Allah ibn Amr (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The affair of the Children of Israil remained upright until there appeared among them the children of the captives of the nations, so they gave fatwa by opinion, and went astray and led astray."" And this hadith, we do not know anyone who said from Hisham from his father from Abd Allah ibn Amr except Qays, while others narrated it mursal."
"2432","2425 - Abu Said Abd Allah ibn Said narrated to us, he said: Abu Yahya al-Taymi informed us, he said: Abu Sinan informed us, from Abd Allah ibn Abi al-Hudhayl, from Abd Allah ibn Amr (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: ""O Allah, I seek refuge in You from incapacity and laziness, and old age, and cowardice, and miserliness."""
"2433","2426 - And Muhammad ibn Bashshar informed us, he said: Abd al-Rahman informed us, from Sufyan, from Abu Sinan, from Abd Allah ibn Abi al-Hudhayl, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with the like of it."
"2434","2427 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abi Adi informed us, from Said, meaning Ibn Abi Aruba, from Qatada, from Abu Ayyub, from Abd Allah ibn Amr (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: ""When the sun passes the belly of the sky, the Dhuhr prayer is caught until one prays Asr, then the Asr prayer, while the sun is white and clear, is caught until the first horn of the sun falls; when the sun sets, the Maghrib prayer is caught until the twilight disappears; when the twilight disappears, the Isha prayer is caught until midnight; when dawn rises, the Subh prayer is caught until the first horn of the sun rises."""
"2435","2428 - And Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna informed us of it, he said: Muhammad ibn Jafar informed us, he said: Shuba informed us, he said: I heard Qatada say: I heard Abu Ayyub narrate from Abd Allah ibn Amr (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: ""The time of Dhuhr is while Asr has not come, the time of Asr is while the sun has not yellowed, the time of Maghrib is while the brightness of the twilight has not gone, the time of Isha prayer is until midnight, and the time of Subh prayer is while the sun has not risen."""
"2436","2429 - And Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna informed us of it, he said: Muadh ibn Hisham informed us, he said: My father narrated to me, from Qatada, from Abu Ayyub, from Abd Allah ibn Amr (may Allah be pleased with them both), that the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""When you pray Subh, its time is until the first horn of the sun rises; then when you pray Dhuhr, its time is until Asr comes; when you pray Asr, its time is until the sun yellows; when you pray Maghrib, its time is until the twilight falls; when you pray Isha, its time is until midnight."" And this hadith, we do not know it narrated with this wording except from Abd Allah ibn Amr with this chain. And Said ibn Abi Aruba did not raise it, while Muhammad ibn Yazid al-Wasiti raised it from Shuba, and none other than him raised it from him; Hisham and Hammam raised it, and the name of Abu Ayyub is Yahya ibn Malik."
"2437","2430 - Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Waki informed us, he said: Hammam - meaning Ibn Yahya - informed us, from Qatada, from Abu Ayyub, from Abd Allah ibn Amr (may Allah be pleased with them both), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: ""Whoever recites the Quran in less than three has not understood it."" And this hadith, we do not know anyone who said from Qatada from Abu Ayyub from Abd Allah ibn Amr except Waki from Hammam."
"2438","2431 - And Shuba opposed him, saying from Qatada from Yazid ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Shikhkhir from Abd Allah ibn Amr from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna informed us of it from Muhammad ibn Jafar from Shuba."
"2439","2432 - And Yusuf ibn Musa informed us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Maghra al-Dawsi informed us, he said: al-Amash informed us, from Abu Ayyub, from Abd Allah ibn Amr (may Allah be pleased with them both), the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The Hour shall not come until obscenity, severing of kinship, and bad neighborliness appear, and the trustworthy is deemed treacherous."" It was said: O Messenger of Allah, how shall the believer be on that day? He said: ""Like the palm tree: it fell yet was not broken, it was eaten yet was not corrupted, and it yielded goodness; and like a piece of gold entered into fire then brought out, only increased in goodness."" And this hadith, we do not know it narrated except from Abd Allah ibn Amr, nor do we know a path for it except this path, nor do we know that al-Amash narrated marfu from Abu Ayyub except this hadith."
"2440","2433 - Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Maslama informed us, he said: Abu Bakr ibn Abi Sabra informed us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abd Allah ibn Amr (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, is it of pride that I have a hulla (fine suit) and wear it? He said: ""No."" I said: Is it of pride that I have a mount and ride it? He said: ""No."" I said: Is it of pride that I prepare food and invite my companions? He said: ""No; pride is to belittle the truth and despise people."""
"2441","2434 - Bishr ibn Adam narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud informed us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abi al-Waddah informed us, he said: al-Ala ibn Abd Allah ibn Rafi informed us, from Hanan ibn Kharija, from Abd Allah ibn Amr (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: A Bedouin came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, inform us about hijra: is it to you wherever you are, or to you specifically, or to a known land, or when you die is it cut off? So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was silent for a while, then said: ""Where is the asker?"" He said: Here I am, O Messenger of Allah. He said: ""Hijra is to abandon al-fawahish (indecencies), what is apparent of them and what is hidden; then you are a muhajir, even if you die in the city."" He said: And Abd Allah said: And a man stood and said: O Messenger of Allah, inform us about the garments of the people of Paradise: are they created as creation or woven as weaving? So some of the people laughed, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""What do you laugh at? At an ignorant one asking a knowledgeable one? Where is the asker?"" He said: Here I am, O Messenger of Allah. He said: ""The fruits of Paradise shall split open with them."" And this hadith, we do not know it narrated with this wording except from Abd Allah ibn Amr, nor do we know a path for it except this path."
"2442","2435 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Raja informed us, he said: Hammam informed us, from Qatada, from Ibn Burayda, from Abu Sabra al-Hudhali, he said: The Hawd (Basin) was mentioned before Ibn Ziyad, so he sent for men among whom was Ibn Amr al-Muzani - meaning Aidh ibn Amr - and he sent for Abu Barza, who came to him in two cloaks, so Ibn Ziyad said: This Muhammadi of yours is short and stocky, and the old man heard it and said: I did not think I would live until I am reproached for the companionship of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: So Ibn Ziyad reclined, and when he was embarrassed by something he would recline, and a man said to him: The amir called you to ask you about the Hawd: did you hear the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mention it? He said: Yes, I heard him; whoever disbelieves in it, may Allah not give him to drink from it. Abu Sabra al-Hudhali said: Your father sent me to Muawiya, and I met Abd Allah ibn Amr, and he narrated to me a hadith from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), which I understood and wrote with my hand, so Ibn Ziyad said to him: I adjure you to ride the mule and sweat it until you bring the writing. He said: So I rode it and brought out the sahifa and came to him with it, and he said: Did you sweat the mule? I said: Yes, and he read the sahifa: In the name of Allah, the Most Merciful, the Most Compassionate. This is what Abd Allah ibn Amr narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Allah does not love the obscene nor the deliberately obscene. Then he said: ""By the One in Whose Hand is the soul of Muhammad, the Hour shall not come until obscenity and deliberate obscenity, bad neighborliness, and severing of kinship appear, and until the trustworthy is deemed treacherous and the treacherous is trusted."" Then he said: ""The like of the believer is like the palm tree: it fell and you ate goodness, then it fell yet neither corrupted nor broke; and the like of the believer is like a piece of red gold entered into fire and blown upon, neither changed nor diminished. By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, the best of martyrs are the just, the best of Muslims is he from whose tongue and hand the Muslims are safe, and the best of hijra is he who abandons what Allah and His Messenger have forbidden."" And he said: ""Your appointment is my Hawd, its width like its length, its expanse what is between Ayla and Makka, its pitchers as many as the stars of the sky, its drink whiter than silver; whoever comes to it and drinks from it shall never thirst after it ever."" And we do not know that Abu Sabra narrated from Abd Allah ibn Amr except this hadith, nor did anyone narrate it from Abu Sabra except Abd Allah ibn Burayda."
"2443","2436 - Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Abu Muawiya informed us, from al-Amash, from Abu al-Safar, from Abd Allah ibn Amr (may Allah be pleased with them both): The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by me, I and my mother, while we were repairing a thatched hut of ours that had weakened, and he said: What is this, O Abd Allah? I said: A thatched hut of ours has weakened and we are repairing it. He said: ""O Abd Allah, the matter is quicker than that."" And this hadith, we do not know it narrated except from Abd Allah ibn Amr, and al-Amash did not narrate marfu from Abu al-Safar except this hadith."
"2444","2437 - Salama ibn Shabib narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Yazid informed us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Ziyad al-Ifriqi informed us, from Abd Allah ibn Yazid, from Abd Allah ibn Amr (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever’s head is cracked in the path of Allah and he seeks reward, is forgiven what came before that of sin."""
"2445","2438 - Salama narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Yazid informed us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Ziyad informed us, from Abd Allah ibn Yazid, from Abd Allah ibn Amr (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Do not marry women for their beauty, for perhaps their beauty shall destroy them; and do not marry them for their wealth, for perhaps their wealth shall make them transgress; but marry them for religion, and a black, mutilated slave-girl of religion is better."""
"2446","2439 - Salama narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Yazid informed us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Ziyad informed us, from Abd Allah ibn Yazid, from Abd Allah ibn Amr (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever loves a man for Allah and says: I love you for Allah, and they both enter Paradise, the one who loved shall be of higher rank than the other, joined with the one he loved for Allah."""
"2447","2440 - And Salama informed us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Yazid informed us, he said: Haywa ibn Shurayh informed us, he said: Rabia ibn Sayf al-Maafiri informed me, from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Hubuli, from Abd Allah ibn Amr (may Allah be pleased with them both), from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he saw Fatima his daughter and said to her: ""From where have you come, O Fatima?"" She said: I have come from behind the funeral of this man. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Did you reach with them al-kuda (the graves)?"" She said: No; and how would I reach it when I have heard from you what I heard? So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, had you reached with them, you would not have seen Paradise until the grandfather of your father sees it."""
"2448","2441 - Salama ibn Shabib narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Yazid informed us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Ziyad informed us, from Abd Allah ibn Yazid, from Abd Allah ibn Amr (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The whole world is but enjoyment, and nothing of the enjoyment of the world is better than the righteous woman."""
"2449","2442 - Salama narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Yazid informed us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Ziyad informed us, he said: Yazid ibn Yaqub al-Maafiri narrated to me, from Abd Allah ibn Yazid, from Abd Allah ibn Amr (may Allah be pleased with them both), that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: ""Allah, Blessed and Exalted, is more sparing of the blood of His believing servant than one of you of his precious wealth, until He takes him upon his bed."""
"2450","2443 - Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Qabisa informed us, he said: al-Thawri informed us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Saib, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"2451","2444 - And Zayd ibn Akhzam al-Tai informed us, he said: Abd al-Samad informed us, he said: Shuba informed us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Saib ibn Malik, from Abd Allah ibn Amr (may Allah be pleased with them both), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he prayed in the eclipse of the sun two rakas. And this hadith has been narrated by Ata ibn al-Saib from his father from Abd Allah ibn Amr, so we mentioned it from the hadith of Abu Ishaq from al-Saib from Abd Allah ibn Amr, because we do not know anyone who narrated it marfu from Shuba except Abd al-Samad, while others besides Abd al-Samad narrate it from Abu Ishaq from al-Saib mursal, and we do not know anyone who narrated it marfu from al-Thawri except Qabisa."
"2452","2445 - Khalid ibn Yusuf ibn Khalid narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, he said: Musa ibn Uqba informed us, he said: Ubayd Allah ibn Salman al-Agharr narrated to me, from his father, that Abd Allah ibn Amr said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""No believing man or believing woman falls ill except Allah makes it an expiation for his past sins."" And we do not know that Salman al-Agharr narrated marfu from Abd Allah ibn Amr from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except this hadith, nor do we know it narrated from Musa ibn Uqba except by Yusuf ibn Khalid."
"2453","2446 - Abda ibn Abd Allah al-Qasmali narrated to us, he said: Yazid informed us, from Abu Sad Said ibn al-Marzuban, from Maymun, from Abd Allah ibn Amr (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed a prayer, and when he said: ""Allah hears him who praises Him,"" a man behind him said: O Allah, to You is praise, abundant, good, blessed in it. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) finished, he said: ""Who is the sayer of the words?"" The man said: I am, O Messenger of Allah. He said: ""I saw a group of angels surrounding them and ascending with them, and I looked at them until they disappeared from me."" And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from Abd Allah ibn Amr except with this chain."
"2454","2447 - Muhammad ibn Bashshar Bundar narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Jafar informed us, he said: Shuba informed us, from Abu Balj, from Amr ibn Maymun, from Abd Allah ibn Amr (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: Whoever says: There is no god but Allah, and Allah is Greatest, and praise be to Allah, and there is no power nor strength except with Allah, his sins are forgiven, even if they are more than the foam of the sea."
"2455","2448 - And Muhammad ibn Bashshar informed us of it, he said: Muhammad ibn Abi Adi informed us, he said: Hatim ibn Abi Saghira Abu Yunus informed us, from Abu Balj, from Amr ibn Maymun, from Abd Allah ibn Amr (may Allah be pleased with them both), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with the like of it. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it except Abu Yunus, and he is thiqa (trustworthy)."
"2456","2449 - Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Jafar informed us, he said: Shuba informed us, he said: I heard Abu Balj narrate from Amr ibn Maymun, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, that he said: ""Had the servants not sinned, Allah would have created a creation who sin, then He forgives them; indeed, He is the Forgiving, the Merciful."""
"2457","2450 - And Yahya ibn Muhammad ibn al-Sakan informed us of it, he said: Yahya ibn Kathir informed us, he said: Shuba informed us, from Abu Balj, from Amr ibn Maymun, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with the like of it. And this hadith, Muhammad ibn Jafar did not raise it, while Yahya ibn Kathir and Shababa ibn Sawwar raised it."
"2458","2451 - Abu Kurayb narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad al-Muharibi informed us, from al-Ifriqi Abd al-Rahman ibn Ziyad, from Bakr ibn Sawada and Abd al-Rahman ibn Rafi, from Abd Allah ibn Amr (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""When the imam completes his prayer, then breaks his wudu before saluting, his prayer is complete."" And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except by Abd Allah ibn Amr. And Abd al-Rahman ibn Rafi, we do not know anyone who narrated from him except al-Ifriqi, and he was not a memorizer of hadith, nor do we know a path for it except this path."
"2459","2452 - Ahmad ibn Abda narrated to us, he said: Umar ibn Ali informed us, he said: Nafi ibn Umar informed us, from Bishr ibn Asim, from his father, from Abd Allah ibn Amr (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Allah, Blessed and Exalted, hates the eloquent of men who moves his tongue about as the cow moves about with its tongue."" And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except by Abd Allah ibn Amr, nor do we know a path for it from Abd Allah except this path."
"2460","2453 - Bishr ibn Adam and Salama ibn Shabib narrated to us, they said: Abd Allah ibn Yazid informed us, he said: Said ibn Abi Ayyub informed us, he said: Kab ibn Alqama narrated to me, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Jubayr, from Abd Allah ibn Amr (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""When you hear the muadhhin, say as he says, and send blessings upon me, for there is none who sends a blessing upon me except Allah sends ten upon him; and ask Allah for me al-Wasila, for al-Wasila is a station in Paradise befitting none but a servant of the servants of Allah, and I hope I am he; and whoever asks it for me, my intercession becomes due for him on the Day of Resurrection."" And this hadith, similar words have been narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) through several ways, and we do not know it narrated with this wording except from Abd Allah ibn Amr with this chain."
"2461","2454 - And al-Hasan ibn Ahmad ibn Abi Shuayb al-Harrani informed us, he said: Muhammad ibn Salama al-Harrani informed us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from al-Walid ibn Abda, he said: I heard Abd Allah ibn Amr ibn al-As say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbid wine, and maysir (gambling), and al-kuba (a drum), and al-ghubayra (an intoxicant), and he said: ""Every intoxicant is forbidden."""
"2462","2455 - And Salama ibn Shabib informed us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Yazid informed us, he said: Said ibn Abi Ayyub informed us, he said: Ayyash ibn Abbas informed me, from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Hubuli, from Abd Allah ibn Amr (may Allah be pleased with them both), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: ""Killing in the path of Allah expiates everything except debt."""
"2463","2456 - And Salama ibn Shabib informed us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Yazid informed us, he said: Haywa ibn Shurayh informed us, he said: Abu Hani al-Khawlani informed us, that he heard Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Hubuli say: I heard Abd Allah ibn Amr say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""Allah decreed the decrees before He created the heavens and earth by fifty thousand years."""
"2464","2457 - And Salama informed us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Yazid informed us, he said: Said - meaning Ibn Abi Ayyub - informed us, he said: Maruf ibn Suwayd al-Judhami narrated to me, from Abu Ushshana al-Maafiri, from Abd Allah ibn Amr (may Allah be pleased with them both), from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: ""Do you know the first of Allah’s creation to enter Paradise?"" They said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: ""The first of Allah’s creation to enter Paradise are the poor emigrants, by whom the frontiers are guarded and hardships warded off; one of them dies while his need is in his chest, unable to fulfill it; and the Almighty, Blessed and Exalted, says to whom He wills of His angels: Go to them and greet them. So the angels say: Our Lord, we are the dwellers of Your heaven and the choicest of Your creation; do You command us to go to these and salute them? He says: They were servants of Mine, worshipping Me, associating nothing with Me; by them the frontiers are guarded and hardships warded off."" He said: So the angels come to them at that, entering upon them from every gate: {Peace be upon you for what you endured; excellent is the final Home}."
"2465","2458 - Salama narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Yazid informed us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Ziyad ibn Anum informed us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Rafi, from Abd Allah ibn Amr (may Allah be pleased with them both), that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by two gatherings in his mosque, one of the two gatherings supplicating Allah and beseeching Him, while the other learned fiqh and taught it. He said: ""Both gatherings are upon good, and one of them is better than its companion. As for these, they supplicate Allah and beseech Him; if He wills He gives them, and if He wills He withholds from them. As for these, they learn knowledge and teach the ignorant, so they are better; and I was only sent as a teacher."" Then he sat with them."
"2466","Salama ibn Shabib narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Yazid informed us, he said: Sa'id ibn Abi Ayyub informed us, he said: Ayyash ibn Abbas narrated to me, from Isa ibn Hilal al-Sadafi, from Abdullah ibn Amr, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: A man came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Teach me to recite, O Messenger of Allah. The Messenger of Allah said to him: Recite three from those beginning with Alif-Lam-Ra. The man said: My age is advanced, my heart has grown hard and my tongue has grown heavy. He said: Then recite three from those beginning with Ha-Mim. He said the same as his first statement. He said: Then recite three from the Musabbihat. He said the same as his statement. Then he said: Teach me, O Messenger of Allah, a comprehensive surah. So he taught him (When the earth is shaken) until he finished it. The man said: By the One Who sent you with the truth, I will never add anything to it. Then the man turned away, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The little man has prospered, the little man has prospered. Then he said: Bring him to me. He said to him: I have been commanded to take the day of sacrifice as a festival which Allah has made for this ummah. The man said: What if I find nothing but a loaned milch animal to sacrifice? He said: No; rather take from your hair, trim your nails, shorten your mustache and shave your pubic hair; that is the completion of your sacrifice with Allah, blessed and exalted."
"2467","Salama narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Yazid informed us, he said: Haywa, meaning Ibn Shurayh, informed us, he said: Abu Hani informed me that he heard Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Hubuli, that he heard Abdullah ibn Amr saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: All the hearts of the children of Adam are between two fingers of the fingers of the Most Merciful, blessed and exalted; He turns them wherever He wills. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, Turner of the hearts, turn our hearts to Your obedience."
"2468","Salama informed us, he said: Abdullah ibn Yazid informed us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Ziyad informed us, from Abdullah ibn Yazid, from Abdullah ibn Amr, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said. [The text ends here in the source without the wording of the hadith.]"
"2469","Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Yusuf ibn Kamil al-Attar informed us, he said: Nafi ibn Umar al-Jumahi informed us, from Ibn Abi Mulayka, from Abdullah ibn Amr, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: My Hawd (Pool) is a month's journey; its water is whiter than milk, its scent is sweeter than musk, and its cups are like the stars of the sky; whoever drinks a drink from it will never thirst after it, ever. Asma bint Abi Bakr said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I will be at my Hawd watching who comes to me from among you, and some people will be pulled away from me, so I will say: O Lord, my ummah; and He will say: You do not know what they did after you, or: Do you know what they did after you? They kept turning back on their heels, retreating backward. He said: And Ibn Abi Mulayka used to say: O Allah, we seek refuge in You from turning back on our heels or being tempted away from our religion."
"2470","Abd al-A'la ibn Hammad narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salama informed us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Suhayb al-Hadhdha, from Abdullah ibn Amr, may Allah be pleased with them both, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever kills a sparrow without its right, Allah will question him about it on the Day of Resurrection. It was said: And what is its right? He said: He slaughters it properly, and does not seize it by its neck and cut it off."
"2471","Abd al-Wahid ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salama informed us, from Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, from his father, from Abdullah ibn Amr, may Allah be pleased with them both, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: How do you fast? I said: I fast and do not break my fast. He said: Fast and break your fast; fast three days of the month. He said: Give me more, O Messenger of Allah, for I have strength. He said: I kept decreasing for him and he kept bargaining with me, until he said: Fast the most beloved fast to Allah, blessed and exalted: the fast of Dawud; he used to fast a day and break fast a day. Then when Abdullah grew old he said: That I had stopped at what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded me would be dearer to me than whatever the sun rises upon; but I will not abandon an obligation which the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) imposed upon me."
"2472","And Abd al-Wahid ibn Ghiyath informed us, he said: Hammad ibn Salama informed us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Ata ibn Farrukh, from Abdullah ibn Amr, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with similar wording."
"2473","Abd al-Wahid ibn Ghiyath informed us, he said: Hammad ibn Salama informed us, he said: Thabit informed us, from Shu'ayb, from his father, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Fast one day and you have ten days. He said: Give me more, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Fast two days and you have nine days. He said: Give me more, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Fast three days and you have eight days. Thabit said: I informed Mutarrif ibn Abdullah of that, and he said: I see it only as an increase in deed and a decrease in reward."
"2474","Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: al-Dahhak ibn Makhlad informed us, he said: Yunus ibn al-Harith informed us, from Amr ibn Shu'ayb, from his father, from his grandfather, who said: This verse was not revealed except concerning the people of Qadar (the deniers of divine decree): (Indeed the criminals are in error and madness * On the day they are dragged into the Fire on their faces: Taste the touch of Saqar * Indeed We created everything with decree)."
"2475","Salama ibn Shabib narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Bishr informed us, he said: Yunus ibn al-Harith informed us, from Amr ibn Shu'ayb, from his father, from his grandfather, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever says: Glory be to Allah and with His praise, a palm tree is planted for him in Paradise."
"2476","Abd al-A'la ibn Hammad narrated to us, he said: Hammad informed us, from Ya'la ibn Ata, from Nafi ibn Asim, from Abdullah ibn Amr, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever drinks wine and becomes intoxicated, his prayer is not accepted for forty nights; if he repents, Allah accepts his repentance. If he drinks it and becomes intoxicated, his prayer is not accepted for forty nights; if he repents, Allah accepts his repentance. If he drinks it and becomes intoxicated, his prayer is not accepted for forty nights; if he repents, Allah accepts his repentance. If he drinks it a fourth time and becomes intoxicated, his prayer is not accepted for forty nights, and if he repents, Allah will not accept his repentance, and it will be binding upon Allah, blessed and exalted, to give him to drink from the spring of al-Khabal, or the river of al-Khabal. It was said: And what is the spring of al-Khabal or the river of al-Khabal? He said: The pus of the people of the Fire."
"2477","Abd al-A'la ibn Hammad narrated to us, he said: Hammad informed us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Amr ibn Shu'ayb, from his father, from his grandfather, that he said: O Messenger of Allah, shall I write from you what I hear? He said: Yes. I said: Even what you say in pleasure and in anger? He said: Yes, for I do not utter in that any word except the truth."
"2478","Muhammad ibn al-Layth al-Haddadi narrated to us, he said: Zakariyya ibn Adi informed us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Amr informed us, from Abd al-Karim, from Amr ibn Shu'ayb, from his father, from his grandfather, that a man said: O Messenger of Allah, I gave my mother a garden during her lifetime, and she has died leaving no heir besides me. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, I think he said: Allah, blessed and exalted, has returned your garden to you and accepted your charity."
"2479","Ahmad ibn Malik narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Warith ibn Sa'id informed us, he said: Amir al-Ahwal informed us, from Amr ibn Shu'ayb, from his father, from his grandfather, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no divorce before marriage, and no freeing before ownership, or he said: There is no freeing except after ownership."
"2480","Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Abu Mu'awiya informed us, he said: al-A'mash informed us, from Abu al-Safar, from Abdullah ibn Amr, who said: A man from those before you would have a mile between his shoulders."
"2481","And al-Hasan ibn Khalaf informed us, he said: Ishaq ibn Yusuf informed us, he said: Sufyan informed us, from al-A'mash, from Abu al-Safar, from Abdullah ibn Amr, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: A man from those before you would reach eighty years before he had a wet dream."
"2482","Ibrahim ibn Sa'id al-Jawhari narrated to us, he said: Abu Usama informed us, he said: Hisham ibn Urwa informed us, from his father, from Abdullah ibn Amr, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: The angels were created from light."
"2483","Abdullah ibn Ishaq al-Attar narrated to us, he said: Affan informed us, he said: Hammam ibn Yahya informed us, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from his father, from Abdullah ibn Amr, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: The son of Adam who killed his brother will share half the punishment of the people of the Fire with them, an exact share."
"2484","And Muhammad ibn al-Ala informed us, he said: Abu Mu'awiya informed us, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from his father, from Abdullah ibn Amr, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: There is none of Allah's creation more numerous than the angels; He creates them like flies, then the blessed and exalted says: Be a thousand, two thousand."
"2485","And Muhammad ibn Bashir informed us, he said: Abu Dawud informed us, he said: Shu'ba informed us, from Abu Balj, from Amr ibn Maymun, from Abdullah ibn Amr, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: There will come upon Hell a time when its doors will rattle with no one in it, meaning among the monotheists."
"2486","Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Jarir informed us, from Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, from his father, from Abdullah ibn Amr, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Two qualities which whoever guards will admit him into Paradise, and they are easy, yet few act upon them: you praise Allah, magnify Him and glorify Him after every prescribed prayer ten times each, and when you go to your bed you glorify Allah, praise Him and magnify Him a hundred times; that is two hundred and fifty upon the tongue, and two thousand five hundred upon the scale. So which of you commits two thousand five hundred evil deeds in a day and night? They said: And how is it that few act upon them? He said: Satan comes to one of you in his prayer and reminds him of such-and-such need, so he does not say them; and he comes to him at his sleep and puts him to sleep, so he does not say them."
"2487","Abdullah ibn Abi Thumama al-Ansari narrated to us, he said: Affan informed us, he said: Hammad, meaning Ibn Salama, informed us, from Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, from his father, from Abdullah ibn Amr, may Allah be pleased with them both, that a man came to the prayer and said: Praise be to Allah, Lord of the worlds. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Who said it? The man said: I did. He said: I saw the angels receiving it from one another."
"2488","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abi Adi informed us, from Sulayman al-Taymi, from Aslam al-Ijli, from Bishr ibn Shighaf, from Abdullah ibn Amr, may Allah be pleased with them both, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about the Trumpet (al-Sur), and he said: A horn that will be blown into."
"2489","And Abd al-A'la ibn Zayd informed us, he said: Khallad ibn Yahya informed us, from Sufyan al-Thawri, from Sulayman al-Taymi, from Aslam al-Ijli, from Bishr ibn Shighaf, from Abdullah ibn Amr, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with similar wording."
"2490","Amr ibn Abdullah al-Awdi narrated to us, he said: Waki informed us, from Mis'ar, and Sufyan from Sa'd ibn Ibrahim, from Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abdullah ibn Amr - Sufyan raised it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and Mis'ar stopped it (as a Companion's statement) - he said: Among the major sins is that a man reviles his parents. They said: And how does he revile his parents? He said: A man reviles another man's father, so he reviles his father; and he reviles his mother, so he reviles his mother."
"2491","Rawh ibn Hatim narrated to us, he said: Shihab ibn Abbad informed us, he said: Dhawwad ibn Ulba informed us, he said: Mutarrif informed us, from Sa'id ibn Zarbi, from Abdullah ibn Amr, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Abdullah ibn Amr, how will you be when you remain among the dregs of the people whose covenants and trusts have been corrupted, and they differ so that they become like this, and he interlaced his fingers. He said: Then what should I do, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Take, I think he said, what you recognize, and leave what you disapprove of; and hold to your own private affairs, and beware of their common masses."
"2492","And I heard Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Bilal mentioning from Isa ibn Abdullah, from Ubaydullah ibn Amr, from Ayyub, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Uqba ibn Aws, from Abdullah ibn Amr, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with similar wording. And this hadith is narrated from Abdullah ibn Amr through various chains, and we do not know of an isnad better than the isnad of Uqba ibn Aws from Abdullah ibn Amr."
"2493","Talut ibn Abbad narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salama informed us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakra, who said: I came to Abdullah ibn Amr in his house with two rows of people around him and no one on his bed, so I sat on his bed near his feet. Then a red-faced man with a large belly came and sat down, and said: Who is the man? I said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakra. He said: Who is Abu Bakra? I said: Do you not remember the man who climbed down to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from the wall of Ta'if? He said: Yes indeed. Then he welcomed me, and began narrating to us, saying: It is imminent that the son of Hamal al-Da'n will emerge, three times. I said: And what is Hamal al-Da'n? A man said: One of whose parents is a devil; he will rule Rome, coming with a million people, five hundred thousand on land and five hundred thousand at sea, landing in a land called al-Amiq. He will say to his companions: I have some remainder in your ship, so stay behind upon it; then he will burn it with fire. Then he will say: There is no Rome nor Constantinople for you; whoever wishes to flee, let him flee. The Muslims will reinforce one another until the people of Aden Abyan reinforce them. The Muslims will say to them: Join them and be a single pass. They will fight for a month until horses wade in their hooves in blood. The believer will have on that day a double share of reward over what was before, except those who were among the companions of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). When the last day of the month comes, Allah, blessed and exalted, will say: Today I unsheathe My sword, aid My religion and avenge My enemy. Allah will turn the circle against them and defeat them, until Constantinople is opened. Their leader will say: No spoils today. While they are thus dividing gold and silver with their shields, it will be called out among them: Verily the Dajjal has replaced you in your homes. So they will leave what is in their hands and turn toward the Dajjal."
"2494","Muhammad ibn Thawab narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Numayr informed us, from Abdullah ibn Muslim, from Ibn Sabit, and he is Abd al-Rahman ibn Sabit, from Abdullah ibn Amr, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: In Paradise there is a palace called Adan, around it are towers and meadows; it has five thousand gates, at every gate five thousand chambers; none shall enter it, or dwell in it, except a prophet, or a truthful one, or a martyr, or a just ruler. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated with this wording except from Abdullah ibn Amr."
"2495","Tamim ibn al-Muntasir al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Numayr informed us, from al-A'mash, from Uthman ibn Umayr Abu al-Yaqzan, from Abu Harb ibn Abi al-Aswad, who said: I heard Abdullah ibn Amr saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Neither the dusty earth has carried nor the green sky has shaded a man more truthful than Abu Dharr. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from Abdullah ibn Amr except through this chain, and we do not know anyone who narrated it from al-A'mash except Abdullah ibn Numayr."
"2496","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik al-Qurashi narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Zayd informed us, he said: Abu Imran al-Jawni informed us, he said: Abdullah ibn Rabah al-Ansari wrote to me informing from Abdullah ibn Amr, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: I came early to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) one day, and two men differed over a verse, and their voices rose. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heard the sound and came out, I think he said: with anger recognizable on his face, and said: Verily those before you perished only because of their differing over the Book."
"2497","And al-Husayn ibn Ali ibn Ja'far al-Ahmar informed us of it, he said: Dawud ibn al-Rabi informed us, he said: Qays informed us, from Jabir, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Sabit, from Abdullah ibn Amr, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with similar wording."
"2498","Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Abu Ghassan informed us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Humayd informed us, from Sulayman al-A'mash, from Amr ibn Murra, from Abdullah ibn al-Harith, from Abdullah ibn Malik al-Zubaydi, from Abdullah ibn Amr, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent for Mu'awiya, and he was his scribe."
"2499","Zayd ibn Abdullah narrated to us, he said: Mu'awiya ibn Hisham informed us, from Sufyan, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Mujahid, from Abdullah ibn Amr, may Allah be pleased with them both, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The prayer of one sitting is half the prayer of one standing. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from al-Thawri, from Habib, from Mujahid, from Abdullah ibn Amr except Mu'awiya ibn Hisham."
"2500","Salama ibn Shabib informed us, he said: Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Faryabi informed us, he said: al-Awza'i informed us, he said: Rabi'a ibn Yazid narrated to me, he said: Abdullah al-Daylami narrated to me, he said: I said to Abdullah ibn Amr: It has reached me from you that you narrate from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: Whoever drinks wine, a single drink, his prayer is not accepted for forty mornings. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever drinks wine, a single drink, his repentance is not accepted for forty mornings; if he repents, Allah accepts his repentance. If he returns, his repentance is not accepted for forty mornings; if he repents, Allah accepts his repentance. If he returns, his repentance is not accepted for forty mornings; and if he repents, al-Awza'i said: I do not know whether in the third or the fourth, it will be binding upon Allah to give him to drink from the clay of al-Khabal or the dregs of al-Khabal."
"2501","Salama ibn Shabib narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Mughira Abd al-Quddus ibn al-Hajjaj informed us, he said: Hisham ibn al-Ghaz informed us, from Amr ibn Shu'ayb, from his father, from his grandfather, who said: We descended with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from the pass of al-Adhakhir. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) looked, and I was wearing a cloth dyed with safflower. He said: What is this? I realized the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) disliked it, so I went to my family while they were heating their oven, wrapped it up and threw it in. Then I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: What did the cloth do? I said: I recognized what you disliked in it, O Messenger of Allah, so I went to my family while they were heating their oven and threw it into it. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Why did you not clothe some of your family with it. He mentioned that when he descended from the pass of al-Adhakhir, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed with them toward a wall which he took as a qibla. A young sheep came wanting to pass in front of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he kept drawing near and warding it off until I saw the belly of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pressed against the wall, and it passed behind him."
"2502","Hudba ibn Khalid narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salama informed us, from Thabit, from Amr ibn Shu'ayb, from his father, from his grandfather, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever says in a day a hundred times: There is no god but Allah alone, without partner; to Him belongs dominion and to Him belongs praise, and He is over all things powerful, no one before him will have reached him, nor will anyone after him catch up with him, except one who does better than his deed."
"2503","Al-Sakan ibn Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Umar ibn Yunus informed us, he said: Isma'il ibn Hammad informed us, from Muqatil ibn Hayyan, from Amr ibn Shu'ayb, from his father, from his grandfather, who said: We were sitting with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when Abu Bakr and Umar came with a crowd of people, and their voices had risen. Abu Bakr sat near the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and Umar sat near. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Why have your voices risen? A man said: O Messenger of Allah, Abu Bakr said: Good deeds are from Allah and evil deeds are from ourselves. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: And what did you say, O Umar? He said: I said: Good and evil are from Allah. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The first to speak concerning it were Jibril and Mika'il; Mika'il said your statement, O Abu Bakr, and Jibril said your statement, O Umar. They said: Shall we differ so the people of heaven differ? And if the people of heaven differ, the people of earth will differ. So they sought judgment from Israfil, and he judged between them that good and evil are from Allah. Then he turned to Abu Bakr and Umar and said: Preserve my judgment between you both: Had Allah willed that we not disobey Him, He would not have created Iblis."
"2504","Musa ibn Abdullah Abu Talha narrated to us, he said: Bakr ibn Sulayman informed us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Yahya ibn Urwa, from his father, who said: I said to Abdullah ibn Amr: What is the most you saw Quraysh inflict upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in what they displayed of enmity toward him? He said: I was present with them when their nobles gathered one day in al-Hijr, and they mentioned and said: We have never seen the like of our patience with this man ever; he has declared our minds foolish, reviled our forefathers, faulted our religion and divided our unity; we have endured from him a grave matter. While they were thus, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came walking until he touched the Corner. When he passed by them, they winked at him, and I recognized it in the face of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). When he passed by them the second time, they winked at him likewise, and I recognized that in his face. He passed by them a third time and they winked at him likewise. Then he said: Listen, O company of Quraysh; by the One in Whose hand is the soul of Muhammad, I have indeed come to you with slaughter. The people were seized with gloom until there was not a man among them but that it was as if a bird had fallen upon his head, until the harshest of them toward him before that met him with the best speech he could find, saying: Go away, O Abu al-Qasim; go away rightly guided; by Allah, you were never ignorant. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) left. The next day they gathered, and I was with them. Some of them said to others: You mentioned what you suffered from him and what reached you about him, until when he brought you what you dislike, you left him. While they were thus, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) appeared. They said: Rise against him with the rising of one man. They kept saying: Are you the one who says such-and-such, for what reached them of his faulting their gods. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would say: Yes, I am the one who says that. One of them seized the folds of his cloak. Abu Bakr stood in front of him weeping, saying: (Do you kill a man for saying: My Lord is Allah). Then they left him. That was the harshest I ever saw Quraysh inflict upon him, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. The end of the twenty-third part and the beginning of the twenty-fourth, and praise be to Allah abundantly."
"2505","The Musnad of Salman al-Farisi, may Allah be pleased with him. The hadith of Salman. Abu al-Hasan Muhammad ibn Ayyub al-Raqqi narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Amr ibn Abd al-Khaliq al-Bazzar informed us, he said: Muhammad ibn Isma'il and Ibrahim ibn Sa'id informed us, and the wording is that of Muhammad, from Sa'id ibn Muhammad al-Warraq, who said: Musa al-Juhani informed us, from Zayd ibn Wahb, from Atiyya ibn Amir, from Salman al-Farisi, may Allah be pleased with him, that he was compelled to eat food, so he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: The most satiated people in this world will be the hungriest in the Hereafter. O Sulayman, the world is the prison of the believer and the paradise of the disbeliever."
"2506","Musa ibn Abdullah al-Khuza'i narrated to us, he said: Bakr ibn Sulayman informed us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ishaq informed us. And Amr ibn Ali informed us, he said: Abdullah ibn Harun ibn Abi Isa informed us, from his father, from Ibn Ishaq, that he heard Asim ibn Umar ibn Qatada, from Mahmud ibn Labid, from Abdullah ibn Abbas, who said: Salman al-Farisi narrated to me his story from his own mouth. He said: I was a Persian man from the people of Asbahan, from a village of it called Jayy. My father was the headman of his village, and I was the dearest of Allah's creation to him; his love for me kept him confining me in his house as a slave girl is confined. I strove in Magianism until I became the keeper of the fire, kindling it and never letting it die down for an hour. My father had a great estate, and one day he was occupied, so he said to me: O my son, I am occupied today with my estate; go to it and inspect it. He commanded me concerning some of what he wanted in it. Then he said to me: Do not be detained from me, for if you are detained from me, you will be more important to me than my estate and will occupy me from everything. I went out intending his estate, traveling to it, and passed by a church of the Christians' churches. I heard their voices in it while they were praying, and I did not know people's affairs because of my father's confining me in his house. When I heard their voices, I entered upon them to see what they were doing. When I saw them, their prayer pleased me and I desired their matter, and I said: By Allah, this is better than the religion we are upon. I did not leave them until the sun set, and I neglected my father's estate. Then I said to them: Where is the origin of this religion? They said: A man in Syria. Then I returned to my father, who had sent seeking me and whom I had occupied from his work. He said: O my son, where were you? Did I not entrust to you what I entrusted? I said: I passed by people praying in a church of theirs, entered to them and remained with them while they prayed until the sun set. He said: O my son, there is no good in that religion; your religion and your fathers' religion is better than it. Then he confined me in his house. I sent to the Christians saying: When a caravan comes to you from Syria, inform me of them. A caravan of Syrian Christian merchants came to them, and they informed me of them. I said to them: When they finish their needs and intend to return to their land, let me know. When they intended to return to their land, they informed me, so I cast off the iron from my feet and went out with them until I reached Syria. When I reached it, I said: Who is the most knowledgeable of this religion? They said: The bishop in the church. I came to him and said: I have desired this religion, and I wish to be with you, serving you in your church, learning from you and praying with you. He said: Enter. I entered with him, and he was an evil man: he would command charity and urge them to it, but when they gathered something of it to him, he hoarded it for himself and gave no one anything, until he amassed jars of gold and silver. I hated him intensely for what I saw him doing. Then he died, and the Christians gathered to bury him. I said to them: This was an evil man; he commanded you with charity and urged you to it, but when you brought it to him, he hoarded it for himself and gave no one, or gave the poor nothing of it. They said: How do you know that? I said: I will show you his treasure. They said: Show us. I showed them, and they extracted gold and silver. When they saw it, they said: By Allah, you shall never bury him. So they crucified him, then stoned him. There was another man there, and they put him in his place. Salman says: I never saw a man who does not pray the five prayers better than him, more ascetic in this world, more desirous of the Hereafter, nor more diligent night and day than him. I loved him with a love I never loved anything before. I remained with him a time, then death came to him. I said to him: O so-and-so, I was with you and loved you with a love I never loved anything before you, and what you see of Allah's decree has come to you; to whom do you commend me, and what do you command me? He said: O my son, by Allah, I do not know anyone upon what I was upon; the people have perished, altered and abandoned much of what they were upon, except a man in Mosul, and he is so-and-so, and he is upon what I was upon; so join him. When he died and was buried, I joined the companion of Mosul. I said to him: O so-and-so, so-and-so commended me at his death to join you, and informed me that you are upon his matter. He said: Stay with me. I stayed with him and found him the best man upon his companion's matter. I had hardly stayed when he died. When death came to him, I said to him: O so-and-so, so-and-so commended me to you and commanded me to join you, and what you see of Allah's decree has come; to whom do you commend me, and what do you command me? He said: O my son, by Allah, I do not know a man upon the like of what we were upon except a man in Nasibin, and he is so-and-so; so join him. When he died and was buried, I joined the companion of Nasibin. I came to him and informed him of what his companion commanded me. He said: Stay with me. I stayed with him and found him upon the matter of his two companions; I stayed with the best man. By Allah, he had hardly remained when death descended upon him. When he was dying, I said to him: O so-and-so, so-and-so commended me to so-and-so, and so-and-so commended me to you; to whom do you commend me, and what do you command me? He said: O my son, I do not know anyone remaining upon what I command you to come to except a man in Ammuriya of the land of Rome, upon the like of what we are upon; he is upon our matter. When he died and was buried, I joined the companion of Ammuriya. I informed him of my story. He said: Stay with me. I stayed with the best man upon the guidance of his companions and their matter. I earned until I had some cows and a few sheep. Then Allah's decree descended upon him. When he was dying, I said to him: O so-and-so, I was with so-and-so, who commended me to so-and-so; then so-and-so commended to so-and-so; then so-and-so commended me to so-and-so; then so-and-so commended me to you; to whom do you commend me, and what do you command me? He said: By Allah, I do not know anyone more fit for you upon what we were upon among people for me to command you to come to; but the time of a prophet has cast its shadow over you: he is sent with the religion of Ibrahim, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him; he will emerge in the land of the Arabs, emigrating to a land between two lava tracts; he has signs that are not hidden: he eats gifts and does not eat charity; between his shoulders, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, is the seal of prophethood. If you can join that land, do so. Then he died and was buried. I remained in Ammuriya as long as Allah willed me to remain. Then some merchants of Kalb passed by me. I said to them: Will you carry me to the land of the Arabs, and I will give you these cows of mine and these sheep of mine? They said: Yes. I gave them and they carried me with them, until when they brought me to Wadi al-Qura, they wronged me and sold me to a Jewish man. I stayed with him and saw the palm trees, hoping it was the land my companion described to me, though it did not settle in my mind. While I was with him, a cousin of his from Banu Qurayza came to him and bought me from him, carrying me to Medina. By Allah, no sooner did I see it than I recognized it by my companion's description to me. I stayed there. Allah sent His Messenger (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he stayed in Mecca as long as he stayed, and I heard no mention of him, busy as I was with slavery. Then he emigrated to Medina. By Allah, I was at the top of a date-palm cluster for my master, doing some work for him in it, with my master sitting beneath me, when a cousin of his came until he stood over him and said: May Allah fight Banu Qayla; by Allah, they are now gathered around a man who has come to them from Mecca today, claiming he is a prophet. When I heard it, joy seized me until I thought I would fall upon my master. I came down from the palm tree, saying to that cousin of his: What are you saying? What are you saying? My master became angry and struck me a severe blow, then said to me: What is it to you? Attend to your work. I said: Nothing; I only wanted to ask him about what he said. I had something I had gathered; in the evening I took it and went to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was in Quba. I entered upon him and said to him: It has reached me that you are a righteous man, with companions of yours, strangers in need; and this is something I had as charity, and I saw you more deserving of it than others. I brought it near to him. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to his companions: Eat. He himself refrained and did not eat of it. I said to myself: This is one. Then I left him, gathered something, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) moved to Medina. Then I brought it to him and said to him: I saw you do not eat charity, and this is a gift with which I honor you. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ate of it and commanded his companions, so they ate. I said to myself: These are two. Then I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was in Baqi al-Gharqad, having followed the funeral of a man of his companions, sitting. I greeted him, then went behind to look at his back whether I could see the seal my companion described to me. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw me going behind him, he knew I was verifying something described to me, so he cast his cloak from his back. I looked at the seal and recognized it. I fell upon him kissing him and weeping. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Turn around. I turned and sat before him. I narrated to him my story as I narrated to you, O Ibn Abbas. It pleased the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that his companions hear that. Then slavery occupied Salman until he missed with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) Badr and Uhud. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Write a contract, O Salman. I contracted with my master for three hundred palm trees which I would plant for him, and forty ounces. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to his companions: Help your brother. They helped me with the palms: a man with thirty, a man with twenty, a man with fifteen, a man with ten, and a man according to what he had, until three hundred were gathered for me. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: Go, O Salman, and when you finish, let me know; I will be with you, placing them with my hand. I dug holes for them, and my companions helped me, until when I finished, I came to him and informed him. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out with me to them, and we brought the young palms near to him while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) placed them with his hand until we finished. By the One in Whose hand is the soul of Salman, not a single palm tree of them died. I delivered the palms, and the money remained upon me. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought something like a hen's egg of gold from one of the mines. He said: What has the Persian contract-slave done? I was called to him. He said: Take this and pay with it what is upon you, O Salman. I said: And where will this fall, O Messenger of Allah, against what is upon me? He said: Take it, for Allah will pay it off for you. I weighed out to him from it, by the One in Whose hand is the soul of Salman, forty ounces; I paid them their due. Salman was freed. I witnessed with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) al-Khandaq, then no battle with him escaped me."
"2507","Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: al-Fadl ibn Qurra informed us, he said: al-Hasan ibn Abi Ja'far informed us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Salman al-Farisi, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever gives a fasting person food and drink from lawful means to break his fast, the angels pray for him during the hours of the month of Ramadan, and Jibril, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, shakes his hand on the Night of Decree, and greets him; whoever Jibril shakes hands with on the Night of Decree is granted tears and softness of heart. Salman said: If he cannot afford his sustenance? He said: Even for a morsel of bread, or a draught of milk, or a drink of water, he shall have this."
"2508","Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Waki informed us, from al-A'mash, from Ibrahim, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, from Salman, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: One of the polytheists said to him mockingly: Your companion has taught you, until he has taught you even defecation. Salman said: Yes indeed; he commanded us not to face the qibla, nor to clean ourselves with our right hands, nor to suffice with less than three stones containing neither dung nor bone."
"2509","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Uthman ibn Umar informed us, he said: Ibn Abi Dhi'b informed us. And Amr ibn Ali informed us, he said: Abu Dawud informed us, he said: Ibn Abi Dhi'b informed us, he said: Sa'id ibn Abi Sa'id informed us, from his father, from Abdullah ibn Wadi'a, from Salman, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever bathes on Friday, washes thoroughly, purifies himself and perfumes himself from his family's perfume, goes out to Friday prayer, does not separate between two people, then prays what is decreed for him until the imam comes out, he is forgiven what is between it and the next Friday."
"2510","Yahya ibn Khalid narrated to us, he said: Abd al-A'la informed us, he said: Dawud ibn Abi al-Furat informed us, from Muhammad ibn Zayd, from Abu Shurayh al-Abdi, from Abu Muslim, from Salman, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wiping over the turban and the two leather socks, or he said: the head-cover and the two leather socks."
"2511","Abu Kurayb narrated to us, he said: Abu Mu'awiya informed us, from Dawud ibn Abi Hind, from Abu Uthman, from Salman. [The text ends here in the source without the wording of the hadith.]"
"2512","And Amr ibn Ali informed us, he said: Yahya informed us, from al-Taymi, from Abu Uthman, from Salman, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Allah created, on the day He created the heavens and the earth, a hundred mercies; one mercy He divided among the creatures, and He withheld with Him ninety-nine until the Day of Resurrection."
"2513","Bishr ibn Adam narrated to us, he said: Ash'ath ibn Ash'ath informed us, from Imran al-Qattan, from Sulayman al-Taymi, from Abu Uthman, from Salman, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When a Muslim performs ablution and perfects it, then prays the five prayers, his sins fall away as these leaves fall away. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited: (And establish prayer at the two ends of the day and at the approaches of the night; indeed good deeds remove evil deeds)."
"2514","Jamil ibn al-Hasan narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn al-Zibriqan informed us, from al-Taymi, from Abu Uthman, from Salman, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about locusts, and he said: The most numerous of Allah's troops; I neither eat them nor forbid them."
"2515","Jamil informed us, he said: Muhammad ibn al-Zibriqan informed us, he said: al-Taymi informed us, from Abu Uthman, from Salman, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said. [The text ends here in the source without the wording of the hadith.]"
"2516","And Amr ibn Ali informed us, he said: Yahya informed us, from Ja'far ibn Maymun, from Abu Uthman, from Salman, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah is Modest and Generous; He is shy to have the servant raise his hands and return them empty."
"2517","Amr ibn Ali and Yahya ibn Hakim narrated to us, both said: Makki ibn Ibrahim informed us, he said: Musa ibn Ubayda informed us, from Abu al-Azhar, from Salman, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out visiting a man of the Ansar. When he entered upon him, he placed his hand upon his forehead and said: How do you find yourself? He did not respond anything to him. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, he is preoccupied from you. He said: Leave me alone with him. The women went out from him, leaving the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) raised his hand, and the sick man signaled to return his hand to where it was. Then he called him: O so-and-so, what do you feel? He said: I feel well, and two have come to me, one black and the other white. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Which of them is nearer to you? He said: The black. He said: Good is little, and evil is much. He said: Then grant me enjoyment from yourself, O Messenger of Allah, with a supplication. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, forgive the much and increase the little. Then he said: What do you see? He said: Good, may my father and mother be sacrificed for you; I see good increasing and evil diminishing, and the black one has withdrawn from me. He said: Which of your deeds had most hold over you? He said: I used to give water to drink. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Listen, O Salman, do you deny anything of me? He said: Yes, may my father and mother be sacrificed for you; I have seen you in places, but never seen you in the like of your state today. He said: I know what he is meeting; there is no vein of him but that it is in the pain of death upon its edge. And Musa ibn Ubayda was a man occupied with worship, and Abu al-Azhar, we do not know anyone who narrated from him except Musa ibn Ubayda."
"2518","Amr ibn Ali and Yahya ibn Hakim narrated to us, both said: Shuja ibn al-Walid informed us, from Qabus ibn Abi Zibyan, from his father, from Salman, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Salman, do not hate me, lest you leave your religion. I said: O Messenger of Allah, should I hate you, when through you Allah guided us? He said: You hate the Arabs, and so hate me."
"2519","Ibrahim ibn Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Husayn ibn Muhammad informed us, he said: Sulayman ibn Qarm informed us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Wa'il, from Salman, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade us to burden ourselves for a guest with what we do not have."
"2520","And Zayd ibn Akhzam informed us, he said: Abu Qutayba informed us, he said: Qays informed us, from Uthman ibn Shabur, from Abu Wa'il, who said: I came to Salman, and he brought near to me bread and salt, and said: Were it not that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade burdening ourselves for a guest with what we do not have, I would have burdened myself for you."
"2521","Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Abd al-A'la informed us, he said: Burd informed us, from Sulayman ibn Musa, from Shurahbil ibn al-Simt, from Salman. [The text ends here in the source without the wording of the hadith.]"
"2522","And Ahmad ibn Abda informed us, he said: Abu Damra informed us, he said: Muhammad ibn Amr informed us, from Ubayda ibn Sufyan, from Abu al-Ja'd al-Damri, from Salman, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Guarding the frontier for a day in the path of Allah is better than fasting a month."
"2523","Salama ibn Shabib narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Munib informed us, he said: al-Sari ibn Yahya informed us, from Sulayman al-Taymi, from Abu Uthman, from Salman, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with the like of the hadith of Qatada, from Uqba ibn Abd al-Ghafir, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that a man never did any good at all, and said: When I die, burn me; then he mentioned the hadith."
"2524","And Zayd ibn Akhzam al-Ta'i informed us, he said: Abu Qutayba informed us, he said: Qays informed us, from Abu Hashim, from Zadham, from Salman, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: I read in the Torah: Part of the blessing of food is ablution before it. He said: I mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: Part of the blessing of food is ablution before it, and ablution after it."
"2525","Yusuf informed us, he said: Yahya ibn Durays informed us, from Qays, from Abu Hashim, from Zadham, from Salman, and he mentioned the like of it."
"2526","Hilal ibn Bishr narrated to us, he said: Abu Musa informed us, he said: Abu Hashim informed us, from Zadham, from Salman, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Ali: One who loves you loves me, and one who hates you hates me."
"2527","Ahmad ibn Abda narrated to us, he said: Husayn ibn al-Hasan informed us, he said: Ja'far ibn Ziyad al-Ahmar informed us, he said: Abu Khalid informed me, from Abu Hashim, from Zadham, from Salman, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: I had a nosebleed in the presence of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he commanded me to renew my ablution."
"2528","Humayd ibn al-Rabi narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Asim informed us, he said: Sulayman al-Taymi informed us, from Abu Uthman, from Salman, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, blessed and exalted, said to the son of Adam: O son of Adam, three things: one for Me, one for you, and one between Me and you. As for what is for Me: you worship Me and associate nothing with Me. As for what is for you: whatever deed you do, I recompense you for it; if I forgive, I am the Forgiving, the Merciful. As for what is between Me and you: from you is supplication and asking, and upon Me is answering and giving."
"2529","Abdullah ibn Ishaq al-Attar narrated to us, he said: Khalid ibn Hamza al-Attar informed us, he said: Uthman ibn Ghiyath informed us, he said: Abu Uthman informed us, from Salman, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man will come on the Day of Resurrection with good deeds by which he thinks he will be saved, but a man whom he wronged with some wrong will keep standing, and from his good deeds will be taken and given to the wronged one, until no good deed of his remains. Then one whom he wronged will come while nothing of his good deeds remains, so from the wronged one's evil deeds will be taken and placed upon his evil deeds."
"2530","Khalid ibn Yusuf ibn Khalid narrated to us, he said: Abu Awana informed us, from al-Mughira, from Abu Ma'shar, from Ibrahim, from Alqama, from Qartha al-Dabbi, from Salman, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me. [The text ends here in the source without the wording of the hadith.]"
"2531","And Yusuf ibn Musa informed us of it, he said: Jarir informed us, from Mansur, from Abu Ma'shar, from Ibrahim, from Alqama, from Qartha, from Salman, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: O Salman, do you know what Friday is? I said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: Do you know what Friday is? three times, I do not know whether he mentioned the fourth or not in the hadith of al-Mughira. He said: It is the day on which your father was gathered. I shall first narrate to you your story about Friday: There is no Muslim who performs ablution on Friday, then comes to Friday prayer, listens attentively until the imam finishes his prayer, but that it will be an expiation for him for what is between it and the next Friday, as long as killing is avoided."
"2532","Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Jarir informed us. And Abu Kurayb informed us, he said: Abu Mu'awiya informed us, and the wording is that of Jarir, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Jamil ibn Abi Maymuna, from al-Khuza'i, who said: al-Farisi, meaning Salman, may Allah be pleased with him, narrated to me that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Guarding the frontier for a day and night in the path of Allah is like fasting a month and standing it in prayer. Whoever, meaning dies while guarding, the reward of the guard will flow for him until he is resurrected on the Day of Resurrection, he will be safe from the tester, and his provision from Paradise will be allotted to him."
"2533","Al-Abbas ibn Abi Talib narrated to us, he said: Minjab ibn al-Harith informed us, he said: Hafs ibn Ghiyath informed us, from Asim, from Abu Uthman, from Salman, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Three shall not enter Paradise: the old adulterer, the lying ruler, and the poor arrogant one."
"2534","Ubaydullah ibn Yusuf narrated to us, he said: al-Hajjaj ibn Farrukh informed us, he said: Ibn Jurayj informed us, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, from Salman, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you marries a woman, on the night of consummation let him pray two rak'as and command her to pray two rak'as behind him; for Allah will place good in the house."
"2535","Ahmad ibn ... narrated to us, he said: Zayd ibn al-Hubab informed us, he said: Humayd, the freed slave of Abu Alqama, informed us, from Ata, from Abu Hurayra, from Salman, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever says: O Allah, I call You to witness, and I call Your angels and the bearers of Your Throne to witness, and I call those in the heavens to witness that You are Allah, there is no god but You alone, without partner, and I bear witness that Muhammad is Your servant and Messenger; whoever says it once, a third of him is freed from the Fire; whoever says it twice, two-thirds of him is freed from the Fire; and whoever says it thrice, all of him is freed from the Fire."
"2536","Ibrahim ibn Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Abu Usama informed us, from Mis'ar, from Umar ibn Qays al-Masir, from Amr ibn Abi Qurra, from Salman, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I am only a human; I become angry as you become angry. Whichever servant I insult with an insult, or curse with a curse, or supplicate against without its being deserved, make it for him a prayer and mercy."
"2537","Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: al-Husayn ibn Ali informed us, from Za'ida, from Umar ibn Qays, from Amr ibn Abi Qurra, from Salman, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with similar wording."
"2538","Yusuf narrated to us, from Ubaydullah, who said: Isra'il informed us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Qurra al-Kindi, from Salman, who said: I was among the sons of the Persian horsemen."
"2539","Ibrahim ibn Abdullah narrated to us, he said: Bishr ibn Ubayd informed us, he said: Maslama ibn al-Salt informed us, he said: Umar ibn Yazid al-Azdi narrated to me, from Abu Rashid al-Absi, who said: I asked Salman al-Farisi about the tashahhud, and he said: I shall teach you as the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) taught it to me. He took my hand and taught me the tashahhud letter by letter: Greetings belong to Allah, and prayers and pure words; peace be upon you, O Prophet, and the mercy of Allah and His blessings; peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah; I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger. Then he said: O Salman, say it in your prayer, and do not add a letter to it nor omit a letter from it."
"2540","Ibrahim ibn Abdullah narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Muhammad informed us, he said: Ali ibn Ghurab informed us, from Sa'id ibn al-Hurr, from Salama ibn Kulthum, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Salman, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever takes servants other than those he marries, then they commit adultery, upon him is the like of their sins, without diminishing anything of their sins."
"2541","Bishr ibn Adam narrated to us, he said: Nusayr ibn Abi al-Ash'ath informed us, he said: al-Salt al-Dahhan narrated to me, from Jathima ibn Ri'ab, who said: I asked Salman about the statement of Allah, blessed and exalted: (That is because among them are priests and monks). He said: Leave the priests in the churches and ruins; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) taught me to recite: (That is because among them are truthful ones and monks)."
"2542","Muhammad ibn Ashras narrated to us, he said: Abu Jabir Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik informed us, he said: al-Hasan ibn Abi Ja'far informed us, from Thabit, from Abu Uthman, from Salman, may Allah be pleased with him, that a man entered the mosque while the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had already prayed, so he said: Will not a man give charity to this one and pray with him."
"2543","Muhammad ibn al-Mu'ammal narrated to us, he said: Bakr ibn Yahya informed us, he said: Mindal informed us, from Asim, from Abu Uthman, from Salman, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whom do you count as a martyr among you? They said: Being killed in the path of Allah. He said: Then the martyrs of my ummah would be few: being killed is martyrdom, drowning is martyrdom, burning is martyrdom, and I think he said: and the woman whom her child in her womb kills is martyrdom."
"2544","Ahmad ibn al-Nu'man ibn Ziyad al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Ya'qub al-Talaqani informed us, he said: Yahya ibn Durays narrated to me, from Abu Mawdud, from Sulayman al-Taymi, from Abu Uthman, from Salman, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Nothing repels the decree except supplication, and nothing increases lifespan except righteousness."
"2545","Al-Qasim ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Fudayl informed us, from Asim al-Ahwal, from Abu Uthman, from Salman, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Do not be, if you can, the first to enter the market nor the last to leave it; for it is the battlefield of Satan, and there he plants his banner."
"2546","Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Mihran ibn Abi Umar informed us, he said: Sufyan informed us, from Asim al-Ahwal, from Ibn Sirin, from Salman al-Farisi, thus he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not single out Friday for fasting, nor its night for standing in prayer."
"2547","Muhammad ibn Harb narrated to us, he said: Ishaq ibn Yusuf informed us, from al-Jurayri, from Abu Uthman, from Salman al-Farisi, raising the hadith: Allah said: When My servant draws near to Me a handspan, I draw near to him a cubit; when he draws near to Me a cubit, I draw near to him a fathom; and when he comes to Me walking, I come to him hastening."
"2548","Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Mihran ibn Abi Umar informed us, he said: Ali ibn Abd al-A'la informed us, from Abu al-Nu'man, who said: Abu al-Waqqas narrated to me, who said: Salman al-Farisi narrated to me, who said: Abu Bakr and Umar, may Allah be pleased with them, entered upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: Among the traits of the hypocrite: when he speaks he lies, when he promises he breaks it, and when he is entrusted he betrays. They left the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heavy-hearted. Ali met them and said to them: Why do I see you heavy-hearted? They said: A hadith we heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Among the traits of the hypocrite: when he speaks he lies, when he is entrusted he betrays, and when he promises he breaks it. Ali said: Did you not ask him? They said: We were awed by the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: But I shall ask him. He entered upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Abu Bakr and Umar met me, heavy-hearted; then he mentioned what they said. He said: I did narrate to them, but I did not place it in the place they place it; rather the hypocrite is one who, when he speaks, tells himself he is lying; when he promises, tells himself he will break it; and when he is entrusted, tells himself he will betray."
"2549","Abdullah ibn Abi Thumama narrated to us, he said: Affan informed us, he said: Hammad informed us, from Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, from Abu al-Bakhtari, that Salman besieged a fortress of the fortresses of Qudayd, and said to his companions: Let me do what I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) doing. He praised Allah and extolled Him, then said: I am a man of you, and Allah has granted me Islam; you have seen the obedience of the Arabs to me. If you believe and emigrate, you shall be in our rank; if you submit and remain in your lands, you shall be in the rank of the Bedouins: for you shall be what is for them, and upon you shall be what is upon them. If you refuse and acknowledge the jizya, you shall have what the people of jizya have. He offered that to them for three days, then said to his companions: Rise against them. So they opened it."
"2550","Abdullah ibn Mu'awiya narrated to us, he said: Salih al-Murri informed us, from al-Jurayri, from Abu Uthman, who said: Salman wrote to Abu al-Darda: O my brother, hold to the mosque and stay in it; for I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: The mosque is the house of every God-fearing one. The end of the Musnad of Salman."
"2551","In the name of Allah, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful; may Allah bless our master Muhammad and his family and companions and grant them peace. What Umar ibn al-Khattab narrated from Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with them both. Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Mufarrij informed us, he said: Abu al-Hasan Muhammad ibn Ayyub ibn Habib ibn Yahya al-Raqqi al-Samut narrated to us, he said: Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Amr ibn Abd al-Khaliq al-Basri al-Azdi al-Bazzar narrated to me, he said: Salama ibn Shabib narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq informed us, he said: Ma'mar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from Ibn Umar, from Umar. [The text ends here in the source without the wording of the hadith.]"
"2552","And Umar ibn al-Khattab narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Yaman al-Hakam ibn Nafi narrated to us, he said: Shu'ayb ibn Abi Hamza narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, who said: Salim ibn Abdullah ibn Umar narrated to me that he heard his father Abdullah ibn Umar, that Umar ibn al-Khattab said: When Hafsa became widowed from Khunays ibn Hudhafa al-Sahmi, of the companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who had witnessed Badr and died in Medina, Umar said: I met Uthman ibn Affan and offered him Hafsa, saying: If you wish, I shall marry Hafsa bint Umar to you. He said: I shall consider my affair. I waited some nights, then he met me and said: I do not wish to marry these days of mine. Then I met Abu Bakr and said to him: If you wish, I shall marry Hafsa bint Umar to you. Abu Bakr remained silent and did not return anything to me. I was angrier with him than with Uthman. I waited some nights, then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) proposed her to me, and I married her to him. Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, met me and said: Perhaps you were angry with me when you offered me Hafsa and I returned nothing to you? I said: Yes. He said: Nothing prevented me from returning to you concerning what you offered me except that I knew the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had mentioned Hafsa, and I would not disclose the secret of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); had he left her, I would have accepted her, or married her. This hadith belongs in the Musnad of Abu Bakr and Umar; most of the chain is from Umar, and what belongs in it from Abu Bakr is what he said: I knew the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had mentioned Hafsa, and I disliked disclosing the secret of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); it is as if a narration from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and information from him to Umar about the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"2553","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Bishr ibn Umar narrated to us, he said: Malik narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Malik ibn Aws ibn al-Hadathan, from Umar ibn al-Khattab, from Abu Bakr, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: We are not inherited; what we leave is charity. And this hadith, thus Malik narrated it, from al-Zuhri, from Malik ibn Aws, from Umar, from Abu Bakr, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); and others followed him upon the like of this narration, from Umar, from... [the text breaks off here in the source]."
"2554","The Musnad of Usama ibn Zayd, may Allah be pleased with them both. The Musnad of Usama ibn Zayd. And of what Ibn Abbas narrated from Usama ibn Zayd. Ahmad ibn Abda narrated to us, he said: Sufyan ibn Uyayna informed us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Abu Salih, from Ibn Abbas, from Usama ibn Zayd, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). [The text ends here in the source without the wording of the hadith.]"
"2555","And Amr ibn Ali informed us of it, he said: Abu Asim informed us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Abu Salih, from Ibn Abbas, from Usama, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: There is no riba except in delay (nasi'a)."
"2556","Al-Fadl ibn Sahl narrated it to us, he said: al-Aswad ibn Amir informed us, he said: Sharik informed us, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Rafi, from Abu Salih, from Ibn Abbas, from Usama ibn Zayd, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). [The text ends here in the source without the wording of the hadith, which is: There is no riba except in delay.]"
"2557","And Muhammad ibn Isma'il al-Bukhari informed us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Sharik informed us, from his father, from al-A'mash, from Abu Salih, from Ibn Abbas, from Usama ibn Zayd, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). [The text ends here in the source without the wording of the hadith.]"
"2558","And Ali ibn Dawud al-Qantari informed us of it, he said: Amr ibn Khalid informed us, from Ubaydullah ibn Amr, from Zayd ibn Abi Unaysa, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Abu Salih, from Ibn Abbas, from Usama ibn Zayd, may Allah be pleased with them, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: There is no riba except in delay (nasi'a)."
"2559","And Mu'ammal ibn Hisham informed us of it, he said: Isma'il ibn Ibrahim informed us, from Khalid al-Hadhdha, from Ikrima, from Ibn Abbas, from Usama ibn Zayd, may Allah be pleased with them, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: There is no riba except in delay (nasi'a)."
"2560","And Abdullah ibn Ishaq al-Attar informed us, he said: Abu Asim informed us, he said: Isma'il ibn Abd al-Malik informed us, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, and once he said: from Abd al-Aziz ibn Rafi, from Ibn Abbas, from Usama ibn Zayd. [The text ends here in the source without the wording of the hadith.]"
"2561","And Yusuf ibn Musa informed us, he said: Mihran ibn Abi Umar informed us, he said: Uthman ibn al-Aswad informed us, from Ibn Abi Mulayka, from Ibn Abbas, from Usama ibn Zayd, may Allah be pleased with them, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: There is no riba except in delay (nasi'a)."
"2562","Ali ibn Muslim narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Samad ibn Abd al-Warith informed us, he said: my father narrated to me, from Amir al-Ahwal, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, from Usama, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). [The text ends here in the source without the wording of the hadith.]"
"2563","And Abu al-Khattab Ziyad ibn Yahya informed us of it, he said: Abu Attab Sahl ibn Hammad informed us, he said: Sa'id ibn Abi Aruba informed us, from Kathir ibn Shinzhir, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, from Usama ibn Zayd, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). [The text ends here in the source without the wording of the hadith.]"
"2564","And al-Hasan ibn Yahya al-Aruzzi informed us of it, he said: Harun ibn Isma'il al-Khazzaz informed us, he said: Ali ibn al-Mubarak informed us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, from Usama ibn Zayd, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). [The text ends here in the source without the wording of the hadith.]"
"2565","And Abd al-Warith ibn Abd al-Samad informed us of it, he said: my father narrated to me, from Dawud ibn Abi al-Furat, from Ibrahim al-Sa'igh, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, from Usama ibn Zayd, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). [The text ends here in the source without the wording of the hadith.]"
"2566","And Amr ibn Ali informed us of it, he said: Abu Asim informed us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, from Usama ibn Zayd, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). [The text ends here in the source without the wording of the hadith.]"
"2567","Abu Bakr said: And I found in my book from Khalid ibn Khidash, who said: Muhammad ibn Thabit al-Asri informed us, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Qurayr, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, from Usama, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: There is no riba except in delay (nasi'a)."
"2568","And Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim informed us, he said: Sahl ibn Hammad informed us, he said: Wuhayb informed us, from Ibn Tawus, from his father, from Ibn Abbas, from Usama, may Allah be pleased with them, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: There is no riba except in delay (nasi'a). And this hadith was narrated by Ibn Abbas from Usama, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). And Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib narrated it from Usama, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). It has been reported from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: Gold for gold, like for like, and silver for silver, like for like. The report is established in that from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). It was reported from him, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said: Gold for silver is riba except hand to hand. As for the hadith of Usama reported in that, we do not know anyone who affirmed it except its transmitter. Abu Sa'id al-Khudri objected to it against Ibn Abbas, and narrated to him in that what made Ibn Abbas hold back at that time, by the narration of Abu Sa'id from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). We do not know anyone afterwards among the jurists of the cities in all regions who ruled by the hadith of Usama; the meaning of the hadith of Usama, if it were established, would be that a dirham for two dirhams hand to hand is unobjectionable. As for this statement, we have sufficed from arguing about it, since no mufti is known to openly give fatwa by it."
"2569","Ibn Umar from Usama. Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Abu Mu'awiya informed us, he said: al-A'mash informed us, from Umara, meaning Ibn Umayr, from Abu al-Sha'tha, from Ibn Umar, who said: Usama, may Allah be pleased with them, informed me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed inside the House (Ka'ba). He said: I said: How many did he pray? He said: He did not inform me how many he prayed."
"2570","Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, he said: Mu'ammal ibn Isma'il informed us, he said: Isra'il informed us, he said: Ash'ath ibn Abi al-Sha'tha informed us, from his father, from Abdullah ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out to us walking between Usama ibn Zayd and Bilal until he entered the Ka'ba, in which there was a crossbeam. When Usama ibn Zayd came out, I asked him: How did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) do? He said: He left two-thirds of the beam to his right and prayed in the remaining third to his left. I said: How many did he pray? He said: I did not ask Bilal."
"2571","Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib from Usama ibn Zayd. Muhammad ibn Mansur al-Tusi narrated to us, he said: Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim ibn Sa'd informed us, he said: my father informed us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, who said: Ibn Abi Rafi narrated to me, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Usama, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: There is no riba except in delay (nasi'a). And this hadith we have mentioned in the hadith of Ibn Abbas, and what the meaning of the narration reported in that is, so we sufficed from repeating its mention afterwards. We do not know for Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib any path from Usama except this path."
"2572","And of what Urwa ibn al-Zubayr narrated from Usama ibn Zayd. Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Sufyan ibn Uyayna informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Urwa, from Usama ibn Zayd, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) looked out over a fortress of the fortresses of Medina and said: Do you see what I see? Verily I see tribulations amid your houses like the falling places of rain. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated with this wording except from Usama ibn Zayd with this isnad."
"2573","Amr ibn Ali and Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, both said: Mu'adh ibn Mu'adh informed us, he said: Salih ibn Abi al-Akhdar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Urwa, from Usama ibn Zayd, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded him to raid Ubna in the morning, then to burn. And this hadith was narrated by others than Salih, from al-Zuhri, from Urwa, mursal (unconnected); Salih narrated it connected. We do not know it narrated with this wording except from Usama."
"2574","And Salama ibn Shabib and al-Husayn ibn Mahdi informed us, and the wording is that of Salama, both said: Abd al-Razzaq informed us, he said: Ma'mar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Urwa: that Usama ibn Zayd, may Allah be pleased with him, informed him that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) rode a donkey upon which was a saddle, with a Fadak-made velvet cloth beneath it, and mounted me behind him, while he was visiting Sa'd ibn Ubada among Banu al-Harith ibn al-Khazraj, before the battle of Badr, until he passed a gathering containing a mix of Muslims, idol-worshipping polytheists and Jews, among them Abdullah ibn Ubayy ibn Salul, and in the gathering was Abdullah ibn Rawaha. When the dust of the mount covered the gathering, Abdullah ibn Ubayy covered his nose with his cloak, then said: Do not raise dust over us. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) greeted, then stopped, dismounted, called them to Allah and recited the Qur'an to them. Abdullah ibn Ubayy said to him: O man, there is nothing better than this, if what you say is true; so do not trouble us in our gatherings, return to your saddle, and whoever comes to you from us, narrate to him. Abdullah ibn Rawaha said: Rather visit us in our gatherings, for we love that. The Muslims, polytheists and Jews reviled one another until they were about to leap upon one another. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) kept calming them. Then he rode his mount until he entered upon Sa'd ibn Ubada, and said: O Sa'd, did you not hear what Abu Hubab said? meaning Abdullah ibn Ubayy. He said such-and-such. He said: Pardon him, O Messenger of Allah, and overlook; by Allah, Allah has given you what He has given you, and the people of this lake had agreed to crown him and bind the turban upon him. When Allah repelled that with the truth He gave you, he choked with it; that is why he did what you saw. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pardoned him. And this hadith was narrated from al-Zuhri, from Urwa, by Muhammad ibn Ishaq, Shu'ayb ibn Abi Hamza and Abdullah ibn Abi Atiq; all of them narrated it from al-Zuhri, from Urwa, from Usama."
"2575","As for the hadith of Ibn Ishaq: Ibrahim ibn Ziyad al-Sa'igh narrated it to us, he said: Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim ibn Sa'd informed us, from his father, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from al-Zuhri, from Urwa, from Usama, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). [The text ends here, referring to the preceding hadith about the Prophet's passing the mixed gathering and pardoning Ibn Ubayy.]"
"2576","As for the hadith of Shu'ayb: Ibrahim ibn Hani and Umar ibn al-Khattab narrated it to us, both said: Abu al-Yaman informed us, from Shu'ayb, from al-Zuhri, from Urwa, from Usama, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). [Referring to the same preceding hadith.]"
"2577","And I heard one of our companions, he is Isma'il ibn Ishaq, mentioning it from Isma'il ibn Abi Uways, from his brother, from Sulayman ibn Bilal, from Ibn Abi Atiq, and he is Muhammad ibn Abi Atiq, from al-Zuhri, from Urwa, from Usama, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). We do not know these words narrated connected from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except from the hadith of al-Zuhri, from Urwa, from Usama."
"2578","And Abu Kurayb informed us, he said: Yunus ibn Bukayr informed us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from al-Zuhri, from Urwa, from Usama ibn Zayd, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Abdullah ibn Ubayy in the illness in which he died: I used to forbid you from loving the Jews. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from al-Zuhri, from Urwa, from Usama except Yunus ibn Bukayr, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq; others narrated it mursal."
"2579","Umar ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan narrated to us, he said: my father narrated to me, he said: Uthman ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to me, from al-Zuhri, from Urwa, from Usama ibn Zayd, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: Abdullah ibn Ubayy said: If we return to Medina, the mightier will surely expel the humbler from it. Abdullah ibn Abdullah said: By Allah, you shall not enter until you say: Muhammad is the mighty, and you are the humbled, or: you are the humiliated. Abdullah ibn Abdullah sought permission to kill his father, and he said: The people shall not say that Muhammad kills his companions. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from the hadith of al-Zuhri, from Urwa, except from the hadith of Uthman ibn Abd al-Rahman, and he is weak in hadith; this is his wording or its meaning."
"2580","And Ahmad ibn Aban al-Qurashi informed us, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad informed us, from Hisham ibn Urwa. And Yusuf ibn Musa informed us, he said: Jarir informed us, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from his father, who said: Usama ibn Zayd was asked about the Prophet's travel from Arafat to Muzdalifa, and he said: He would travel at a gentle pace (al-anaq); when he found an open space, he would hasten (nass). And this hadith, we do not know it narrated with this wording except from Usama with this isnad; others narrated it from Hisham ibn Urwa, from Usama."
"2581","Zayd ibn Akhzam narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Qahir ibn Shu'ayb informed us, he said: Salih ibn Abi al-Akhdar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Urwa, from Usama, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If you hear of the plague in a land, do not enter it; and if it occurs in a land while you are in it, do not leave it. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who followed Salih ibn Abi al-Akhdar in this narration of his; for al-Zuhri narrates it from a group, and Salih contradicted all who narrated it from al-Zuhri: al-Zuhri narrated it from Amir ibn Sa'd, from Usama, except Abd al-Wahid, from Ma'mar, who said: from al-Zuhri, from Amir ibn Sa'd, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); and Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq said: from al-Zuhri, from Amir ibn Sa'd, from Zayd ibn Thabit."
"2582","And Ubaydullah ibn Sa'd ibn Ibrahim informed us, he said: Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim ibn Sa'd informed us, he said: my father narrated to me, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from his father, from Usama ibn Zayd, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) combined the two prayers at Muzdalifa with one iqama, meaning that he called the adhan and iqama for Maghrib, and iqama for Isha, and did not pray voluntary prayers between them. And this hadith with this wording, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Hisham ibn Urwa, from his father, from Usama except Muhammad ibn Ishaq."
"2583","And of what Muhammad ibn Usama ibn Zayd narrated from his father Usama. Abu Kurayb narrated to us, he said: Yunus ibn Bukayr informed us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Sa'id ibn Ubayd ibn al-Sabbaq, from Muhammad ibn Usama ibn Zayd, from his father, who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) became gravely ill, I descended, and the people descended with me. I entered upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he had lost speech and did not speak. He began raising his hand to the sky, then placing it upon me, so I knew he was supplicating for me. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Muhammad ibn Usama, from his father, except Sa'id ibn Ubayd ibn al-Sabbaq; Abu Salama ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated from Usama something similar to this description."
"2584","And Khalid ibn Yusuf ibn Khalid informed us, he said: my father narrated to me, he said: Musa ibn Uqba informed us, from Ibn Usama ibn Zayd, from his father, meaning Muhammad ibn Usama. [The text ends here in the source without the wording of the hadith.]"
"2585","And Ubayd ibn Bukhayt informed us of it, he said: Abdullah ibn Ja'far al-Raqqi informed us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Amr informed us, from Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, from Ibn Usama ibn Zayd, from his father: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) clothed him with a Qibti garment, and he clothed his wife with it. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What did you do with the Qibti garment? He said: I clothed my wife with it. He said: Command her to wear an inner garment beneath it, so it does not describe the size of her bones. And this hadith with this wording, we do not know anyone who narrated it except Usama ibn Zayd with this isnad."
"2586","And of what al-Hasan ibn Usama ibn Zayd narrated from his father Usama. Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Khalid ibn Utma informed us, he said: Musa ibn Ya'qub narrated to me, from Ibn Zayd ibn al-Muhajir, from Muslim ibn Abi Sahl al-Nabbal, who said: al-Hasan ibn Usama ibn Zayd narrated to me, from his father, who said: I knocked on the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) one night for some need. He came out to me wrapped in something, I know not what it was. When I finished my need, I said: What is this you are wrapped in? And there were Hasan and Husayn upon his hips. He said: O Allah, You know that I love them both, so love them both, three times. We do not know al-Hasan ibn Usama narrated from his father except this hadith."
"2587","And of what Amr ibn Uthman ibn Affan narrated from Usama. Ahmad ibn Abda narrated to us, he said: Sufyan informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Ali ibn Husayn, from Amr ibn Uthman, from Usama ibn Zayd, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Muslim does not inherit the disbeliever, nor the disbeliever the Muslim. Abu Bakr said: And this hadith was narrated by Ibn Uyayna, Ma'mar and a group, from al-Zuhri, from Ali ibn Husayn, from Amr ibn Uthman, from Usama; they agreed upon the name Amr ibn Uthman, except Malik ibn Anas, who narrated it from al-Zuhri, from Ali ibn Husayn, from Umar ibn Uthman, from Usama; they consider he erred in that, although he once stopped and said: This is the house of Amr, and this is the house of Umar, pointing to them both. As for the narration, we do not know anyone who followed him in his narration except perhaps Abu Uways, for his hearing from al-Zuhri resembles the hearing of Malik."
"2588","And Isma'il ibn Hafs informed us, he said: al-Walid ibn Muslim informed us, he said: al-Awza'i informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Ali ibn Husayn, from Amr ibn Uthman, from Usama ibn Zayd, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: We shall descend tomorrow, if Allah the Exalted wills, at the valley of Banu Kinana, where they swore upon disbelief. It was said: Shall we not pitch a tent for you at Mina? He said: And has Aqil left us any dwelling? And this hadith which al-Awza'i narrated was also narrated by others than al-Awza'i, from al-Zuhri, from Ali ibn Husayn, from Amr ibn Uthman, from Usama, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). We do not know Amr ibn Uthman narrated from Usama except these two hadiths."
"2589","Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Ibn Uyayna informed us, from al-Zuhri. Amr said: And Yazid ibn Zuray and Muhammad ibn Ja'far informed us of it, from Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri. Amr said: And Abu Asim informed us of it, from Ibn Jurayj, who said: al-Zuhri narrated to me, who said: Ali ibn Husayn informed us, from Amr ibn Uthman, from Usama ibn Zayd, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The Muslim does not inherit the disbeliever, nor the disbeliever the Muslim."
"2590","And of what Amir ibn Sa'd narrated from Usama ibn Zayd. Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Abu Usama informed us, he said: Muhammad ibn Amr informed us, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Amir ibn Sa'd, from Usama ibn Zayd, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If you hear of the plague in a land, do not enter upon it; and if it occurs in a land while you are in it, do not leave it."
"2591","Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Shabib informed us, he said: my father narrated to me, from Yunus al-Ayli, from Ibn Shihab, who said: Amir ibn Sa'd narrated to me, from Usama ibn Zayd, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: This pain is a punishment with which some nations were punished; it goes away one time and comes another. Whoever hears of it in a land, let him not come to it; and whoever is in a land where it occurs, let him not leave fleeing from it."
"2592","Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Yazid informed us, he said: Haywa ibn Shurayh informed us, he said: Ayyash ibn Abbas informed us that Abu al-Nadr, meaning Salim, narrated to him, from Amir ibn Sa'd: that Usama ibn Zayd informed his father Sa'd, who said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I practice withdrawal from my wife. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Why is that? or: For what is that? He said: I pity her child, or her children. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If it were so, it harmed neither Persia nor Rome, or: the Romans. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from Usama except through this chain."
"2593","And of what Kurayb, the freed slave of Ibn Abbas, narrated from Usama. Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Abu Asim informed us, he said: Ibn Abi Dhi'b informed us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Mihran, from Kurayb, from Usama ibn Zayd, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The angels do not enter a house in which there is a dog, nor an image. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from Usama except with this isnad."
"2594","And Bishr ibn Adam informed us, he said: Uthman ibn Umar informed us, he said: Ibn Abi Dhi'b informed us, from al-Harith ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Kurayb, from Usama ibn Zayd, who said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and saw grief upon him. It was said to him, and he said: Jibril, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, has not come to me for three days, and I see a puppy in the house. He commanded it and it was removed. Then Jibril, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, appeared to him. He said: Why did you not come to me? He said: We do not enter a house in which there is a dog, nor images. We do not know al-Harith ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated from Kurayb, from Usama except this hadith."
"2595","And Ahmad ibn al-Faraj al-Himsi informed us, he said: Uthman ibn Sa'id ibn Kathir ibn Dinar al-Himsi informed us, he said: Muhammad ibn al-Muhajir informed us, from al-Dahhak al-Ma'afiri, from Sulayman ibn Musa, who said: Kurayb narrated to me that he heard Usama ibn Zayd, may Allah be pleased with him, saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Will there be no one striving for Paradise? For Paradise has no equal: it is, by the Lord of the Ka'ba, a shining light, a swaying sweet basil, a lofty palace, a fragrant river, ripe fruit, a beautiful fair wife, many garments, in an eternal station, in a sound abode, with fruit, greenery, vessels and blessing, in a lofty splendid dwelling. They said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah, we are the strivers for it. He said: Say: If Allah wills. The people said: If Allah wills. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except Usama; we do not know for it any path from Usama except this path; we do not know anyone who narrated it from al-Dahhak al-Ma'afiri except this man Muhammad ibn Muhajir."
"2596","Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi informed us, he said: Sufyan al-Thawri informed us, from Ibrahim ibn Uqba, from Kurayb, from Usama ibn Zayd, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: I poured forth with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); when he reached the mountain pass, he dismounted and urinated. I said: The prayer. He said: The prayer is ahead of you. When we reached Muzdalifa, he called the adhan and iqama and prayed Maghrib; then nothing else came until he called iqama and prayed Isha."
"2597","Of what Abu Uthman al-Nahdi narrated from Usama ibn Zayd. Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik al-Qurashi narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Zayd informed us, from Asim ibn Sulayman al-Ahwal, from Abu Uthman, from Usama ibn Zayd, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: I was with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when the messenger of one of his daughters came calling him, saying: A boy of hers is dying. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Return to her and say to her: Let her seek reward, for to Allah belongs what He takes and to Him belongs what He gives, and everything with Him is to an appointed term. She sent to him swearing upon him that he come to her. He rose, and with him rose Mu'adh ibn Jabal and Sa'd ibn Ubada. He came to her, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) placed the boy in his lap while his soul rattled as if in a waterskin. The eyes of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) shed tears. Sa'd ibn Ubada said: What is this, O Messenger of Allah? He said: A mercy which Allah placed in the hearts of His servants; Allah shows mercy only to the merciful of His servants. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from the hadith of Usama except through this chain with this isnad, though others narrated it from Asim, from Abu Uthman."
"2598","And Amr ibn Ali informed us of it, he said: Abd al-A'la ibn Abd al-A'la informed us, he said: Hisham ibn Hassan informed us, from Asim al-Ahwal, from Abu Uthman al-Nahdi, from Usama ibn Zayd, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with similar wording."
"2599","And Humayd ibn Mas'ada informed us, he said: al-Mu'tamir ibn Sulayman informed us, he said: my father narrated to me, from Abu Tamima, from Abu Uthman, from Usama ibn Zayd, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would take me and al-Hasan ibn Ali, saying: O Allah, I love them both, so love them both. And this hadith is only narrated from Usama ibn Zayd: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said it for al-Hasan and al-Husayn; and in the hadith of Abu Uthman from Usama he said it for him and for al-Hasan."
"2600","Amr ibn Ali and Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, both said: Yahya ibn Sa'id informed us, from Sulayman al-Taymi, from Abu Uthman, from Usama ibn Zayd, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). [The text ends here in the source without the wording of the hadith.]"
"2601","And Abbad ibn Ziyad al-Saji informed us, he said: Uthman ibn Umar informed us, he said: Shu'ba informed us, from al-Taymi, from Abu Uthman, from Usama ibn Zayd, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: I have not left after me a trial more harmful to men than women."
"2602","And al-Qasim ibn Wahb al-Kufi informed us, he said: Ali ibn Abd al-Hamid informed us, he said: Mindal informed us, from Asim al-Ahwal, from Abu Uthman, from Usama, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: I have not left after me a trial more harmful to men than women. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Asim, from Abu Uthman, from Usama except Mindal; it is only known from the hadith of al-Taymi, from Abu Uthman, from Usama."
"2603","And Yusuf ibn Musa informed us, he said: Amr ibn Humran informed us, he said: Hisham ibn Hassan informed us. And Azhar ibn Jamil informed us, he said: Abd al-Wahhab informed us, from Hisham ibn Hassan, from Asim al-Ahwal, from Abu Uthman, from three of the companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Usama ibn Zayd, Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas and another man of the companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever claims to belong to other than his father, Allah forbids Paradise to him. And this hadith was narrated by a group from Asim, from Abu Uthman, from Sa'd and Abu Bakra. And Hisham ibn Hassan said: from Asim, from Abu Uthman, from Usama ibn Zayd, Sa'd and another man; we consider him Abu Bakra. We do not know anyone who combined three in this hadith from Asim and named Usama except Hisham, from Asim."
"2604","And Ibrahim ibn Sa'id al-Jawhari and Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Mani informed us, both said: al-Ahwas ibn Jawwab informed us, he said: Su'ayr ibn al-Khums informed us, from Sulayman al-Taymi, from Abu Uthman, from Usama ibn Zayd, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is done a favor and says to its doer: May Allah reward you with good, has excelled in praise. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Sulayman al-Taymi except Su'ayr, nor from Su'ayr except al-Ahwas ibn Jawwab."
"2605","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn Habib informed us, he said: al-Mu'tamir ibn Sulayman informed us, he said: my father informed us, from Abu Uthman, who said: I was informed that Jibril, peace be upon him, came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while Umm Salama was with him, conversing, then stood up. The Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Umm Salama: Who is this? or as he said. She said: This is Dihya. Umm Salama said: By Allah, I thought him none but he, until I heard the sermon of the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) informing, I think he said: about Jibril, or as he said. I said to Abu Uthman: From whom did you hear this? He said: From Usama ibn Zayd. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from al-Taymi, from Abu Uthman, from Usama except al-Mu'tamir."
"2606","Salm ibn Junada ibn Salm narrated to us, he said: Abu Usama informed us, he said: al-Jurayri informed us, from Abu Uthman, from Usama ibn Zayd, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). [The text ends here in the source without the wording of the hadith.]"
"2607","And al-Jarrah ibn Makhlad informed us of it, he said: Salim ibn Nuh informed us, from al-Jurayri, from Abu Uthman, from Usama ibn Zayd, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that: when travel hastened him, he combined Zuhr with Asr, and Maghrib with Isha. And this hadith was narrated by others from al-Jurayri, from Abu Uthman, from Usama, stopped (mawquf); Abu Usama and Salim ibn Nuh narrated it raised; al-Taymi narrated it from Abu Uthman, from Usama ibn Zayd, stopped."
"2608","And of what Ibrahim ibn Sa'd narrated from Usama. Amr ibn Ali informed us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi informed us, he said: Shu'ba informed us, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, who said: I heard Ibrahim ibn Sa'd narrating from Usama ibn Zayd, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If you hear of the plague in a land, do not enter it; and if it occurs in a land while you are in it, do not leave it."
"2609","Yusuf ibn Musa informed us, he said: Jarir informed us, from al-A'mash, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Ibrahim ibn Sa'd, from Usama ibn Zayd, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with similar wording."
"2610","Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Mu'ammal, meaning Ibn Isma'il, informed us, he said: Sufyan al-Thawri informed us, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Ibrahim ibn Sa'd, from Usama ibn Zayd and Khuzayma ibn Thabit: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: This pain is a punishment with which those before you were punished; when it occurs in a land while you are in it, do not leave it; and when it occurs in a land while you are not in it, do not come to it. We do not know Ibrahim ibn Sa'd narrated from Usama except this hadith, nor did anyone narrate it from him except Habib ibn Abi Thabit."
"2611","Of what Kulthum al-Khuza'i narrated from Usamah ibn Zayd: 2608 — Yusuf ibn Musa and Muhammad ibn al-Layth narrated to us, they said: Ubaydullah ibn Musa informed us, he said: Shayban al-Nahwi, i.e. Ibn Abd al-Rahman, informed us, from al-A'mash, from Jami' ibn Shaddad, from Kulthum al-Khuza'i, from Usamah ibn Zayd, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: We entered upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was ill and found him sleeping with his face covered by an Adani cloak; he uncovered the cloak from his face and then said: May Allah curse the Jews; they declare forbidden the fat of sheep yet eat its price. And this hadith we do not know to be narrated from Usamah except through this channel with this chain."
"2612","2609 — Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim and Ahmad ibn Uthman ibn Hakim narrated to us, the wording being that of Ahmad ibn Uthman, they said: Malik ibn Isma'il informed us, he said: Qays informed us, from Jami' ibn Shaddad, from Kulthum al-Khuza'i, from Usamah ibn Zayd, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: May Allah curse the Jews; they took the graves of their prophets as mosques. And this hadith we do not know to be narrated from Usamah ibn Zayd except through this channel with this chain, and Kulthum narrated from Usamah nothing but these two hadiths."
"2613","Of what Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami narrated from Usamah ibn Zayd: 2610 — Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Jarir informed us, from Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami, who said: Usamah ibn Zayd said: I charged at a man and cut off his hand, whereupon he said: There is no god but Allah; so I finished him off. That reached the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: O Usamah, did you kill him while he was saying: There is no god but Allah? I said: O Messenger of Allah, he only said it seeking protection after I had cut him. He said: He kept repeating it until I wished I had not become Muslim except on that day."
"2614","2611 — And Amr ibn Ali informed us of it, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi informed us, from Shu'ayb ibn Safwan, from Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami, from Usamah ibn Zayd, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: I killed a man who said: There is no god but Allah, and that reached the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: What about 'There is no god but Allah'? He kept repeating it until I wished I had not known Islam except on that day. And we do not know that Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami narrated from Usamah ibn Zayd except this hadith."
"2615","Of what Abu Zibyan narrated from Usamah ibn Zayd: 2612 — Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi informed us, he said: Mansur ibn Abi al-Aswad informed us, from Husayn, i.e. Ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Zibyan, who said: I heard Usamah ibn Zayd, may Allah be pleased with him, say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent us in the army of al-Huraqat, and when we had routed them, I and a man of the Ansar pursued a man of them; he said: There is no god but Allah, so the Ansari held back from him, while I thought he had only said it seeking protection, so I killed him. The Ansari reported that to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Usamah, did you kill him while he was saying: There is no god but Allah? How will you deal with 'There is no god but Allah' on the Day of Resurrection? He kept saying that until I felt I had not become Muslim except on that day."
"2616","Of what al-Sha'bi narrated from Usamah ibn Zayd: 2613 — Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Mu'adh ibn Hisham informed us, he said: Hammam informed us, from Qatadah, from Azrah, from al-Sha'bi, who said: Usamah ibn Zayd informed me that he was riding behind the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from Jam', and it (the mount) did not hasten its pace until he stoned the Jamrah. And we do not know that al-Sha'bi narrated from Usamah anything but this hadith, and none narrated it from al-Sha'bi except Azrah, and this Azrah is Azrah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from whom Qatadah, Dawud ibn Abi Hind, and others narrated."
"2617","Of what Nafi', the freedman of Ibn Umar, narrated from Usamah ibn Zayd: 2614 — Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, he said: Abu Bakr al-Hanafi informed us, from Abdullah ibn Nafi', from his father, from Usamah ibn Zayd, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet said: Do not face the qiblah while defecating or urinating. And we do not know that Nafi' narrated with a chain from Usamah except this hadith, and it is not narrated from Usamah except through this route."
"2618","Of what Qays ibn Abi Hazim narrated from Usamah ibn Zayd: 2615 — Abdullah ibn Muhammad al-Minqari narrated to us, he said: Abu Usamah informed us, from Isma'il, from Qays ibn Abi Hazim, from Usamah ibn Zayd, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: When Zayd was struck down, Usamah came and stood facing him, and his eye shed tears, so he turned away; when the next day came he came and stood, and he said: Shall I meet from you today what I met yesterday? So he turned away. And we do not know that Qays narrated with a chain from Usamah except this hadith, and Abu Usamah used to narrate this hadith from Qays, that Usamah... and once he raised it, saying: from Usamah."
"2619","Of what Iyad, the cousin of Usamah, narrated from Usamah: 2616 — Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud informed us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Sa'd informed us, from al-Zuhri, who said: Iyad narrated to me — and he was the cousin of Usamah ibn Zayd, and Usamah had married him to his daughter — from Usamah ibn Zayd, that a man from one of the regions came until, when he drew near Madinah, he thought sickness was in it, i.e. the plague. He said: I knew — or he knew — that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I hope the plague will not rise upon Madinah. And we do not know that Iyad narrated from Usamah ibn Zayd except this hadith, and none narrated it from him except al-Zuhri."
"2620","Of what Abu Sa'id al-Maqburi narrated from Usamah ibn Zayd: 2617 — Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi informed us, he said: Thabit ibn Qays Abu al-Ghusn informed us, he said: Abu Sa'id al-Maqburi informed us, he said: Usamah ibn Zayd, may Allah be pleased with him, narrated to me, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to fast days continuously until it was said: He does not break his fast, and he would break his fast for days until it was said: He hardly fasts, and he did not fast in any month as he fasted in Sha'ban. I said: O Messenger of Allah, you fast until we say you do not break your fast, and you hardly fast; I said: And you fast Mondays and Thursdays. He said: They are two days on which deeds are presented to the Lord of the worlds, so I love that my deed be presented while I am fasting; and I fast in the month of Sha'ban, for it is a month people neglect."
"2621","Of what Zuhrah narrated from Usamah ibn Zayd: 2618 — Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud informed us, he said: Ibn Abi Dhi'b informed us, from al-Zibriqan, from Zuhrah, who said: We were sitting with Usamah ibn Zayd in the mosque, and he was asked about the middle prayer; he said: It is Zuhr; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray it at midday heat. And we do not know that Zuhrah narrated from Usamah ibn Zayd except this hadith."
"2622","Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman from Usamah ibn Zayd: 2619 — Khalid ibn Yusuf narrated to us, he said: Abu Awanah informed us, from Umar ibn Abi Salamah, from his father, from Usamah ibn Zayd. [The matn is absent in the source; the entry ends with the chain.]"
"2623","2620 — And Muhammad ibn Ma'mar informed us, he said: Abu Dawud informed us, he said: Abu Awanah informed us, he said: Umar ibn Abi Salamah informed me, from his father, who said: Usamah ibn Zayd, may Allah be pleased with him, narrated to me, he said: I was in the mosque when al-Abbas and Ali ibn Abi Talib came to me and said: O Usamah, ask permission for us to see the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: So I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and informed him, saying: Ali and al-Abbas seek permission. He said: Do you know what they need? I said: No, by Allah. He said: But I know. He said: So he gave them permission. They said: O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), we came to you to tell us which of your family is dearest to you. He said: The dearest of my family to me is Fatimah bint Muhammad. They said: O Messenger of Allah, we are not asking you about Fatimah. He said: Then Usamah ibn Zayd, the son of the one upon whom Allah bestowed favor and upon whom I bestowed favor. End of the Musnad of Usamah ibn Zayd, which is the end of the twenty-fourth part; and praise be to Allah abundantly."
"2624","The Musnad of Mu'adh ibn Jabal, may Allah be pleased with him — the beginning of the twenty-fifth part, and Allah is the Helper — from the hadith of Mu'adh ibn Jabal: 2621 — Ahmad ibn Amr ibn Abd al-Khaliq narrated to us, he said: Ziyad ibn Ayyub informed us, he said: Isma'il Ibn Ulayyah informed us, he said: Yunus, i.e. Ibn Ubayd, informed us, from Humayd ibn Hilal, from Hissan ibn Kahil, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Samurah, from Mu'adh ibn Jabal, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). [The matn follows in the next entries.]"
"2625","2622 — And Ishaq ibn Ibrahim informed us, he said: Quraysh ibn Anas informed us, he said: Habib ibn al-Shahid informed us, from Humayd ibn Hilal, from Hissan ibn Kahil, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Samurah, from Mu'adh ibn Jabal, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). [The matn follows in the next entries.]"
"2626","2623 — And Ziyad ibn Yahya informed us of it, he said: Sahl ibn Aslam al-Adawi informed us, from Humayd ibn Hilal, from Hissan ibn Kahil, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Samurah, from Mu'adh ibn Jabal, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). [The matn follows in the next entry.]"
"2627","2624 — And Ziyad ibn Yahya informed us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abi Adi informed us, from al-Hajjaj al-Sawwaf, from Humayd ibn Hilal, from Hissan, who said: I heard Abd al-Rahman ibn Samurah narrating from Mu'adh ibn Jabal, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: There is no soul that dies while testifying that there is no god but Allah, that returning to a certain heart, except that Allah forgives it."
"2628","2625 — And Ziyad ibn Ayyub informed us of it, he said: Abu Sufyan al-Himyari Sa'id ibn Yahya informed us, he said: Abd al-Hamid ibn Ja'far informed us, from Salih ibn Abi Arib, from Kathir ibn Murrah, from Mu'adh ibn Jabal, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever dies not associating anything with Allah enters Paradise."
"2629","2626 — And Ziyad ibn Ayyub al-Tusi informed us, he said: Dahhak ibn Makhlad informed us, he said: Abd al-Hamid ibn Ja'far informed us, he said: Salih ibn Abi Arib narrated to me, from Kathir ibn Murrah, from Mu'adh ibn Jabal, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever's last speech is 'There is no god but Allah' enters Paradise."
"2630","2627 — Ziyad ibn Ayyub narrated to us, he said: Ya'la ibn Ubayd informed us, he said: al-A'mash informed us, from Abu Sufyan, from Anas, who said: We came to Mu'adh ibn Jabal and said: Narrate to us from the rare hadith of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: I was riding behind the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a donkey, and he said: O Mu'adh. I said: At your service, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Do you know what Allah's right upon the servants is? I said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: That they worship Him and associate nothing with Him. Then he said: Do you know what the servants' right upon Allah is if they do that? I said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: The servants' right upon Allah, if they do that, is that He not punish them."
"2631","2628 — And Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik informed us of it, he said: Abu Awanah informed us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Abd al-Rahman. [The entry is a bare chain fragment in the source; the matn follows in the next entry.]"
"2632","Tell me of a deed by which Paradise becomes due for the servant when he does it. He said: Splendid, splendid! You have asked about a tremendous matter, yet it is easy for one for whom Allah makes it easy: establish the prescribed prayer, pay the obligatory zakah, and do not associate anything with Allah. [The isnad opening is missing in the source.]"
"2633","2630 — Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, he said: Shabbabah ibn Sawwar informed us, he said: Mughirah ibn Muslim informed us, from Habib, i.e. Ibn Umar, from Imran al-Kala'i, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ghanm, from Mu'adh ibn Jabal, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Hour will not come until Allah sends lying rulers, wicked ministers, treacherous trustees, and dissolute reciters whose appearance is that of monks yet who have no desire — or he said: no fear, or he said: awe — so Allah clothes them in a dark, gloomy tribulation in which they plunge as the Jews plunge in darkness."
"2634","2631 — Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, he said: al-Hasan ibn Bishr informed us, he said: al-Mu'afa ibn Imran informed us, from Abu Ghassan al-Madani, from Ubadah ibn Nusayy, from al-Aswad ibn Tha'labah, from Mu'adh ibn Jabal, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You are upon a clear proof from your Lord so long as two intoxications do not appear among you: the intoxication of ignorance and the intoxication of love of life; you enjoin the good, forbid the evil, and strive in the path of Allah; but when love of the world appears among you, you will no longer enjoin the good, nor forbid the evil, nor strive in the path of Allah; those who speak then by the Book and the Sunnah are like the foremost predecessors among the Muhajirun and the Ansar."
"2635","2632 — Abdullah ibn Sa'id al-Kindi narrated to us, he said: Uqbah ibn Khalid al-Sakuni informed us, from Musa ibn Muhammad ibn Ibrahim, from his father, from al-Saluli, from Mu'adh ibn Jabal, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If I take the pulpit, my father Ibrahim has already taken it; and if I take the staff, my father Ibrahim (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) has already taken it. And this hadith we do not know to be narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except through this channel with this chain."
"2636","2633 — And Ibrahim ibn Yusuf al-Muwaffi informed us of it, he said: Isa ibn Yunus informed us, he said: Rabi'ah ibn Uthman informed us, from Sa'd ibn Ibrahim, from his father, who said: The first who preached upon the pulpits was Ibrahim (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"2637","2634 — Humayd ibn Mas'adah narrated to us, he said: Bishr ibn al-Mufaddal informed us, he said: al-Jurayri informed us, from Abi al-Ward, from al-Lajlaj, from Mu'adh ibn Jabal, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). [The matn follows in the next entry.]"
"2638","2635 — And Ziyad ibn Ayyub informed us of it, he said: Isma'il ibn Ibrahim, i.e. Ibn Ulayyah, informed us, he said: Sa'id al-Jurayri informed us, from Abi al-Ward ibn Thumamah, from al-Lajlaj, from Mu'adh ibn Jabal, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he passed by a man who was saying in his supplication: O Allah, I ask You for patience; so he said: You have asked Allah for trial, so ask Allah for well-being. And he came upon a man who was saying: O Allah, I ask You for the completion of Your blessing; so he stood over him and said: Do you know what completion of blessing is? He said: O Messenger of Allah, a supplication I made hoping for good thereby. He said: Completion of blessing is salvation from the Fire and entry into Paradise. And he came upon a man who was saying: O Possessor of Majesty and Honor; so he said: It has been answered for you, so ask. And this hadith we know no route for it from Mu'adh except this route, and we do not know that any narrated it from al-Lajlaj except Abu al-Ward."
"2639","2636 — Ziyad ibn Ayyub narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Harun informed us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah informed us, from Khalid al-Hadhdha, from Amr ibn Kurdi, from Yahya ibn Ya'mar, from Mu'adh ibn Jabal, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Islam increases and does not decrease."
"2640","2637 — Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, he said: Abu Amir Abd al-Malik ibn Amr informed us, he said: Qurrah ibn Khalid informed us, from Abi al-Zubayr, from Abi al-Tufayl, from Mu'adh ibn Jabal. [The matn follows in the next entries.]"
"2641","2638 — And Ziyad ibn Ayyub informed us of it, he said: Abu Amir informed us, he said: Abu Khaythamah informed us, from Abi al-Zubayr, from Abi al-Tufayl, from Mu'adh ibn Jabal, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: We went out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the expedition of Tabuk, and he would join Zuhr with Asr, and Maghrib with Isha."
"2642","2639 — And Ziyad ibn Ayyub informed us of it, he said: al-Fadl ibn Dukayn informed us, he said: Hisham ibn Sa'd informed us, from Abi al-Zubayr, from Abi al-Tufayl, from Mu'adh ibn Jabal, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: We went out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the expedition of Tabuk, and he would not depart at midday until it had cooled, joining Zuhr with Asr; then he mentioned similar to it."
"2643","2640 — Ibrahim ibn Ziyad al-Sa'igh narrated to us, Qabisah ibn Uqbah informed us, he said: Sufyan informed us, from Layth, from Adi ibn Adi, from al-Sunabihi, from Mu'adh — I think he raised it — he said: The two feet of a servant will not move from before Allah, mighty and majestic, until he is asked about four: about his life in what he spent it, about his body in what he wore it out, about his knowledge what he did with it, and about his wealth from where he earned it and in what he spent it."
"2644","2641 — And Yusuf ibn Musa informed us of it, he said: Jarir ibn Abd al-Hamid informed us, he said: Layth informed us, from Adi ibn Adi, from al-Sunabihi, from Mu'adh, similar to it, and he did not raise it."
"2645","2642 — Ali ibn Dawud narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Kathir ibn Ufayr informed us, he said: Ibn Lahi'ah informed us, from Abi al-Zubayr, from Abi al-Tufayl, from Mu'adh ibn Jabal, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent him to a people, and he said: O Messenger of Allah, advise me. He said: Spread peace, offer food, be shy of Allah with the shyness of a man of dignity among your family, and when you do evil then do good, and improve your character as much as you can. And this hadith we do not know to be narrated with this wording except from Mu'adh."
"2646","2643 — Ahmad ibn Mansur ibn Sayyar narrated to us, he said: Abu Ahmad informed us, he said: Amr ibn Abdullah informed us, from Abi Amr al-Shaybani, from Mu'adh ibn Jabal, may Allah be pleased with him, that he said: O Messenger of Allah, advise me. He said: Guard your tongue. He repeated it to him, and he said: May your mother lose you, O Muadh, does anything throw people upon their nostrils into the Fire except the harvests of their tongues? This is the wording of the hadith, and its meaning."
"2647","2644 — Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna and Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, they said: Abu Dawud informed us, he said: Imran, i.e. al-Qattan, informed us, from Qatadah, from Shahr, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ghanm, from Mu'adh ibn Jabal, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The people of Paradise are hairless, beardless, sons of thirty-three years."
"2648","2645 — Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, he said: Mu'alla ibn Mansur informed us, he said: Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash informed us, from Asim, i.e. Ibn Abi al-Nujud, from Abi Wa'il, from Masruq, from Mu'adh. [The matn follows in the next entry.]"
"2649","2646 — And al-Hasan ibn Affan informed us of it, he said: Yahya ibn Adam informed us, he said: Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash said, from Asim, from Abi Wa'il, from Masruq, from Mu'adh, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent me to Yemen and ordered me to take from what the sky waters, and what is watered by ba'l, the tenth, and what is watered by buckets, half the tenth. And this hadith we do not know anyone narrating it from Mu'adh with a chain except with this chain."
"2650","2647 — al-Abbas ibn Abdullah narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Quddus ibn al-Hajjaj informed us, he said: Safwan ibn Amr informed us, from Rashid ibn Sa'd, from Asim ibn Humayd, from Mu'adh ibn Jabal, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he sent him to Yemen, the Prophet, peace be upon him, went out with him that day while Mu'adh was riding and the Messenger of Allah was walking beside his mount, and he said: O Mu'adh, perhaps you will not meet me after this year of mine, and you will pass by my grave and my mosque. He said: So Mu'adh wept in eagerness at parting from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: Do not weep, O Mu'adh, for weeping is from Satan."
"2651","2648 — And Ishaq ibn Jibril ibn al-Mubarak informed us, he said: Yazid ibn Harun informed us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakr informed us, from Abdullah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Husayn, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ghanm, from Mu'adh ibn Jabal, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: A man came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I am a man who loves praise. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said a word — I think he said: It suffices you to live praised and die missed — and I was only sent with the beauties of character."
"2652","2649 — Muhammad ibn Uthman al-Uqayli narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Tufawi informed us, from al-Khalil ibn Murrah, from Thawr ibn Yazid, from Khalid ibn Ma'dan, from Malik ibn Yukhamir, from Mu'adh ibn Jabal, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: I approached the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) — or I confronted the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) — while he was circumambulating, and I said: O Messenger of Allah, which people are worst? So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, forgiveness; ask about good and do not ask about evil; the worst of people are the worst scholars among people."
"2653","2650 — Muhammad ibn Amir narrated to us, he said: al-Hakam ibn Nafi' informed us, he said: Abu Bakr ibn Abi Maryam narrated to me, from Habib ibn Ubayd, from Mu'adh ibn Jabal, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There will be in the end of time peoples who are brothers in public and enemies in secret. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, how can that be? He said: By the desire of some of them for others, and by the fear of some of them of others."
"2654","2651 — And Muhammad ibn Amir informed us, he said: al-Hakam ibn Nafi' informed us, he said: Abu Bakr, i.e. Ibn Maryam, informed us, from Atiyyah ibn Qays, from Mu'adh ibn Jabal, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Jihad is the pillar of Islam and the peak of its hump."
"2655","2652 — Ibrahim ibn Ziyad narrated to us, he said: al-Haytham ibn Kharijah informed us, he said: Rishdin ibn Sa'd informed us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ziyad, from Ubadah ibn Nusayy, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ghanm, from Mu'adh ibn Jabal, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he performed ablution would wipe his face with the edge of his garment. And this hadith we do not know to be narrated with this wording except from Mu'adh, and Abd al-Rahman ibn Ziyad was not a memorizer, though al-Thawri and a large group narrated from him."
"2656","2653 — Ibrahim ibn Abdullah ibn al-Junayd narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Abdullah ibn Bukayr informed us, he said: Khunays ibn Amir ibn Yahya al-Ma'afiri informed us, from Abi Qabil, from Junadah ibn Abi Umayyah, that some people entered upon Mu'adh ibn Jabal while he was ill and said: Narrate to us a hadith you heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about which you have no doubt. He said: Seat me. So one of the people took his hand and he sat. He said: I shall narrate to you only a hadith I heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: There is no prophet but that he warned his people of the Dajjal, and I warn you of the Dajjal: he is one-eyed, with 'disbeliever' written between his eyes, which the literate and the illiterate will read; with him are a garden and a fire — his garden is fire and his fire is garden. And this hadith was narrated by other than Khunays ibn Amir, who said: from Junadah ibn Abi Umayyah, from Ubadah."
"2657","2654 — Muhammad ibn Miskin narrated to us, he said: al-Faryabi informed us, from Sufyan, from al-A'mash, from Abi Wa'il, from Masruq, from Mu'adh, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he sent him to Yemen, ordered him to take from thirty cattle a tabi', from forty a musinnah, and from every adult a dinar or its equivalent in Ma'afir cloth."
"2658","2655 — Salamah ibn Shabib narrated to us, he said: Bistam ibn Khalid al-Harrani informed us, he said: Nasr ibn Abdullah Abu al-Fath informed us, from Thawr ibn Yazid, from Khalid ibn Ma'dan, from Mu'adh ibn Jabal, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever among you prays at night, let him raise his voice in his recitation; for the angels pray with his prayer and listen to his recitation, and the believing jinn who are in the air, and his neighbors with him in his dwelling, pray with his prayer and listen to his recitation; and he drives away by the loudness of his recitation from his house and the houses around him the dissolute jinn and the rebellious devils; and the house in which the Qur'an is recited is covered by a tent of light by which the people of heaven are guided as they are guided by the brilliant star in the depths of the seas and in the barren land; and when the companion of the Qur'an dies, that tent is lifted, and the angels look from heaven and do not see that light, so the angels announce his death from heaven to heaven, and the angels pray over his spirit among the spirits; then the angels meet the two guardian angels who were with him, then the angels seek forgiveness for him until the day he is raised; and there is no man who learns the Book of Allah then prays an hour of the night except that the past night enjoins upon the coming night to wake him at his hour and to be light upon him; and when he dies, while his family are preparing him, the Qur'an comes in a fine, beautiful form standing at his head until he is wrapped in his shrouds, and the Qur'an is upon his chest beneath the shroud; and when he is placed in his grave and it is leveled over him and his companions disperse from him, Munkar and Nakir come to him and seat him in his grave, and the Qur'an comes until it is between him and them, and they say to him: Stand aside so we may question him; and it says: No, by the Lord of the Ka'bah, he is my companion and my friend, and I shall not forsake him in any state; if you were commanded with something, proceed to what you were commanded and leave me in my place, for I shall not part from him until I enter him into Paradise, Allah willing; then the Qur'an looks at its companion and says to him: Be still, for you will find me among neighbors a truthful neighbor, among friends a truthful friend, and among companions a truthful companion; and he says to it: Who are you? And it says: I am the Qur'an which you used to recite aloud and conceal, and you used to love me, so I am your beloved; whomever I love, Allah loves him; there is upon you after the questioning of Munkar and Nakir no grief, nor care, nor sorrow; so Munkar and Nakir question him and ascend, and he and the Qur'an remain; and it says: I shall surely spread for you a soft bed and cover you with a fine, beautiful covering as recompense for your keeping your night wakeful and tiring your day; he said: Then the Qur'an ascends to heaven quicker than a blink and asks Allah that for him, and Allah gives him that; then there descend with it a million of those brought near from the sixth heaven, and the Qur'an comes to him and says: Have you felt lonely? I have not ceased since I parted from you until I spoke to Allah, blessed and exalted, and brought out for you from Him a bed, a covering, and a lamp, and I have come to you with it; so rise until the angels spread for you; he said: So the angels raise him with a gentle raising, then his grave is widened for him the distance of four hundred years' journey; then there is placed for him a bed whose lining is of green silk stuffed with aromatic musk, and there are placed for him cushions at his feet and head of sundus and istabraq, and two lamps of the light of Paradise are lit for him at his head and feet shining until the Day of Resurrection; then the angels lay him on his right side facing the qiblah; then jasmine of the jasmine of Paradise is brought, and they ascend from him, and he and the Qur'an remain; and the Qur'an takes the jasmine and places it upon his nose fresh, and he inhales it until he is raised; and the Qur'an returns to his family and informs them of his news every day and night, and tends to him as the compassionate father tends to his child with news; if one of his children learns the Qur'an, it gives him glad tidings of that, and if his offspring are evil offspring, it supplicates for them for righteousness and devotion, or as was mentioned. And this hadith we do not know to be narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with this wording except through this channel; and Khalid ibn Ma'dan did not hear from Mu'adh; we only mentioned it because we did not preserve it from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except through this channel, so for that we mentioned it; and it is the reward of the Qur'an that comes, and the proof of that is that it is narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): That a morsel or a piece of bread comes on the Day of Resurrection like Uhud — and it is its reward that comes; so everything of that narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) of what will be in the Hereafter, it is the reward."
"2659","2656 — Umar ibn al-Khattab narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Abi Salamah informed us, he said: Sadaqah, i.e. Ibn Yazid, informed us, from Nasr ibn Alqamah, from his brother, from Ibn A'idh, from Amr ibn al-Aswad, from Mu'adh ibn Jabal, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The most hateful of creation to me is one who believed and then disbelieved."
"2660","2657 — Ibrahim ibn Abdullah ibn al-Junayd narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Isma'il ibn Ayyash informed us, he said: My father narrated to me, from Safwan ibn Amr, from Sharahil al-Ansi, from Mu'adh ibn Jabal, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no servant who stands in the world in a station of reputation and showing off except that Allah exposes him before the heads of creation on the Day of Resurrection. And Sharahil al-Ansi — we do not know that he heard from Mu'adh ibn Jabal."
"2661","2658 — Ibrahim ibn Abdullah narrated to us, he said: al-Walid ibn Salih informed us, he said: Isa ibn Yunus informed us, from al-Ahwas ibn Hakim, from Abi al-Zahiriyyah, from Jubayr ibn Nufayr, from Mu'adh ibn Jabal, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was cupped while fasting. And this hadith we do not know to be narrated from Mu'adh, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), except through this channel; and we do not know that any narrated it from Isa ibn Yunus except al-Walid ibn Salih."
"2662","2659 — Ibrahim ibn Abdullah narrated to us, he said: al-Haytham ibn Kharijah informed us, he said: Isma'il, i.e. Ibn Ayyash, informed us, from al-Azhar ibn Rashid, from Sulaym ibn Amir, from Jubayr ibn Nufayr, from Mu'adh ibn Jabal, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw a man wearing a jubbah buttoned — or edged — with silk, and said to him: A collar of Fire on the Day of Resurrection."
"2663","2660 — Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Isma'il ibn Ayyash informed us, he said: My father narrated to me, from Abdullah ibn Abi Husayn, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Mu'adh ibn Jabal, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The key to Paradise is the testimony that there is no god but Allah. And Shahr ibn Hawshab did not hear from Mu'adh ibn Jabal."
"2664","2661 — Salamah ibn Shabib narrated to us, he said: Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Muqri informed us, he said: Haywah, i.e. Ibn Shurayh, informed us, he said: I heard Uqbah ibn Muslim al-Tujibi say: Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Hubuli narrated to me, from al-Sunabihi, from Mu'adh ibn Jabal, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took my hand one day and said: O Mu'adh, by Allah, I love you. So Mu'adh said to him: May my father and mother be ransom for you, O Messenger of Allah, and I, by Allah, love you. He said: I advise you, O Mu'adh, at the end of every prayer to say: O Allah, help me to remember You, thank You, and worship You well. And Mu'adh advised al-Sunabihi of that, and al-Sunabihi advised Abu Abd al-Rahman of it, and Abu Abd al-Rahman advised Uqbah ibn Muslim of it."
"2665","2662 — Dawud ibn Sulayman Abu Mutarrif al-Khazzaz narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn al-Harith al-Makhzumi informed us, he said: Abdullah ibn Amir informed us, from al-Walid ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Jubayr ibn Nufayr, from Mu'adh ibn Jabal, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to seek refuge, saying: I seek refuge in You from greed that leads to natural miserliness, and I seek refuge in You from greed where there is no object of hope — or in other than an object of hope."
"2666","2663 — Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Azdi narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Wahhab ibn Ata informed us, he said: Muhammad ibn al-Sa'ib informed us, concerning the saying of Allah, blessed and exalted: {So whoever hopes for the meeting with his Lord, let him do righteous work and not associate in the worship of his Lord anyone} — he said: Abu Salih narrated to me, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Ghanm was in the mosque of Damascus among a group of the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), among them Mu'adh ibn Jabal; so Abd al-Rahman ibn Ghanm said: O people, what I fear most for you is hidden polytheism. So Mu'adh said: O Allah, forgiveness. He said: O Mu'adh, did you not hear the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever fasts showing off has associated, whoever gives charity showing off has associated, and whoever prays showing off has associated? He said: Yes indeed; but the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited this verse {So whoever hopes for the meeting with his Lord} — the verse — and that distressed the people and weighed heavily upon them, so he said: Shall I not relieve it for you? They said: Yes, may Allah relieve from you worry and harm. He said: It is like the verse in al-Rum {And whatever you give of usury to increase in the wealth of people does not increase with Allah} — the verse: Whoever does a deed showing off, it is neither recorded for him nor against him — neither for him nor against him."
"2667","2664 — Hamdan ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Mubarak informed us, he said: Fudayl ibn Sulayman informed us, he said: Musa ibn Uqbah informed us, from Ubayd ibn Salman al-Agharr, from his father, from Mu'adh ibn Jabal, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A woman does not cease to be cursed by the angels — or he said: Allah and His angels curse her — and the keepers of mercy and punishment, so long as she violates anything of the disobediences of Allah."
"2668","2665 — And Hamdan ibn Ali informed us, he said: Abd al-Rahman informed us, he said: Fudayl informed us, he said: Musa ibn Uqbah informed us, from Ubayd ibn Salman, from his father, from Mu'adh ibn Jabal, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If a woman knew the right of the husband, she would not sit while his lunch and dinner are present until he finishes from it."
"2669","2666 — Ibrahim ibn Abdullah ibn al-Junayd narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Abd al-Rahman informed us, he said: al-Hasan ibn Yahya al-Khushani informed us, from Khalifah ibn Abdullah, from Ubadah ibn Nusayy, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ghanm al-Ash'ari, who said: I said to Mu'adh ibn Jabal: Did you perform ablution from what fire has touched? He said: Yes; when one of us ate food touched by fire, he would wash his hands and mouth, and we used to count this as ablution."
"2670","2667 — Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Bazi' narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Hakim ibn Mansur al-Wasiti informed us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Mu'adh ibn Jabal, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The congregational prayer exceeds the prayer of a man alone by twenty-five prayers. And Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla did not hear from Mu'adh, though he met Umar."
"2671","2668 — Abdullah ibn Suwayd al-Kufi narrated to us, he said: My father informed us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Mu'adh ibn Jabal, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: My Lord, blessed and exalted, came to me in the finest form and said: O Muhammad. I said: At Your service, my Lord, and blessed. He said: About what does the highest assembly dispute? He said: I said: About expiations and ranks? He said: And what are expiations and ranks? I said: Performing ablution fully in cold weather, carrying feet to the Friday prayers, waiting for prayers after prayers. Say, O Muhammad: O Allah, I ask You for good things, abandoning evil things, doing good deeds, loving the poor; and if You intend a trial among people, take me to You untested. Whoever says that lives well, dies well, and emerges from his sins as on the day his mother bore him."
"2672","2669 — Ya'qub ibn Nasr al-Khazzaz informed us, he said: Abd al-Hamid ibn Bahram al-Fazari informed us, he said: Shahr ibn Hawshab informed us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ghanm, from Mu'adh ibn Jabal, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) traveled by night with the people one night, and when morning came he prayed the dawn prayer with the people, then said: The people mounted, and when the sun rose the people dozed after the night journey; Mu'adh looked for the trace of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) following his trace with the people, their mounts on the sides of the road grazing and moving; while Mu'adh was upon the trace of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), his she-camel grazing and moving, it stumbled, so he checked it with the rein, and the she-camel of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) shied from it; then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was uncovered from his doze and turned, and there was none of the army nearer to him than Mu'adh ibn Jabal; so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called him and he said: At your service, O Prophet of Allah. He said: Come near. So he drew near until their two mounts touched one another. Mu'adh said: O Prophet of Allah, the people dozed and their mounts scattered with them — or their mounts turned with them — grazing and moving. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: And I was dozing. When Mu'adh saw the privacy of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: O Messenger of Allah, permit me to ask you about a word that has sickened me. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Ask whatever you wish. He said: O Messenger of Allah, inform me of a deed that admits me to Paradise; I shall not ask you about anything else. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Splendid, splendid! You have asked about a tremendous matter, yet it is easy for one for whom Allah intends good. He said: You believe in Allah and the Last Day, establish prayer, and worship Allah alone associating nothing with Him, until you die upon that. He said: O Prophet of Allah, repeat it; so he repeated it three times. Then the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If you wish, I shall tell you, O Mu'adh, of the foundation of this matter and its highest peak. Mu'adh said: Yes indeed, O Prophet of Allah, may my father and mother be ransom for you. The Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The head of this matter is the testimony that there is no god but Allah alone without partner, and that I am His servant and Messenger, establishing prayer and giving zakah; and its highest peak is jihad in the path of Allah; I was only commanded to fight people until they establish prayer, give zakah, and testify that there is no god but Allah and that I am His servant and Messenger; when they do so they have protected themselves. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No foot is dustied in a deed seeking thereby the ranks of Paradise after the obligatory prayer like jihad in the path of Allah, and no scale of a servant weighs heavier than a mount spent for him in the path of Allah or worked upon in the path of Allah."
"2673","2670 — And Umar ibn al-Khattab informed us, he said: Abu al-Yaman informed us, he said: Shu'ayb ibn Abi Hamzah informed us, from Abdullah ibn Abi Husayn, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ghanm, from Mu'adh ibn Jabal, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), similar to it."
"2674","2671 — Ya'qub ibn Nasr narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Hamid ibn Bahram informed us, he said: Shahr ibn Hawshab informed us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Ghanm narrated to me, from the account of al-Harith ibn Umayrah, that he came with Mu'adh from Yemen and stayed with him in his house and dwelling, and the plague struck them: Mu'adh, Abu Ubaydah ibn al-Jarrah, Shurahbil ibn Hasanah, and Abu Malik were all struck on one day. Amr ibn al-As, when he sensed the plague, fled in great fear and said: O people, disperse in these ravines, for there has descended upon you a matter from Allah's decree which I see only as punishment and plague. Shurahbil ibn Hasanah said to him: You lie; we accompanied the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while you are more astray than your family's donkey. Amr said: You speak truth. Mu'adh ibn Jabal said to Amr ibn al-As: You lie; it is not plague nor punishment, but the mercy of your Lord, the supplication of your Prophet, and the taking of the righteous. O Allah, grant the family of Mu'adh the fullest share of this mercy. He said: Evening did not come before his son Abd al-Rahman — the dearest of creation to him, by whom he was kunya'd — was struck. Mu'adh returned from the mosque and found him distressed, and said: O Abd al-Rahman, how are you? He answered him, saying: O my father, {The truth is from your Lord, so be not of the doubters}. Mu'adh said: And we, Allah willing, you will find me of the patient. He died that night and was buried the next day. Mu'adh ibn Jabal kept sending al-Harith ibn Umayrah to Abu Ubaydah ibn al-Jarrah asking how he was; Abu Ubaydah showed him his plague-boil on his palm, and al-Harith ibn Umayrah wept and feared it when he saw it; Abu Ubaydah swore by Allah he would not love to have red camels in its place. He said: Al-Harith returned to Mu'adh and found him unconscious; al-Harith wept and made others weep. Then Mu'adh recovered and said: O son of al-Humayriyyah, why do you weep over me? I seek refuge in Allah from you. Al-Harith said: By Allah, I do not weep over you. Mu'adh said: Then over what do you weep? He said: I weep over what I shall miss of you — the two late-afternoon times of going and returning. Mu'adh said: Seat me; so he seated him in his lap and said: Hear from me, for I enjoin upon you a bequest: that which you weep over of your going and returning — knowledge is situated between the two boards of the mushaf; if its interpretation eludes you, seek it after me from three: Uwaymir Abu al-Darda, or Salman al-Farisi, or Ibn Umm Abd. And I warn you of the slip of the scholar and the disputation of the hypocrite. Then the death-throes intensified upon Mu'adh, throes none had suffered; whenever he recovered from a swoon he opened his glance and said: Choke me with Your choking, for by Your might, You know that I love You. He said: When he fulfilled his term, al-Harith went to Abu al-Darda in Hims and stayed with him as long as Allah willed, then al-Harith said: My brother Mu'adh enjoined me to you, to Salman al-Farisi, and to Ibn Umm Abd, and I see myself departing to Iraq. He came to Kufah and attended the مجلس of Ibn Umm Abd morning and evening; one day in the مجلس Ibn Umm Abd said: Who are you? I said: A man of the people of Sham. Ibn Umm Abd said: Good folk are the people of Sham, but for one thing. Al-Harith said: What is that one thing? He said: That they testify of themselves that they are of the people of Paradise. He said: Al-Harith said istirja' twice or thrice and said: Mu'adh spoke truth when he told me. Ibn Umm Abd said: And what did he say, O son of my brother? He said: He warned me of the slip of the scholar; by Allah, you, O Ibn Mas'ud, are but one of two men: either a man upon certainty testifying that there is no god but Allah — then you are of the people of Paradise — or a doubting man who does not know where his abode is. Ibn Mas'ud said: My brother spoke truth; it was a slip, so do not hold me for it. Ibn Mas'ud took al-Harith's hand and went with him to his lodging, and he stayed with him as long as Allah willed. Then al-Harith said: I must visit Abu Abdullah Salman al-Farisi in al-Mada'in. Al-Harith went to Salman in al-Mada'in, and when he greeted him he said: Stay where you are till I come out to you. Al-Harith said: By Allah, I do not think you know me, O Abu Abdullah. He said: Yes indeed; my spirit knew your spirit before I knew you: spirits with Allah are marshalled troops — those that recognize one another unite, and those that disown one another besides Allah differ. He stayed with him as long as Allah willed, then returned to Sham. Those were the ones who knew one another for Allah and visited one another for Allah."
"2675","2672 — Ya'qub ibn Nasr narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Hamid ibn Bahram informed us, he said: Shahr ibn Hawshab informed us, he said: A'idhullah ibn Abdullah informed us that he entered the mosque one day with the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) — they were at the beginning of Umar ibn al-Khattab's rule — he said: I sat in a مجلس of twenty-odd, all mentioning the hadith of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and in the circle was a handsome youth, very dark, sweet of speech, radiant, the youngest of the people in age; when anything of the hadith was obscure to them they referred it to him and he narrated their hadith to them. While A'idhullah was sitting with them in their circle, prayer was called and separated them. He swore to me that no night of time passed upon him — neither severe sickness that ailed him nor pressing need — longer upon him than that night, hoping to meet them in the morning. He said: He went early to the mosque, coming and going without meeting any of them, then came early at midday, coming and going, and there was the youth of yesterday to whom they referred their hadith, praying toward a pillar in the mosque. A'idhullah stood at the pillar before him; when he finished his prayer he leaned his back against it, and I kept looking at him until he knew I had need of him. He said: I said: Have you prayed, may Allah set you right? The youth said: Yes. I said: So I rose and sat facing him in ihtiba', neither he telling me anything nor I beginning him with anything, until I thought prayer would separate us. He said: I said: May Allah set you right, narrate to me, for by Allah I love you and love your hadith. He said: By Allah, do you love me and love my hadith? I said: By Allah besides whom there is no god, I love you and love your hadith. The youth said: Why do you love me and love my hadith, when between me and you there is no kinship nor have I given you wealth? He said: I said: I love you for the majesty of Allah. He said to him: Do you love me for the majesty of Allah? I said to him: By Allah, I love you for the majesty of Allah. He said: He took my garment-fold and spread it toward him till he drew me near him, then said: Rejoice, for I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Those who love one another by Allah's majesty are in the shade of Allah's Throne on a day when there is no shade but His shade. When he narrated this hadith to me, prayer was called. He said: I said: Who are you, O servant of Allah? He said: Mu'adh ibn Jabal. And A'idhullah used to narrate the hadith of Mu'adh ibn Jabal often."
"2676","2673 — Abu Kurayb Muhammad ibn al-Ala informed us, he said: Abu Usamah informed us, he said: Dawud ibn Yazid al-Awdi informed us, from al-Mughirah ibn Shibl, from Qays ibn Abi Hazim, from Mu'adh ibn Jabal, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent me to Yemen, and when I had gone he sent after me. He said: So I was brought back, and he said: Do you know why I sent for you? Take nothing without knowledge, for it is misappropriation; whoever misappropriates comes with what he misappropriated on the Day of Resurrection. For this I called you; proceed to your task. And this hadith we do not know to be narrated from Mu'adh except through this channel with this chain."
"2677","2674 — Ahmad ibn Abd al-Jabbar narrated to us, he said: Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash informed us, from Asim, from Abi al-Malih, from Mu'adh ibn Jabal and Abu Musa, may Allah be pleased with them, who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) traveled a journey, those who stayed close to him were the Muhajirun, then the Ansar; and we heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: My intercession is for whoever of my ummah dies not associating anything with me."
"2678","2675 — Umar ibn al-Khattab narrated to us, he said: al-Hakam ibn Nafi' informed us, he said: Abu Bakr ibn Abi Maryam informed us, from Damrah ibn Habib, from Mu'adh ibn Jabal, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the circumcision passes the circumcision, ritual washing becomes obligatory."
"2679","2676 — Zayd ibn Akhzam al-Ta'i narrated to us, he said: Mu'ammal ibn Isma'il informed us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah informed us, from Asim, i.e. Ibn Bahdalah, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Abi Zabyah, from Mu'adh ibn Jabal, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no servant who spends the night pure — or upon purity — then wakes in the night asking Allah for a need of the needs of this world and the Hereafter, except that He gives it to him."
"2680","2677 — Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Abi al-Jawn informed us, he said: Thawr, i.e. Ibn Yazid, informed us, from Khalid ibn Ma'dan, from Mu'adh ibn Jabal, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Arabs are equals to one another, and the mawali are equals to one another."
"2681","The Musnad of Ubadah ibn al-Samit, may Allah be pleased with him — the hadith of Ubadah ibn al-Samit: 2678 — Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ja'far informed us, he said: Shu'bah informed us, from Qatadah, from Anas, from Ubadah ibn al-Samit, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The believer's dream is a part of forty-six parts of prophethood. And this hadith we know no route for it from Ubadah except this route; and Thabit narrated it from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), without mentioning Ubadah."
"2682","2679 — Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ja'far informed us, he said: Shu'bah informed us, from Qatadah, from Anas, from Ubadah ibn al-Samit, may Allah be pleased with them, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever loves the meeting with Allah, Allah loves meeting him; and whoever hates the meeting with Allah, Allah hates meeting him. And this hadith we do not know to be narrated from Ubadah except through this channel with this chain."
"2683","2680 — Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Bazi' narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abi Adi informed us, he said: Humayd informed us, from Anas, from Ubadah ibn al-Samit, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out to us intending to inform us of Laylat al-Qadr, then two men quarreled, so he said: I came out to you intending to inform you of Laylat al-Qadr, then so-and-so and so-and-so quarreled, and it was taken from me — or a word like it — and perhaps it is better for you; so seek it in the last ten: in the ninth, the seventh, and the fifth."
"2684","2681 — Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Hanan narrated to us, he said: Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid informed us, he said: Bahir ibn Sa'd informed us, from Khalid ibn Ma'dan, from Amr ibn al-Aswad, from Junadah ibn Abi Umayyah, that he narrated to them from Ubadah ibn al-Samit that he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I have told you about the Dajjal until I feared — and he mentioned a word —: he is a short man, bow-legged, curly-haired, one-eyed, with the eye effaced, neither protruding nor sunken; if he is confused to you, know that you will not see your Lord until you die. And this hadith we do not know to be narrated from Ubadah except from the hadith of Bahir ibn Sa'd; and more than one narrated it from Junadah ibn Abi Umayyah, from some of the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"2685","2682 — Muhammad ibn Amr informed us, he said: Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid informed us, he said: al-Awza'i informed us, he said: Umayr ibn Hani narrated to me, from Junadah ibn Abi Umayyah, who said: I heard Ubadah ibn al-Samit, may Allah be pleased with him, say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever testifies that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger, and that Isa son of Maryam is Allah's servant and His word which He cast to Maryam, and a spirit from Him, and that Paradise is true and the Fire is true, Allah admits him to Paradise for whatever deed he had."
"2686","2683 — And Muhammad ibn Miskin informed us of it, he said: Bishr ibn Bakr informed us, he said: Ibn Jabir, i.e. Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid ibn Jabir, informed us, from Umayr ibn Hani, who said: Junadah ibn Abi Umayyah narrated to me, who said: Ubadah ibn al-Samit, may Allah be pleased with him, narrated to me, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever says: I testify that there is no god but Allah alone without partner, and I testify that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger, and that Isa is Allah's servant and the son of His bondwoman, and His word which He cast to Maryam, and a spirit from Him, and that Paradise is true and the Fire is true — Allah admits him through whichever of the eight gates of Paradise He wills. And this hadith we do not know to be narrated except from Ubadah with this wording, and we know no route from Ubadah better than this route."
"2687","2684 — al-Fadl ibn Sahl narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Salih ibn Muslim informed us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Thabit informed us, from Umayr ibn Hani, that he heard Junadah ibn Abi Umayyah, that he heard Ubadah ibn al-Samit narrating from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): That Jibril, peace be upon him, came to him while he was ill and said: In Allah's name I charm you from everything that harms you, from the envy of an envier and every eye — I think he said: And Allah heals you. And this hadith we do not know to be narrated from Ubadah with better than this chain."
"2688","2685 — Nasr ibn Ali and Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, the wording being Muhammad's, he said: Safwan ibn Isa informed us, he said: Bishr ibn Rafi' informed us, from Abdullah ibn Sulayman ibn Junadah ibn Abi Umayyah, from his father, from his grandfather, from Ubadah ibn al-Samit, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) followed a funeral he would not sit until it was placed in the lahd; a rabbi of the Jewish rabbis confronted him and said: Thus we do. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sat and said: Oppose them. And this hadith we do not know to be narrated with this wording except from Ubadah, and we know no route from Ubadah except this route; and Bishr ibn Rafi' is lenient in hadith, though his hadith was tolerated."
"2689","2686 — Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ja'far informed us, he said: Shu'bah informed us, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Hittan, i.e. Ibn Abdullah al-Raqashi, from Ubadah ibn al-Samit, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Take from me; Allah has made for them a way: the virgin with the virgin — one hundred lashes and exile for a year; the non-virgin with the non-virgin — one hundred lashes and stoning. And this hadith Qatadah narrated with a chain from al-Hasan, from Hittan, from Ubadah; and more than one narrated it from Qatadah; and more than one narrated it from al-Hasan, from Ubadah, mursal. And al-Fadl ibn Dalham said, from al-Hasan, from Qabisah, from Salamah ibn al-Muhabbaq, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); and al-Fadl ibn Dalham was not a memorizer; the hadith is Qatadah's hadith, though it was narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) through sound channels — a group of the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) narrated that with other than this wording."
"2690","2687 — Ibrahim ibn Ziyad al-Sa'igh narrated to us, he said: Zayd ibn al-Hubab informed us, he said: Mu'awiyah ibn Salih informed us, he said: Ayyub ibn Abi Zayd Abu Yazid narrated to me, from Ubadah ibn al-Walid ibn Ubadah, from his father, from his grandfather Ubadah ibn al-Samit, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The first thing Allah created was the Pen; He said to it: Write; so it wrote what will be until the Day of Resurrection. O my son, if you die upon other than this you enter the Fire."
"2691","2688 — Khalid ibn Yusuf ibn Khalid narrated to us, he said: My father informed us, he said: Umar ibn Ishaq ibn Yasar narrated to me, from Ubadah ibn al-Walid ibn Ubadah ibn al-Samit, from his father, from his grandfather, who said: We asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about urine; he said: When anything of it touches you, wash it, for I think part of the punishment of the grave is from it. And this hadith we do not know to be narrated from Ubadah except through this channel, and we do not know that Umar ibn Ishaq narrated with a chain from Ubadah ibn al-Walid except this hadith."
"2692","2689 — al-Fadl ibn Sahl narrated to us, he said: Abu Ahmad informed us, he said: Sa'd ibn Aws informed us, from Bilal ibn Yahya, from Abu Bakr ibn Hafs, from Ibn Muhayriz, from Thabit ibn al-Simt, from Ubadah ibn al-Samit, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The last of my ummah will deem wine lawful under a name they call it."
"2693","2690 — Khalid ibn Yusuf ibn Khalid narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, he said: Musa ibn Uqbah informed us, from Ishaq ibn Yahya, the nephew of Ubadah ibn al-Samit, from Ubadah ibn al-Samit, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever prays the prescribed prayer, performs it and prays it at its time, meets Allah the Exalted with a covenant that He not punish him; and whoever does not uphold the prescribed prayer nor prays it at its time meets Allah with no covenant — if He wills He punishes him, and if He wills He has mercy on him."
"2694","2691 — Hashim ibn al-Qasim al-Harrani narrated to us, he said: Isa ibn Yunus informed us, he said: al-Ahwas ibn Hakim informed us, from Khalid ibn Ma'dan, from Ubadah ibn al-Samit, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When a man prays and perfects ablution and completes its bowing and prostration — I think he said: and the recitation in it — it says: May Allah preserve you as you preserved me; and when he performs its bowing badly and does not complete its bowing nor its prostration, it says: May Allah waste you as you wasted me."
"2695","2692 — Amr ibn Abdullah al-Awdi narrated to us, he said: Waki' ibn al-Jarrah informed us, he said: Mughirah ibn Ziyad informed us, from Ubadah ibn Nusayy, from al-Aswad ibn Tha'labah, from Ubadah ibn al-Samit, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) visited me while I was ill, among some of the Ansar, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do you know what a martyr is? They fell silent. I said: And who knows who the martyr is? I said to my wife: Prop me up; so she propped me up, and I said: The martyr is one who submits, then emigrates, then is killed in the path of Allah — he is a martyr. He said: Then the martyrs of my ummah are few: being killed in the path of Allah is martyrdom, the belly is martyrdom, drowning is martyrdom, and the woman dying in childbirth is martyrdom."
"2696","2693 — Ibrahim ibn Abdullah ibn al-Junayd narrated to us, he said: al-Hasan ibn Bishr ibn Salm informed us, he said: al-Mu'afa ibn Imran informed us, from al-Mughirah ibn Ziyad, from Ubadah ibn Nusayy, from al-Aswad ibn Tha'labah, from Ubadah ibn al-Samit, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), similar to it; and this hadith we do not know to be narrated from Ubadah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), except with this chain."
"2697","2694 — Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Safwan ibn Isa informed us, he said: Bishr ibn Rafi' informed us, from Abdullah ibn Sulayman ibn Junadah ibn Abi Umayyah, from his father, from his grandfather, from Ubadah ibn al-Samit, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) followed a funeral he would not sit until it was placed in the lahd; a rabbi of the Jewish rabbis confronted him and said: Thus we do. He said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sat and said: Oppose them. And we do not know that any narrated this speech and this act from the Messenger of Allah except Ubadah ibn al-Samit, and we know no route from Ubadah except this route."
"2698","2695 — Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Hanan narrated to us, he said: Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid informed us, he said: al-Awza'i informed us, he said: Umayr ibn Hani narrated to me, from Junadah ibn Abi Umayyah, who said: I heard Ubadah ibn al-Samit, may Allah be pleased with him, say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever testifies that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger, and that Isa son of Maryam is Allah's servant and His word which He cast to Maryam, and a spirit from Him, and that Paradise is true and the Fire is true — Allah admits him to Paradise for whatever deed he had. And this speech we do not know that any narrated it from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except Ubadah."
"2699","2696 — Khalid ibn Yusuf ibn Khalid narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, he said: Musa ibn Uqbah informed us, from Ishaq ibn Yahya, the nephew of Ubadah ibn al-Samit, from Ubadah ibn al-Samit, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The martyr has six traits with Allah: he is forgiven with the first spurt of his blood, the robe of honor — or he said: the robe of faith — is placed upon him, he is secured from the greatest terror, he sees his seat in Paradise, and he is married to the wide-eyed houris. Abu Bakr said: And I think: death is made easy for him."
"2700","2697 — Ibrahim ibn Hani narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Kathir al-Massisi informed us, he said: al-Awza'i informed us, from Yunus ibn Halbas, from Abu Idris al-Khawlani, who said: I entered the mosque of Damascus and sat in a circle, and a man said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say, transmitting from Allah, mighty and majestic: My love is due for those who love one another for Me, My love is due for those who maintain ties for Me, My love is due for those who visit one another for Me, and My love is due for those who spend for one another for Me. I said: Who are you, may Allah have mercy on you? He said: I am Ubadah ibn al-Samit."
"2701","2698 — Ibrahim ibn Hani narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Kathir informed us, from al-Awza'i, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Junadah ibn Abi Umayyah, from Ubadah ibn al-Samit, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: Upon you is obedience in your hardship and ease, and when others are preferred over you, and that you not dispute command with its people unless they command you with open disbelief. And other than Yahya said: That they command you with disobedience to Allah. And we do not know that Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated from Junadah anything but this hadith; and this speech was narrated from Ubadah through many channels."
"2702","2699 — And Ziyad ibn Yahya informed us of it, he said: Bakr ibn Bakkar informed us, he said: Hamzah al-Zayyat informed us, from al-A'mash, from Umarah ibn Umayr, from al-Walid ibn Ubadah ibn al-Samit, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). [The matn follows in the next entry.]"
"2703","2700 — And Ziyad ibn Yahya informed us of it, he said: Abu Attab informed us, he said: Shu'bah informed us, from Yahya ibn Sa'id and Sayyar, from Ubadah ibn al-Walid ibn Ubadah, from his father, from his grandfather — and one of them said: from Ubadah ibn al-Walid, from his grandfather Ubadah — and he said: We pledged to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to hear and obey in hardship and ease. And in the hadith of Umarah he said: In your hardship and ease and when others are preferred over you; then he mentioned similar to the hadith of Qatadah."
"2704","2701 — Yahya ibn Khalaf narrated to us, he said: Abd al-A'la informed us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Makhul, from Mahmud ibn al-Rabi', from Ubadah ibn al-Samit. [The matn follows in later entries.]"
"2705","2702 — And Mu'ammal ibn Hisham informed us, he said: Isma'il ibn Ibrahim informed us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ishaq informed us, from Makhul, from Mahmud ibn al-Rabi', from Ubadah ibn al-Samit. [The matn follows in the next entry.]"
"2706","2703 — And Ibrahim ibn Hani informed us of it, he said: Ahmad ibn Khalid al-Wahbi informed us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ishaq informed us, from Makhul, from Mahmud ibn al-Rabi', from Ubadah ibn al-Samit, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led us in the dawn prayer, and the recitation weighed upon him; when he finished he said: I see you recite behind your imam. He said: We said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Do not do so except with the Mother of the Qur'an, for there is no prayer except with the Mother of the Qur'an. And this hadith al-Zuhri also narrated with similar speech from Mahmud, from Ubadah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); and Mahmud ibn al-Rabi' had met the Prophet, peace be upon him."
"2707","2704 — Ibrahim ibn Hani narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Abd al-Rahman informed us, he said: Ibn Ayyash informed us, he said: Aqil ibn Mudrik al-Sulami narrated to me, from Luqman ibn Amir al-Awsabi, from Abi Rashid al-Hubrani, from Ubadah ibn al-Samit, may Allah be pleased with him, that he stood one day and narrated that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: Whoever worships Allah associating nothing with Him, establishes prayer, gives zakah, hears and obeys — Allah admits him through whichever of the gates of Paradise He wills, and it has eight gates; and whoever worships Allah associating nothing with Him, establishes prayer, gives zakah, hears and disobeys — then Allah, blessed and exalted, has choice in his affair: if He wills He has mercy on him, and if He wills He punishes him."
"2708","2705 — Ibrahim ibn Hani narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Yusuf al-Tinnisi informed us, he said: Khalid ibn Yazid informed us, from Ibn Halbas, from Ubadah ibn al-Samit, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no servant who prostrates to Allah a prostration except that Allah raises him a degree thereby, writes for him a good deed thereby, and effaces from him an evil deed thereby; so increase in prostration."
"2709","2706 — Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Abu Asim informed us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Sulayman ibn Musa, that Kathir ibn Murrah narrated to them that Ubadah ibn al-Samit informed them from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). [The matn follows in the next entry.]"
"2710","2707 — And Yahya ibn Habib ibn Arabi informed us of it, he said: Rawh ibn Ubadah informed us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Sulayman ibn Musa, from Kathir ibn Murrah, from Ubadah ibn al-Samit, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: No Muslim soul dies that would love to return to the world except the martyr when he is killed — or until he is killed."
"2711","2708 — Hashim ibn al-Qasim al-Harrani narrated to us, he said: Isa ibn Yunus informed us, he said: al-Ahwas ibn Hakim informed us, from Khalid ibn Ma'dan, from Ubadah ibn al-Samit, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When a man prays and perfects ablution and completes bowing and prostration — and I think he said: and the recitation in it — it says: May Allah preserve you as you preserved me; and when he performs its bowing badly or does not complete its bowing nor its prostration — I think he said: and the recitation in it — it says: May Allah waste you as you wasted me."
"2712","2709 — al-Hasan ibn Qaza'ah narrated to us, he said: Makhlad ibn Yazid informed us, he said: al-Ahwas ibn Hakim informed us, from Khalid ibn Ma'dan, from Ubadah ibn al-Samit, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led us in prayer in a jubbah — and once he said: in a shamlah — which he had knotted, with nothing else upon him."
"2713","2710 — Ibrahim ibn Abdullah ibn al-Junayd narrated to us, he said: al-Hasan ibn Bishr ibn Salm informed us, he said: al-Mu'afa ibn Imran informed us, from al-Mughirah ibn Ziyad, from Ubadah ibn Nusayy, from al-Aswad ibn Tha'labah, from Ubadah ibn al-Samit, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) visited me while I was ill, among some of the Ansar, and said: Do you know who the martyr is? They fell silent. I said to my wife: Prop me up; so she propped me up, and I said: The martyr is one who submits, then emigrates, then is killed in the path of Allah — he is a martyr. He said: Then the martyrs of my ummah are few: being killed in the path of Allah is martyrdom, the belly is martyrdom, drowning is martyrdom, and the woman dying in childbirth is martyrdom."
"2714","2711 — Umar ibn al-Khattab al-Sijistani narrated to us, he said: Asbagh ibn al-Faraj informed us, he said: Abdullah ibn Wahb informed us, he said: Hisham ibn Sa'd informed us, from Hatim ibn Abi Nasr, from Ubadah ibn Nusayy, from his father, from Ubadah ibn al-Samit, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best shroud is the hullah, and the best sacrifice is the horned ram."
"2715","2712 — Ibrahim ibn Abdullah ibn al-Junayd narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Abd al-Rahman informed us, he said: Isma'il ibn Ayyash informed us, from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Maryam, from Abu Sallam, from al-Miqdad ibn Ma'di, that he sat with Ubadah ibn al-Samit, Abu al-Darda, and al-Harith ibn Mu'awiyah, and they recalled the hadith of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); Abu al-Darda said: O Ubadah, repeat to me the words of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in such-and-such expedition. Ubadah said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed with them in an expedition of his toward a camel of the spoils, and when he gave salam he took a hair, faced us and said: Sit; this is of your spoils, and I have in it nothing but the fay' with you, except the fifth, and the fifth is returned to you; so return the thread and the needle, and greater than that and smaller, and do not misappropriate, for misappropriation is shame and fire upon its people in this world and the Hereafter; and strive against people for Allah."
"2716","2713 — And Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna informed us of it, he said: Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr informed us, he said: Isra'il informed us, from Ziyad al-Musaffar, from al-Hasan, from al-Miqdam al-Rahawi, from Ubadah ibn al-Samit, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed toward a camel of the spoils, then took a hair from the side of the camel and said: O people, nothing of the spoils is lawful for me, not even the like of this, except the fifth, and the fifth is returned among you."
"2717","2714 — And Ibrahim ibn Sa'id al-Jawhari informed us of it, he said: Abu Usamah informed us, he said: Isa ibn Sinan informed us, from Ya'la ibn Shaddad ibn Aws, from Ubadah ibn al-Samit, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed with us toward a camel of the shares, then took a tick from the camel and placed it between his fingers and said: O people, these are your spoils; so return the thread and the needle, for misappropriation is shame upon its people on the Day of Resurrection, disgrace, and fire."
"2718","2715 — Khalid ibn Yusuf narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Ishaq ibn Yahya, the nephew of Ubadah ibn al-Samit, from Ubadah ibn al-Samit, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The martyr has traits with Allah: he is forgiven with the first spurt of his blood, the robe of faith is placed upon him — or he is adorned with the robe of faith — he is secured from the greatest terror, he sees his seat in Paradise, and he is married to the wide-eyed houris."
"2719","2716 — Khalid ibn Yusuf narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Ishaq ibn Yahya, from Ubadah ibn al-Samit, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: There is no man who goes out in the path of Allah asking Allah for martyrdom — Allah knowing he has made the supplication sincerely — then dies, except that he has the reward of the martyr; and there is no man for whom a white hair grows in the path of Allah except that it is light for him on the Day of Resurrection."
"2720","2717 — Ibrahim ibn Abdullah ibn al-Junayd narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn al-Ala al-Himsi informed us, he said: Isma'il ibn Ayyash informed us, he said: Rashid ibn Dawud al-San'ani narrated to me, from Ya'la ibn Shaddad ibn Aws, from Ubadah ibn al-Samit — with Shaddad present, who confirmed him — he said: We were with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he said: Is there any stranger among you? — meaning the People of the Book. We said: No, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Close the door. And he said: Raise your hands and say: There is no god but Allah. So we raised our hands for a while, then the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) placed his hand down, then said: Praise be to Allah; You sent me with this word, commanded me with it, and promised me Paradise upon it; You do not break the promise. Then he said: Rejoice, for Allah has forgiven you."
"2721","2718 — Ibrahim ibn Abdullah narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Abdullah informed us, he said: Ibn Lahi'ah informed us, from Abu Qabil, from Ubadah ibn al-Samit, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He is not of us who does not have mercy on our young, revere our old, and fulfill the right of our scholar."
"2722","2719 — al-Fudayl ibn Abdullah narrated to us, he said: al-Rabi' ibn Nafi' informed us, he said: Yazid ibn Rabi'ah informed us, from Yazid ibn Abi Malik, from Abi al-Azhar, from Ubadah ibn al-Samit, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best of my ummah are those who, when seen, Allah is remembered; and the worst of my ummah are those who go about with tale-bearing, separating between loved ones, seeking hardship for the innocent."
"2723","2720 — Nasr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Abu Ahmad informed us, he said: Sa'd ibn Aws informed us, from Bilal ibn Yahya, from Abu Bakr ibn Hafs, from Ibn Muhayriz, from Thabit ibn al-Simt, from Ubadah ibn al-Samit, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The last of my ummah will deem wine lawful under a name they call it by."
"2724","2721 — And al-Fadl ibn Sahl informed us of it, he said: Abu Ahmad informed us, he said: Sa'd ibn Aws informed us, from Bilal ibn Yahya al-Absi, from Abu Bakr ibn Hafs, from Ibn Muhayriz, from Thabit ibn al-Simt, from Ubadah ibn al-Samit, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), similar to it."
"2725","2722 — Muhammad ibn Ubaydullah ibn Yazid al-Harrani narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, from Sulayman ibn Abi Dawud, from Makhul, from Ibn Muhayriz — and another man whom he named — from Ubadah ibn al-Samit, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: I heard the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The dust in the path of Allah and the smoke of Hell do not gather in the belly of a Muslim man."
"2726","2723 — Khalid ibn Yusuf narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Ishaq ibn Yahya, the nephew of Ubadah, from Ubadah ibn al-Samit, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever prays the prescribed prayer, performs it at its time, meets Allah with a covenant with Him that He not punish him; and whoever does not uphold the prescribed prayer at its time meets Allah with no covenant — if He wills He punishes him, and if He wills He has mercy on him."
"2727","2724 — And Raja ibn Muhammad informed us of it, he said: Abu Amir informed us, he said: Zam'ah informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Idris, from Ubadah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), similar to it or close to it."
"2728","2725 — Khalid ibn Yusuf narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Ishaq ibn Yahya, the nephew of Ubadah, from Ubadah ibn al-Samit, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Shall I not point you to what Allah expiates sins with and effaces wrongs with? They said: Yes. He said: Performing ablution fully despite hardships, frequent steps to the mosques, and waiting for prayer after prayer — that is ribat, that is ribat."
"2729","2726 — Khalid ibn Yusuf narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Ishaq ibn Yahya, the nephew of Ubadah, from Ubadah ibn al-Samit, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: There is no soul that dies having good with Allah that loves to return to you except the martyr, for he loves to return and be killed another time, for what he sees of bliss."
"2730","2727 — Khalid ibn Yusuf narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Ishaq ibn Yahya, from his uncle Ubadah ibn al-Samit, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Forbear one who is ignorant toward you, pardon one who wrongs you, give one who deprives you, and join one who cuts you."
"2731","2728 — al-Harith ibn al-Khidr al-Attar narrated to us, he said: Anas ibn Iyad Abu Damrah informed us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Harmalah informed us, from Ya'la ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Hurmuz, from Abdullah ibn Abbad al-Zuraqi, who said: We used to hunt at Bi'r Ihab, a well of theirs, when Ubadah ibn al-Samit came to us after we had caught a sparrow; so he released the sparrow and said: Did you not know that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade hunting it?"
"2732","2729 — Salamah ibn Shabib narrated to us, he said: Marwan ibn Muhammad informed us, he said: Sadaqah ibn Khalid informed us, he said: Khalid ibn Dihqan informed us, from Abdullah ibn Abi Zakariyya, from Umm al-Darda, from Abi al-Darda. [The matn follows in the next entry.]"
"2733","2730 — Khalid said, and Hani ibn Kulthum narrated to me, from Mahmud ibn al-Rabi', from Ubadah ibn al-Samit, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Every sin Allah may forgive on the Day of Resurrection except one who dies a polytheist or kills a believer deliberately."
"2734","2731 — Khalid ibn Yusuf narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, from Abdullah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym, from Isma'il ibn Ubayd ibn Rifa'ah, from his father, from Ubadah ibn al-Samit, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: Donkeys passed by him while he was in Sham carrying wine, so he took a blade from the market and went at them till he tore them open, then said: We pledged to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to hear and obey in activity and laziness, in hardship and ease, to enjoin good and forbid evil, to speak for Allah fearing no blamer's blame, to aid — I think he said: the wronged — and to withhold for him what we withhold for ourselves and our sons. This is what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took pledge upon. I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: After me men will govern your affairs who make you recognize what you deny and deny to you what you recognize; so no obedience to one who disobeys Allah."
"2735","2732 — Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Ghundar informed us, he said: Shu'bah informed us, from Khalid al-Hadhdha, from Abu Qilabah, from Abi al-Ash'ath, from Ubadah ibn al-Samit, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). [The matn is the currency-exchange hadith stated in entry 2738.]"
"2736","2733 — And Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna informed us, he said: Abd al-Samad informed us, he said: Hammam informed us, from Qatadah, from Muslim, from Abi al-Ash'ath, from Ubadah. [The matn is the currency-exchange hadith stated in entry 2738.]"
"2737","2734 — And Abdullah ibn Muhammad al-Zuhri informed us, he said: Ibn Uyaynah informed us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Ibn Sirin, from Muslim ibn Yasar, from Ubadah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). [The matn is the currency-exchange hadith stated in entry 2738.]"
"2738","2735 — And Umar ibn al-Khattab informed us, he said: Hisham ibn Ammar informed us, he said: Yahya ibn Hamzah informed us, from Ibn Qabisah ibn Dhu'ayb, from his father, from Ubadah ibn al-Samit, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Gold for gold, like for like; silver for silver, like for like; wheat for wheat, barley for barley, dates for dates, salt for salt — whoever adds or seeks addition has dealt in usury."
"2739","The Musnad of Awf ibn Malik al-Ashja'i, may Allah be pleased with him — from the hadith of Awf ibn Malik al-Ashja'i: 2736 — Ahmad ibn Mansur ibn Sayyar narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Harun informed us, he said: Yazid ibn Iyad informed us, from Abd al-Rahman al-A'raj, from Abu Hurayrah, from Awf ibn Malik al-Ashja'i, may Allah be pleased with them, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Visit the sick, follow funerals, and it is no harm upon you not to attend weddings; and it is no harm upon you not to marry a woman for her beauty, for perhaps she brings no good; and it is no harm upon you not to marry a woman for her abundant wealth, for perhaps her wealth brings no good; but seek women of religion and trustworthiness. And this hadith we do not know to be narrated with this wording except from Awf ibn Malik; and we do not know that Abu Hurayrah narrated from Awf anything but this hadith; and Yazid ibn Iyad is lenient in hadith."
"2740","2737 — Nasr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Isa ibn Yunus informed us, he said: Abu Hamzah informed us, from Ibn Jubayr ibn Nufayr al-Hadrami, from his father, from Awf ibn Malik, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). [The matn is the funeral supplication stated in entry 2742.]"
"2741","2738 — And Ahmad ibn Mansur informed us of it, he said: Abdullah ibn Salih informed us, from Mu'awiyah ibn Salih, from Habib ibn Ubayd, from Jubayr ibn Nufayr, from Awf ibn Malik, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). [The matn is the funeral supplication stated in entry 2742.]"
"2742","2739 — He said: And Abdullah ibn Salih informed us, from Mu'awiyah ibn Salih, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Jubayr, from his father, from Awf ibn Malik — the wording being Mu'awiyah ibn Salih's — he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed with us over a funeral, and I memorized from his supplication: O Allah, forgive him, have mercy on him, grant him health, pardon him, honor his lodging, widen his entrance, wash him with water, snow, and hail, cleanse him of sins as the white garment is cleansed of dirt, replace for him a home better than his home, a family better than his family, a spouse better than his spouse, admit him to Paradise, and protect him from the punishment of the grave and the punishment of the Fire — until I wished I were that dead one. And this speech we do not know anyone narrating it except Awf ibn Malik, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"2743","2740 — Abu Kurayb Muhammad ibn al-Ala narrated to us, he said: Yunus ibn Bukayr informed us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Ibrahim ibn Abi Ablah, from his father, from Awf ibn Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Before the Hour are deceitful years in which the liar is believed, the truthful is disbelieved, the treacherous is trusted, the trustworthy is betrayed, and the Ruwaybidah speaks. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, what is the Ruwaybidah? He said: The base man speaking in the affair of the public. Muhammad ibn Ishaq said, and Abdullah ibn Dinar narrated to me, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), similar to it."
"2744","2741 — Ahmad ibn Mansur informed us, he said: Abdullah ibn Salih informed us, he said: al-Layth ibn Sa'd informed me, from Ibrahim ibn Abi Ablah, from al-Walid ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Jubayr ibn Nufayr, who said: Awf ibn Malik al-Ashja'i narrated to me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) looked to heaven and said: This is a time when knowledge is lifted. A man of the Ansar called Ziyad ibn Labid said to him: O Messenger of Allah, how is knowledge lifted when it is established and hearts have contained it? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: I used to count you among the most understanding of Madinah's people. Then he mentioned to him the straying of the Jews and Christians despite what is in their hands of Allah's Book."
"2745","2742 — al-Husayn ibn Mahdi narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Mughirah Abd al-Quddus ibn al-Hajjaj informed us, he said: Safwan ibn Amr informed us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Jubayr ibn Nufayr, from his father, from Awf ibn Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and greeted him; he said: Awf? I said: Yes. I said: Shall I enter? He said: Yes. I said: All of me or part of me? He said: All of you. Then he said: Count, O Awf, six before the Hour, the first of them my death. He said: So I wept till the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) quieted me. One; the second the conquest of Bayt al-Maqdis — two; the third a mortality in my ummah taking them like the qu'as of sheep — three; the fourth a trial in my ummah — four; I said: Four; the fifth wealth overflowing and abounding till a man is given a hundred and resents it — five; the sixth a truce between you and the Banu al-Asfar, who gather against you under eighty banners. I said: What is a banner? He said: A flag; under every flag twelve thousand. The camp of the Muslims that day is in a city called al-Ghutah, in a city called Damascus."
"2746","2743 — Muhammad ibn Miskin narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Hassan informed us, he said: Yahya ibn Hamzah informed us, from Yazid ibn Ubaydah, from Abu Ubaydullah, from Awf ibn Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The believer's dream is a part of forty-six parts of prophethood."
"2747","2744 — Muhammad ibn Miskin narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Salih informed us, he said: Mu'awiyah narrated to me, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Jubayr, from his father, from Awf ibn Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: We used to charm in the Jahiliyyah, and we said: O Messenger of Allah, what do you think of that? He said: Present your charms to me; there is no harm in charms so long as they are not polytheism."
"2748","2745 — Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Hanan narrated to us, he said: Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid informed us, from Safwan ibn Amr, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Jubayr, from his father, from Awf ibn Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Will you leave my commanders to me? Your likeness and theirs is but that of a man who bought camels and sheep, brought them to a watering-place, and they entered it and drank the clear, leaving the turbid; so the clear is for you and the turbid upon them."
"2749","2746 — Ibrahim ibn Hani narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Quddus ibn al-Hajjaj Abu al-Mughirah informed us, he said: Safwan ibn Amr informed us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Jubayr ibn Nufayr narrated to me, from his father Jubayr ibn Nufayr, from Awf ibn Malik, who said: We fought an expedition toward Sham under Khalid ibn al-Walid, when a man of Himyar's reinforcements joined us and stayed with us until we entered; no sooner had we met our enemy — among them mixtures of Romans and Arabs of Quda'ah — and they fought fiercely; among the people was a Roman on a blond horse of his with a gilded saddle, a gold belt, and a sword likewise, charging the people and cutting through them; a man came and kept stalking the Roman till he struck him — struck the hock of his horse with the sword — so he fell, then followed with sword blows till he killed him. When Allah granted victory, the youth came asking, and people testified he had killed him; Khalid gave him part of his spoils and kept the rest. When he returned to Awf, he told him what Khalid had done; Awf walked to Khalid and said: Do you not know that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) decreed the spoils to the killer? He said: Yes indeed. He said: What prevented you from giving him his slain one's spoils? Khalid said: I deemed it much for him. Awf said: If I see the face of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), I shall mention that to him. When he came to Madinah, Awf followed him and complained to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); he summoned Khalid while Awf sat there, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What prevented you, O Khalid, from giving this one his slain one's spoils? He said: I deemed it much, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Give it to him. Then he said: Rise, O Awf. Awf dragged his cloak, and Awf said: I have fulfilled what I mentioned to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heard him, and Khalid grew angry. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not give him. Will you leave my commanders to me? My likeness and theirs is but that of a man who bought camels and sheep, pastured them, then brought them to a watering-place, and they entered it and drank the clear of the water, leaving its turbid; so the clear of their affair is for you and its turbid upon them."
"2750","2747 — And al-Husayn ibn Mahdi informed us, he said: Abu al-Mughirah informed us, he said: Safwan ibn Amr informed us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Jubayr, from his father, from Awf ibn Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not take a fifth from the spoils."
"2751","2748 — Ibrahim ibn Hani narrated to us, he said: al-Hakam ibn Nafi' informed us, he said: Safwan ibn Amr informed us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Jubayr, from his father, from Awf ibn Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when wealth came to him, would divide it the same day, giving the married two shares and the unmarried one share."
"2752","2749 — Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Hanan narrated to us, he said: Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid informed us, he said: Bahir ibn Sa'd informed us, from Khalid ibn Ma'dan, from Sayf, from Awf ibn Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) judged between two men, and the one judged against said: Allah suffices me, and an excellent Trustee. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Bring me the man. He said to him: When a matter overcomes you, say: Allah suffices me, and an excellent Trustee."
"2753","2750 — Muhammad ibn Miskin narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Salih informed us, he said: Mu'awiyah ibn Salih narrated to me, from Amr ibn Qays al-Kindi, that he heard Asim ibn Humayd say: I heard Awf ibn Malik say: I stood with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) one night, wanting to observe his prayer; he used the siwak, then performed ablution, then stood praying; I stood with him. He began, opening with Surat al-Baqarah, passing no verse of mercy but that he stopped and asked, passing no verse of punishment but that he stopped and sought refuge; then he bowed and stayed bowing as long as his standing, saying in his bowing: Glory be to the Possessor of omnipotence, dominion, pride, and greatness. Then he prostrated as long as his bowing, saying in his prostration: Glory be to the Possessor of omnipotence, dominion, pride, and greatness. Then he recited Al Imran, doing likewise."
"2754","2751 — And Salamah informed us, he said: Zayd ibn al-Hubab informed us, he said: Mu'awiyah ibn Salih informed us, from Amr ibn Qays al-Kindi, that he heard Asim ibn Humayd narrating from Awf ibn Malik, who said: I observed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he mentioned similar to it."
"2755","2752 — Muhammad ibn Umar ibn Khallad informed us, he said: al-Walid ibn Muslim informed us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid ibn Jabir informed us, from Ruzayq Abu al-Miqdam, from Muslim ibn Qurazah, from Awf ibn Malik al-Ashja'i, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The best of your leaders are those you love and who love you; and the worst of your leaders are those you hate and who hate you, you supplicate against them and they supplicate against you. They said: O Messenger of Allah, shall we not confront them then? He said: No, so long as they pray; and whoever has a governor over him and sees him committing something of disobedience to Allah, let him hate what he commits of disobedience to Allah and not withdraw a hand from obedience."
"2756","2753 - Ahmad ibn Mansur narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Abd al-Rahman informed us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Nimran al-Dhimari informed us, he said: Abu Amr al-Ansi narrated to me, from Makhul, from Abu Idris, from Awf ibn Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Do not kill women."""
"2757","2754 - Ahmad ibn Mansur narrated to us, he said: Abu Salih al-Harrani, meaning Abd al-Ghaffar ibn Dawud, informed us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Lahi'ah informed us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ziyad ibn An'um, from Ubadah ibn Nusayy, from Kathir ibn Murrah, from Awf, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Allah, blessed and exalted, looks upon His creation on the night of the middle of Sha'ban, and forgives them all except a polytheist or one harbouring hatred."""
"2758","2755 - Umar ibn al-Khattab al-Sijistani narrated to us, he said: Nu'aym ibn Hammad informed us, he said: Isa ibn Yunus informed us, from Hariz ibn Uthman, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Jubayr, from his father, from Awf ibn Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""My community will split into seventy-odd sects; the greatest of them in trial against my community are a people who measure matters by their own opinion, forbidding the lawful and permitting the unlawful."" And this hadith, we know no one narrated it except Nu'aym ibn Hammad, and he was not followed in it."
"2759","2756 - Ahmad ibn Mansur narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Ammar informed us, he said: Sadaqah informed us, from Zayd ibn Waqid, from Busr ibn Ubayd Allah, from Yazid ibn al-Asamm, from Awf ibn Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: ""If you wish, I will inform you about leadership and what it is?"" So I stood and called out at the top of my voice three times: What, O Messenger of Allah? He said: ""Its beginning is blame, its second is regret, its third is punishment on the Day of Resurrection, except one who is just - and how can he be just while favouring his relatives?"""
"2760","2757 - Ishaq ibn Shahin narrated to us, he said: Hushaym informed us, he said: Dawud ibn Amr informed us, from Busr ibn Ubayd Allah, from Abu Idris, from Awf ibn Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded us in the expedition of Tabuk to wipe over the leather socks for three days and their nights for the traveller, and a day and a night for the resident."
"2761","2758 - Ibrahim ibn Hani narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Ma'bad informed us, he said: Baqiyyah informed us, from Bahir ibn Sa'd, from Khalid ibn Ma'dan, from Awf ibn Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he stood among his Companions and said: ""Is it poverty you fear, or need, or does the world distract you? For Allah will open for you Persia and Rome, and the world will be poured upon you abundantly."""
"2762","2759 - Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Abu Asim informed us, from Abd al-Hamid, from Salih ibn Abi Arib, from Kathir ibn Murrah, from Awf ibn Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered the mosque and there were clusters hanging in the mosque, among them a cluster of inferior dry dates, so he began piercing it with a stick he had, saying: ""The owner of this will eat inferior dates on the Day of Resurrection."""
"2763","2760 - Ahmad ibn Aban al-Qurashi narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad informed us, from Musa ibn Ubaydah, from Muhammad ibn Ka'b, from Awf ibn Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""I know the last of the people of Paradise to enter it: a man who used to say: O Allah, move me away from the Fire, and did not say: admit me into Paradise. Then the people of Paradise enter Paradise and the people of the Fire enter the Fire, and that man remains, and he says: My Lord, why am I here? He says: That is what you used to ask for, O son of Adam. He says: My Lord, bring me near to Paradise. He says: O son of Adam, you had not asked Me for that. Then Allah creates for him a tree at the gate of Paradise, and he says: My Lord, bring me near to this tree so I may eat from its fruit and shade myself in its shade. He says: O son of Adam, had you not asked Me to move you away from the Fire? He keeps asking until it is said to him: Go, yours is what your feet reach and your eyes see."""
"2764","2761 - And Ahmad ibn Aban informed us, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad informed us, from Musa ibn Ubaydah, from Muhammad ibn Ka'b, from Awf ibn Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever recites a letter of the Qur'an, Allah writes for him - I think he said: ten good deeds - and I do not say Alif Lam Mim is that book, but by Alif, and Lam, and Mim."
"2765","2762 - Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Abu Asim informed us, he said: Abd al-Hamid ibn Ja'far informed us, from Salih ibn Abi Arib, from Kathir ibn Murrah, from Awf ibn Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""None gives religious exhortation except a ruler, or one commanded to do so, or an arrogant pretender."""
"2766","2763 - Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: al-Dahhak ibn Makhlad informed us, he said: Abd al-Hamid ibn Ja'far informed us, from Salih ibn Abi Arib, from Kathir ibn Murrah, from Awf ibn Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered the mosque and there were hanging clusters, among them inferior dates, so he began piercing it with a stick in his hand, saying: ""The owner of this will eat - or take - inferior dates on the Day of Resurrection."""
"2767","2764 - Salamah ibn Shabib narrated to us, he said: Marwan ibn Muhammad informed us, he said: Sa'id ibn Abd al-Aziz informed us, from Rabi'ah ibn Yazid, from Abu Idris, from Abu Muslim al-Khawlani, he said: The beloved, the trustworthy narrated to me - to me he is beloved and to me he is truthful - Awf ibn Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), seven or eight or nine, and he said: ""Will you not pledge allegiance to the Messenger of Allah?"" We had recently pledged allegiance to him, so we said: We have pledged allegiance to you; upon what shall we pledge allegiance to you? He said: Worship Allah and associate nothing with Him, pray the five prayers, hear and obey - and he whispered a hidden word - and do not ask people for anything. He said: Some of those men, his whip would fall yet he would not ask anyone to hand it to him. And this hadith with this wording, we know none narrated it except Awf ibn Malik al-Ashja'i with this chain."
"2768","Musnad of Sa'd ibn Tariq, father of Abu Malik, may Allah be pleased with him. Hadith of Tariq ibn Ashyam al-Ashja'i, father of Abu Malik - and the name of Abu Malik is Sa'd ibn Tariq ibn Ashyam. 2765 - Abu Kurayb narrated to us, he said: Abu Mu'awiyah informed us, he said: Abu Malik al-Ashja'i informed us, from his father, he said: When a man accepted Islam, the first thing the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would teach us - or he said: he taught him - was the prayer."
"2769","2766 - Yahya ibn Dawud al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: Abu Mu'awiyah informed us, from Abu Malik al-Ashja'i, he said: I said to my father: O father, you prayed behind the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and behind Abu Bakr, Umar, Uthman and Ali - did you see any of them recite the qunut? He said: An innovation, O my son."
"2770","2767 - Ahmad ibn Mansur narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Harun informed us, he said: Abu Malik al-Ashja'i informed us, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Being killed suffices my Companions."""
"2771","2768 - Ahmad ibn Sinan and Ahmad ibn Mansur narrated to us - the wording is Ahmad ibn Mansur's - both said: Yazid informed us, he said: Abu Malik al-Ashja'i informed us, from his father, that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""Whoever declares Allah's oneness and disbelieves in what is worshipped besides Him, his wealth and his blood become forbidden, and his reckoning is upon Allah."""
"2772","2769 - Ammar ibn Khalid al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: al-Qasim ibn Malik al-Muzani informed us, he said: Abu Malik informed us, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""I was commanded to fight people until they say: There is no god but Allah; when they say it, they protect from me their blood and their wealth except by its right, and their reckoning is upon Allah."""
"2773","2770 - Ammar ibn Khalid al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: al-Qasim ibn Malik al-Muzani informed us, he said: Abu Malik al-Ashja'i informed us, from his father, he said: I never prayed behind anyone whose prayer was lighter yet complete than the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: And Ibn Malik narrated to me the two which al-Qasim narrated; we know none narrated them from Abu Malik except him."
"2774","2771 - Abu Kamil narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman informed us, from Abu Malik al-Ashja'i, from his father: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) circumambulated the House on his mount, touching the Corner with his crooked stick. And this hadith, we know no one narrated it from Abu Malik except Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman, and none narrated it from Muhammad except Abu Kamil."
"2775","2772 - Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim Abu Yahya, the cloth merchant, narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Hanbal informed us, he said: Bakr ibn Isa narrated to me, he said: Abu Awanah informed us, from Abu Malik al-Ashja'i, from his father, he said: Our dyeing at the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was wars and saffron. And this hadith, we know no one narrated it from Abu Malik, from his father, except Abu Awanah, and none from Abu Awanah except Bakr ibn Isa."
"2776","2773 - Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, he said: Surayj ibn al-Nu'man informed us, he said: Khalaf ibn Khalifah informed us, from Abu Malik al-Ashja'i, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever sees me in a dream has seen me awake, for Satan cannot take my form."" And this hadith, we know no one narrated it from Abu Malik except Khalaf ibn Khalifah."
"2777","2774 - Ishaq ibn Sulayman al-Baghdadi narrated to us, he said: Surayj ibn al-Nu'man informed us, he said: Khalaf ibn Khalifah informed us, from Abu Malik al-Ashja'i, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever lies upon me deliberately, let him take his seat in the Fire."""
"2778","Musnad of Abu al-Tufayl, may Allah be pleased with him. Hadith of Abu al-Tufayl Amir ibn Wathilah al-Kinani. 2775 - al-Abbas ibn al-Walid al-Narsi narrated to us, he said: Khalid ibn Abd Allah al-Wasiti informed us, he said: al-Jurayri informed us, he said: I heard Abu al-Tufayl, and a man asked him: Did you see the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: Yes, he was white, handsome, of moderate stature. And none narrated this except Abu al-Tufayl, and none narrated it from him except al-Jurayri."
"2779","2776 - Nasr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Abd al-A'la informed us, he said: al-Jurayri informed us, he said: I heard Abu al-Tufayl say: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and among men were those taller than him, and among them were those shorter than him."
"2780","2777 - Muhammad ibn Mirdas al-Ansari narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Kathir informed us, he said: al-Jurayri informed us, he said: I heard Abu al-Tufayl say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best you change grey hair with is henna and katam - or he said: The Prophet would dye with henna and katam."
"2781","2778 - Muhammad ibn Uthman al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: Abu Bilal al-Ash'ari informed us, he said: al-Qasim ibn Muhammad al-Asadi informed us, from Ma'ruf ibn Kharrabudh, from Abu al-Tufayl al-Kinani, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Will no man inform me about Mudar? A man from the people said: I will inform you about them, O Messenger of Allah. As for its face in which are its hearing and sight, it is this clan of Quraysh; as for its tongue with which it speaks eloquently in its gatherings, it is this clan of Asad ibn Khuzaymah; as for its shoulder, it is this clan of Tamim ibn Murr; as for its horsemen, it is this clan of Qays ibn Ghaylan. He said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) looked at him as if confirming him."
"2782","2779 - Abu Kurayb narrated to us, he said: Mu'awiyah ibn Hisham informed us, he said: Shayban informed us, from Jabir, from Abu al-Tufayl, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) circumambulate the House on his mount, touching the Corner with his crooked stick."
"2783","2780 - Bishr ibn Sahl narrated to us, he said: Habban ibn Hilal informed us, he said: Mubarak ibn Fadalah informed us, he said: Kathir Abu Muhammad informed us, he said: Abu al-Tufayl, may Allah be pleased with him, narrated to me, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) laughed, then said: Will you not ask me what I laughed at? They said: O Messenger of Allah, what did you laugh at? He said: I saw people being driven to Paradise in chains. We said: O Messenger of Allah, who are they? He said: A people from the non-Arabs whom the Muhajirun take captive and bring into Islam."
"2784","2781 - Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, he said: Abu Asim informed us, he said: Ja'far ibn Yahya ibn Thawban informed us, from his uncle Umarah ibn Thawban, from Abu al-Tufayl, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) distributing meat at al-Ji'ranah, when a Bedouin woman came to him and he spread his cloak for her. I said: Who is she? They said: This is his mother who used to nurse him."
"2785","2782 - Ibrahim ibn Sa'id and Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, both said: Yunus ibn Muhammad informed us, he said: Muhammad ibn Mihzam informed us, from Ma'ruf ibn Kharrabudh, from Abu al-Tufayl, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) come to Zamzam and say: Draw water, and give me to drink; were I not afraid you would be overcome over it, I would have drawn myself."
"2786","2783 - Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, he said: Yunus ibn Muhammad informed us, he said: Muhammad ibn Mihzam informed us, from Ma'ruf ibn Kharrabudh, from Abu al-Tufayl, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on his she-camel al-Qaswa raising his voice in talbiyah, while people were jostling one another wanting to look at him."
"2787","2784 - Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, he said: Yunus ibn Muhammad informed us, he said: Muhammad ibn Mihzam informed us, from Ma'ruf ibn Kharrabudh, from Abu al-Tufayl, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) circumambulated the House seven times, touched the Corner with a crooked stick, and kissed the tip of the stick."
"2788","2785 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn al-Fadl informed us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah informed us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Abu al-Tufayl, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: I saw in what the sleeper sees black sheep followed by dusty-white sheep, and I interpreted the black sheep as the Arabs and the dusty-white as the non-Arabs."
"2789","2786 - Uqbah ibn Mukram and Ahmad ibn Thabit narrated to us, both said: Ya'qub ibn Ishaq informed us, he said: Mahdi ibn Imran informed us, he said: I heard Abu al-Tufayl."
"2790","2787 - And Ahmad ibn Thabit informed us, he said: Ya'qub ibn Ishaq informed us, he said: Khalid ibn Abi Yahya informed us, he said: I heard Abu al-Tufayl, may Allah be pleased with him, say: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was sent while I was a boy carrying meat from the plain to the mountain."
"2791","Musnad of Hudhayfah ibn al-Yaman, may Allah be pleased with them both. First the musnad of Hudhayfah: Ammar ibn Yasir from Hudhayfah. 2788 - Abu al-Hasan Muhammad ibn Ayyub ibn Habib ibn Yahya al-Raqqi informed us, he said: Ahmad ibn Amr ibn Abd al-Khaliq al-Bazzar informed us, he said: Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna informed us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ja'far informed us, he said: Shu'bah informed us, from Qatadah, from Abu Nadrah, from Qays ibn Abbad, he said: We said to Ammar: What of your fighting - is it an opinion you held, for opinion errs and is right, or a covenant the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) made with you? He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) made with us no covenant he did not make with all people, and he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Among my community are - I think he said: hypocrites. He said: I heard him - and I think he said: Hudhayfah narrated to me that he said: Among my community are twelve hypocrites; they will not enter Paradise nor find its scent until a camel passes through the eye of a needle. Eight of them, the dubaylah suffices you against them, appearing on their shoulders until it breaks out on their chests. And this hadith, we know it is narrated from Hudhayfah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) only with this chain."
"2792","Ibn Umar from Hudhayfah. 2789 - Ibrahim ibn Hani narrated to us, he said: Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Kisa'i informed us, he said: Ibn Fudayl informed us, from his father, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, he said: Hudhayfah asked a dihqan for drink and he gave him drink in a silver vessel, so he threw it at him, then said: Had I not warned you once or twice that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade drinking in gold and silver, and forbade us wearing silk and dibaj - for it is theirs in this world and ours in the Hereafter. And we know Ibn Umar narrated from Hudhayfah no supported hadith by a sound route except this hadith."
"2793","Jundub ibn Abd Allah from Hudhayfah. 2790 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Asim, trustworthy, informed us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah informed us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from al-Hasan, from Jundub, from Hudhayfah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is not for a believer to humiliate himself. They said: O Messenger of Allah, how does he humiliate himself? He said: He exposes himself to a trial he cannot bear. And this hadith, we know it is narrated from Hudhayfah only by this route with this chain; others than Amr ibn Asim narrated it from Hammad ibn Salamah, and we know none narrated it from Hammad more reliable than Amr ibn Asim, and by him it is known."
"2794","2791 - Ibrahim ibn al-Mustamirr al-Uruqi narrated to us, he said: Umar ibn Habib informed us, he said: Sulayman al-Taymi informed us, from al-Hasan, from Jundub, from Hudhayfah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: A leader of trial will enter Paradise, and his follower will enter the Fire."
"2795","2792 - And Yahya ibn Habib ibn Arabi informed us, he said: al-Mu'tamir ibn Sulayman informed us, he said: My father informed us, from al-Hasan, from Jundub, from Hudhayfah likewise, but he did not raise it. And this hadith, we know it is narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) only from Hudhayfah's narration with this wording; and Umar ibn Habib al-Adawi who raised this hadith was not a preserver, though his hadith was tolerated; and al-Taymi was a man of texts, so he may have raised it once and once not raised it."
"2796","2793 - Muhammad ibn Marzuq and al-Husayn ibn Abi Kubayshah narrated to us, both said: Muhammad ibn Bakr al-Bursani informed us, he said: al-Salt informed us, from al-Hasan, he said: Jundub informed us in this mosque, meaning the mosque of Basra, that Hudhayfah narrated to him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I fear for you only a man who recites the Qur'an until its radiance is seen upon him, and he was a support for Islam, then he withdraws to whatever Allah wills, goes out against his neighbour with his sword, and accuses him of polytheism. And this hadith with this wording, we know it is narrated only from Hudhayfah with this chain; its chain is good; this al-Salt is a well-known man of Basra, and those after him we need not introduce for their fame."
"2797","2794 - al-Hasan ibn Yahya al-Aruzzi narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Ghaffar ibn Ubayd Allah al-Qurashi informed us, he said: My father narrated to me, from Yunus ibn Ubayd, from al-Walid Abu Bishr, from Jundub, from Hudhayfah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: People used to ask the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about good, and I used to ask him about evil. And this hadith, we know no one transmitted it from Yunus ibn Ubayd with this chain except Abd al-Ghaffar from his father; it has been narrated from Hudhayfah by other routes."
"2798","Abd Allah ibn Yazid al-Khatmi from Hudhayfah. 2795 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to me, he said: Shu'bah informed us, from Adi, meaning Ibn Thabit, from Abd Allah ibn Yazid, from Hudhayfah, may Allah be pleased with him, that he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) narrated to me what will be until the Hour comes, except that I did not ask him what expels the people of Medina from it. And we know Abd Allah ibn Yazid narrated from Hudhayfah no supported hadith except this hadith; Abd Allah ibn Yazid is a Companion, and he narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a dozen-odd hadiths."
"2799","al-Nu'man ibn Bashir from Hudhayfah. 2796 - al-Walid ibn Amr ibn Sukayn narrated to us, he said: Ya'qub ibn Ishaq al-Hadrami informed us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Dawud informed us, he said: Habib ibn Salim narrated to me, from al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, that he narrated to him that he was with his father Bashir ibn Sa'd in the mosque when Abu Tha'labah al-Khushani came and said to him: O Bashir, do you remember the Messenger of Allah's (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sermon about the caliphs? He said: No. Then Hudhayfah ibn al-Yaman, who was sitting, said: I remember it. So Abu Tha'labah sat with them, and Hudhayfah said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Prophethood will be among you as long as Allah wills it to be, then He, blessed and exalted, will lift it when He wills; then there will be caliphate upon the way of prophethood for as long as Allah wills it to be, then He will lift it when He wills to lift it; then there will be biting kingship, kingship for as long as Allah wills, then He will lift it when He wills to lift it; tyrannical kingship; then there will be caliphate upon the way of prophethood, then he fell silent. Habib said: When Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz rose, Ibn al-Nu'man said: I hope Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz is he. He said: So Habib was brought to Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz and narrated it to him, and it pleased him. And this hadith, we know no one said in it al-Nu'man from Hudhayfah except Ibrahim ibn Dawud."
"2800","Abu al-Tufayl from Hudhayfah. 2797 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna and Amr ibn Ali narrated to us - the wording is Amr's - both said: Mu'adh ibn Hisham informed us, from his father, from Qatadah, from Abu al-Tufayl, he said: We entered upon Hudhayfah and said: Narrate to us something you heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: If I narrated to you what I heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), you would not wait for the near night. They said: We do not want that from you; narrate to us what benefits us and does not harm you. He said: The dark throng of Mudar will not leave a righteous servant of Allah except they kill him or tempt him; or Allah, and the angels, and the believers will strike them until you cannot protect even the tail of a ravine. And this hadith, we know none narrated it from Qatadah except Hisham."
"2801","2798 - al-Fadl ibn Sahl narrated to us, he said: Abu Ahmad informed us, he said: Kamil ibn al-Ala informed us, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, he said: Amir ibn Wathilah, who is Abu al-Tufayl, informed us, he said: I entered, I and Amr ibn Sulay', upon Hudhayfah ibn al-Yaman, and we said: O Abu Abd Allah, narrate to us - then he mentioned likewise. And this hadith, we know it is narrated from Hudhayfah with this wording only from Abu al-Tufayl from him; and the hadith of Qatadah, we know none narrated it from Qatadah except Hisham, nor from Hisham except Mu'adh; and we know none narrated it from Habib except Kamil ibn al-Ala."
"2802","2799 - al-Husayn ibn Mahdi narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq informed us, he said: Bakkar ibn Abd Allah informed us, from Khallad al-Saffar, from Furat, meaning al-Qazzaz, from Abu al-Tufayl, from Hudhayfah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: People used to ask the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about good, and I used to ask him about evil. I said: O Messenger of Allah, is there after this good any evil? He said: O Hudhayfah, learn the Book of Allah and act by what is in it. I said: O Messenger of Allah, is there after this evil any good? He said: A truce upon smoke, and a community upon impurities therein. And this hadith, we know none narrated it from Furat al-Qazzaz except Khallad al-Saffar, and we know none narrated this hadith except Abd al-Razzaq with this chain."
"2803","2800 - Abbad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Fudayl informed us, he said: al-Walid ibn Jumay' informed us, from Abu al-Tufayl, from Hudhayfah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: When it was the expedition of Tabuk, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered a caller who called out that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) has taken the mountain pass, so do not take it. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) travelled in the pass, with Ammar driving and Hudhayfah leading him, when they came upon mounts with masked people upon them. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Lead on, lead on, and O Ammar, drive on, drive on. So Ammar approached the people and struck the faces of their mounts. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) descended from the pass, he said: O Ammar, I have recognized the people - or he said: I have recognized most of the people - or the mounts. Do you know what the people intended? I said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: They intended to startle the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). And this hadith, we know it is narrated with this wording only from Hudhayfah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); it has been narrated from Hudhayfah by another route, and this route is the best connected and soundest in chain, except that Abu al-Tufayl narrated hadiths from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); and this al-Walid ibn Jumay' is known, except that he had intense Shi'ism, yet scholars tolerated his hadith and narrated from him."
"2804","2801 - Ali ibn al-Mundhir narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Fudayl informed us, he said: al-Walid ibn Jumay' informed us, from Abu al-Tufayl, from Hudhayfah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: Nothing prevented me and my father from attending Badr except that I came, I and he, intending the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when the disbelievers of Quraysh intercepted us and said: Where are you going? We said: To Medina. They said: You intend Muhammad. So give us a covenant of Allah and His pledge that you will return to Medina and not fight with him. So we gave them what they wanted and they freed us. Then we came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and informed him of the news, and he said: Fulfil their covenant for them, and we seek Allah's help against them. So they returned to Medina, and we returned; that is what prevented us. And this hadith has been narrated from Hudhayfah by other routes; we know it is narrated from Abu al-Tufayl from Hudhayfah only with this chain."
"2805","2802 - Abu Hisham Muhammad ibn Yazid al-Rifa'i narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Fudayl informed us, he said: al-Walid ibn Jumay' informed us, from Abu al-Tufayl, from Hudhayfah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not be opportunists, saying: If people do good we do good, and if they do evil we do evil; rather make yourselves firm: if they do good, do good, and if they do evil, do not wrong. And this hadith, we know it is narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) only by this route with this chain; we heard it only from Abu Hisham."
"2806","2803 - Ali ibn al-Mundhir narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to me, he said: al-Walid ibn Jumay' informed us, from Abu al-Tufayl, from Hudhayfah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said in the expedition of Tabuk: Let no one precede me to the water. Ahmad said: Some speech remained in it which I left. And this hadith, we know it is narrated from Abu al-Tufayl from Hudhayfah only with this chain."
"2807","2804 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Abu Asim informed us, he said: Mahdi ibn Maymun informed us, from Uthman ibn Ubayd, from Abu al-Tufayl, from Hudhayfah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"2808","2805 - And Amr ibn Ali informed us of it, he said: Ubayd Allah ibn Abd al-Majid al-Hanafi informed us, from Mahdi ibn Maymun, from Uthman ibn Ubayd, from Abu al-Tufayl, from Hudhayfah, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Nothing remains of the glad tidings of prophethood except the righteous dream, which the Muslim sees or which is seen for him. And this Uthman ibn Ubayd is a man of Basra; we know this speech was narrated from Hudhayfah only with this chain."
"2809","2806 - Ibrahim ibn Hani narrated to us, he said: Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Kisa'i informed us, he said: Ibn Fudayl informed us, from al-Walid ibn Jumay', from Abu al-Tufayl, from Hudhayfah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: His community was shown to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and I stood behind him; when he finished he turned to me and said: Were you here - did you hear? I said: Yes. And Hudhayfah used to say: Is there in this what a man memorized? He said: So he stood among us and informed us of what will be until the Day of Resurrection - or he said: So he informed us of what is between us and the Hour - whoever memorized, memorized, and whoever forgot, forgot. And this speech has been narrated from Hudhayfah by other routes; we know it is narrated from Abu al-Tufayl from Hudhayfah only by this route."
"2810","Tariq ibn Shihab from Hudhayfah. 2807 - Abu Kurayb narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Adam informed us, he said: Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash informed us, he said: al-A'mash informed us, from Sulayman ibn Maysarah, from Tariq ibn Shihab, from Hudhayfah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when the Dajjal was mentioned, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The trial of some of you is more fearful to me than the trial of the Dajjal. There is no trial small or great except it paves the way for the trial of the Dajjal. Whoever is saved from the trial before it is saved from it. By Allah, he will not harm a Muslim; written between his eyes is: disbeliever."
"2811","2808 - Abd al-A'la ibn Wasil narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Thabit al-Dahhan informed us, he said: Mansur ibn Abi al-Aswad informed us, from al-A'mash, from Sulayman ibn Mushir, from Tariq ibn Shihab, from Hudhayfah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Dajjal was mentioned before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: I am more fearful for you of the trial of some of you than I am of the trial of the Dajjal. And this speech has been narrated from Hudhayfah by another route. Thus Abu Kurayb said, from Sulayman ibn Maysarah."
"2812","Abd Allah ibn Ukaym from Hudhayfah. 2809 - Ibrahim ibn Sa'id al-Jawhari narrated to us, he said: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah informed us, from Abu Farwah, from Abd Allah ibn Ukaym, from Hudhayfah, that he asked a dihqan for drink, and he brought him a silver vessel, so he struck his face with it, then said: Do you know why I did this with it? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade us eating in gold and silver, and wearing silk and dibaj, for it is theirs in this world and ours in the Hereafter. And we know Abd Allah ibn Ukaym narrated from Hudhayfah only this hadith; others than Ibn Uyaynah narrated this hadith from Abu Farwah, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Hudhayfah - and that is correct; and Ibn Uyaynah differed, saying: from Abd Allah ibn Ukaym."
"2813","Zayd ibn Wahb from Hudhayfah. 2810 - Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Kufi narrated to us, he said: Abu Ghassan informed us, he said: Amr ibn Hurayth informed us, from Tariq ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Zayd ibn Wahb, he said: While we were around Hudhayfah, he said: How will you be when the household of your Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) emerge in two factions, striking each other's faces with the sword? We said: O Abu Abd Allah, will that really happen? He said: Yes, by the One who sent Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with the truth, it will happen. One of his companions said: O Abu Abd Allah, what shall we do if we reach that time? He said: Look at the faction calling to the cause of Ali, may Allah be pleased with him - keep to it, for it is upon guidance."
"2814","2811 - Ali ibn al-Mundhir narrated to us, he said: Ishaq ibn Mansur informed us, he said: Abd al-Salam al-Mula'i informed us, from Yazid ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abd al-Malik ibn Maysarah, from Zayd ibn Wahb, from Hudhayfah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, is there after this affair any evil? He said: Yes, evil and trial. I said: Is there after this evil any good? He said: Yes, a truce upon smoke, and a community upon impurities. He said: I said: Is there after this good any evil? He said: Yes, a blind deaf trial, and callers calling to affliction; to die, O Hudhayfah, biting upon the stump of a tree - meaning a stick - is better for you than responding to any of them. And this hadith, we know it is narrated from Zayd ibn Wahb from Hudhayfah only with this chain."
"2815","2812 - al-Abbas ibn Abd al-Azim narrated to us, he said: Imran ibn Aban al-Wasiti informed us, he said: Yazid ibn Ata informed us, from Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid, from Zayd ibn Wahb, from Hudhayfah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: No one resembles the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) more in guidance and manner, from when he leaves his house until he returns, than Abd Allah ibn Mas'ud. And the hadith of Isma'il from Zayd, we know none narrated it except Imran from Yazid ibn Ata; and Isma'il transmitted from Zayd from Hudhayfah only this hadith."
"2816","2813 - Ahmad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Ubayd Allah ibn Musa informed us, he said: Shu'bah informed us, from Husayn, from Zayd ibn Wahb, from Hudhayfah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The lizard is a community that was transformed into beasts on earth - or: lizards are beasts transformed on earth. And this hadith, thus Husayn narrated it from Zayd ibn Wahb from Hudhayfah; and al-A'mash, al-Hakam ibn Utaybah and Adi ibn Thabit differed with him, each differing from his companion."
"2817","2814 - al-Jarrah ibn Makhlad narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Majid ibn Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Rawwad informed us, he said: Ma'mar informed us, from al-A'mash, from Zayd ibn Wahb, from Hudhayfah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was sitting eating when a Bedouin came and took a morsel from it, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took his hand and said: Satan attends food over which Allah's name is not mentioned - then he mentioned the hadith."
"2818","2815 - Abu Sa'id Abd Allah ibn Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Habib ibn Khalid al-Ansari informed us, he said: al-A'mash informed us, from Zayd ibn Wahb, he said: People disapproved of something from a commander in Hudhayfah's time, so a man came in the mosque, the great mosque, threading through people until he reached Hudhayfah, who was sitting in a circle; he stood over his head and said: O Companion of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), will you not command good and forbid evil? Hudhayfah raised his head and understood what he meant, and Hudhayfah said to him: Commanding good and forbidding evil is good, but it is not of the practice to brandish a weapon against your commander. And we know none narrated this hadith from al-A'mash from Zayd ibn Wahb from Hudhayfah except Habib ibn Khalid."
"2819","2816 - Ibrahim ibn Isma'il ibn Yahya ibn Salamah ibn Kuhayl narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, from his father, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from Zayd ibn Wahb al-Juhani, from Hudhayfah ibn al-Yaman, may Allah be pleased with him, that he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was among us; whenever a prayer came he descended and prayed, then returned to his station and narrated to us what will be from his station until the Hour comes. There is no commander over a hundred or more, gone astray or guided, except the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) named him to us; whoever memorized, memorized, and whoever forgot, forgot. Hudhayfah said: As for me, I learned evil and memorized it, and knew that if I memorized evil I would avoid it and fall only into good."
"2820","2817 - Uqbah ibn Mukram narrated to us, he said: Ya'qub ibn Ishaq informed us, he said: Malik ibn Mighwal informed us, from Talhah ibn Musarrif, from Zayd ibn Wahb, from Hudhayfah, that he saw a man praying without straightening his bowing or prostration, and said: For how long have you prayed this prayer? He said: For such-and-such. He said: If you died, you would die upon other than the practice of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"2821","2818 - al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us, he said: Ali ibn Qadim informed us, he said: Mis'ar narrated to me, from Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid, from Zayd ibn Wahb, from Hudhayfah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: None of the hypocrites remain except four, and none of the people of this verse remain except three; one of them is an old man who, if he drank water, would die. He said: A man said to Hudhayfah: Who are these who pierce our houses and steal our valuables? He said: These are the wicked."
"2822","2819 - Abu Kurayb narrated to us, he said: al-Muharibi informed us, from al-A'mash, from Zayd ibn Wahb, he said: Hudhayfah saw a man praying without straightening his spine in bowing and prostration; when he finished, Hudhayfah called him and said: For how long have you prayed? He said: For forty years. He said: No, by Allah, you have not prayed for forty years; had you died today you would have died upon other than the nature Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was given. Then Hudhayfah said: A man may lighten prayer yet complete bowing and prostration."
"2823","Rib'i from Hudhayfah; Abd al-Malik from Rib'i from Hudhayfah. 2820 - Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik al-Qurashi narrated to us, he said: Abu Awanah informed us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Rib'i ibn Hirash, he said: Uqbah ibn Amr said to Hudhayfah ibn al-Yaman: Will you not narrate to us what you heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: I heard him say: When the Dajjal emerges, with him are water and fire. As for what people see as fire, it is cool water; and as for what they see as paradise, it is burning fire. Whoever of you reaches that, let him fall into what he sees as fire, for it is cool water."
"2824","2821 - Hudhayfah said, and I heard him say: A man among those before you, the angel came to take his soul, and it was said to him: Did you do any good? He said: I know of nothing. It was said to him: Look. He said: I know of nothing except that he used to trade with people, giving respite to the insolvent and pardoning the insolvent."
"2825","2822 - He said: And I heard him say: A man whose death approached - or he said: death - said to his sons: When I die, gather for me much firewood, kindle fire in it, and cast me into it, until when it has eaten my flesh, reached my bones, and scorched them, take them - meaning the bones - and make them - or he said: crush them - then look for a windy day and scatter them in the sea. So Allah gathered him and said: Why did you do that? He said: Out of fear of You, so Allah forgave him. Uqbah ibn Amir said: And I heard him say that, meaning the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). And this hadith has been narrated from Abd al-Malik by other routes; more than one narrated it from him."
"2826","2823 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ja'far informed us, he said: Shu'bah informed us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Rib'i ibn Hirash, from Hudhayfah, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said about the Dajjal: With him are fire and water; his fire is cool water, and his water is fire, so do not perish. Abu Mas'ud said: And I heard it from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"2827","2824 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to me, he said: Shu'bah informed us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Rib'i ibn Hirash, from Hudhayfah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): That a man died and entered Paradise, and it was said to him: What did you do? He said: They mentioned - or he was reminded - he said: I used to trade with people; I would give respite to the insolvent and be lenient in the marketplace - or he said: in payment - so he was forgiven. Abu Mas'ud said: And I heard it from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"2828","2825 - Ishaq ibn Buhlul al-Anbari narrated to us, he said: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah informed us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Rib'i, from Hudhayfah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he took his bed, would say: O Allah, protect me from Your punishment on the day You resurrect Your servants. Thus I saw it from him in one place, and I saw it in another place from Hudhayfah that he, when he took his bed, would say: O Allah, in Your name I live and in Your name I die; and when he rose from sleep he would say: Praise be to Allah who gave us life after He caused us to die, and to Him is the resurrection."
"2829","2826 - And Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna informed us of it, he said: Muhammad ibn Ja'far informed us, he said: Shu'bah informed us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Rib'i ibn Hirash, from Hudhayfah, may Allah be pleased with him, that he, when he took his bed, would say: O Allah, in Your name I live and in Your name I die; and when he rose from sleep, he would say: Praise be to Allah who gave us life after He caused us to die, and to Him is the resurrection. Abu Bakr said: And Shu'bah did not raise it."
"2830","2827 - Ahmad ibn Aban al-Qurashi and Ahmad ibn Thabit narrated to us, both said: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah informed us, from Za'idah ibn Qudamah, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Rib'i ibn Hirash, from Hudhayfah, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Follow the two after me, Abu Bakr and Umar. Thus Ibn Uyaynah narrated it from Za'idah from Abd al-Malik from Rib'i from Hudhayfah; and al-Thawri narrated it from Abd al-Malik from a freedman of Rib'i from Hudhayfah, naming the freedman of Rib'i: Ibrahim ibn Sa'd, from al-Thawri."
"2831","2828 - Ahmad ibn al-Walid al-Karkhi informed us of it, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Abd Allah al-Uwaysi informed us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Sa'd informed us, from Sufyan, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Hilal, freedman of Rib'i, from Rib'i, from Hudhayfah, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Follow the two after me, Abu Bakr and Umar."
"2832","2829 - Amr ibn Abd al-Malik al-Awdi informed us of it, he said: Waki' informed us, from Sufyan, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from a freedman of Rib'i, from Rib'i, from Hudhayfah, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: Follow the two after me, Abu Bakr and Umar."
"2833","2830 - Ishaq ibn Buhlul al-Anbari narrated to us, he said: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah informed us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Rib'i, from Hudhayfah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Jews said to the people of Islam - or to a group of the people of Islam: What good people you are, were you not to say: What Allah wills and what Muhammad wills. That reached the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: Do not say: What Allah wills and what Muhammad wills; rather say: What Allah alone wills. Thus Ibn Uyaynah said, from Abd al-Malik from Rib'i from Hudhayfah; and Shu'bah and Abu Awanah said, from Abd al-Malik from Rib'i ibn Hirash from al-Tufayl, brother of A'ishah by her mother. And Ma'mar said, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr from Jabir ibn Samurah; and the correct is the hadith of Abd al-Malik from Rib'i from al-Tufayl, brother of A'ishah."
"2834","2831 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Yunus ibn Ubayd Allah al-Umayri informed us, he said: Mubarak ibn Fadalah informed us, from Khalid ibn Abi al-Salt, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Rib'i, from Hudhayfah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"2835","2832 - And Abdah ibn Abd Allah informed us of it, he said: Amr ibn Asim informed us, he said: Mubarak ibn Fadalah informed us, from Khalid ibn Abi al-Salt, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Rib'i ibn Hirash, from Hudhayfah, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: There will be rulers over you who wrong and lie; whoever believes them in their lies and aids them in their wrongdoing is not of me, and I am not of him, and he will never come to me at the Basin; and whoever does not believe them in their lies nor aid them in their wrongdoing, he is of me and I am of him, and he will come to me at the Basin. And this hadith, we know none narrated it from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr from Rib'i from Hudhayfah except Khalid ibn Abi al-Salt."
"2836","Humayd ibn Hilal from Rib'i. 2833 - Isma'il ibn Mas'ud al-Jahdari narrated to us, he said: Sahl ibn Aslam al-Adawi informed us, he said: Yunus ibn Ubayd informed us, from Humayd ibn Hilal, from Rib'i ibn Hirash, from Hudhayfah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"2837","2834 - And Mu'ammal ibn Hisham informed us of it, he said: Isma'il ibn Ibrahim, who is Ibn Ulayyah, informed us, from Yunus ibn Ubayd, from Humayd ibn Hilal, from Rib'i or another, from Hudhayfah, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: There will be rulers over you who wrong and lie; whoever believes them in their lies and aids them in their wrongdoing is not of me and I am not of them, and he will never come to me at the Basin; and whoever does not believe them in their lies nor aid them in their wrongdoing, he is of me and I am of him, and he will come to me at the Basin. And this hadith, we know none narrated it from Humayd from Rib'i from Hudhayfah except Yunus ibn Ubayd; and Sahl ibn Aslam did not doubt it."
"2838","Abu Malik from Rib'i from Hudhayfah. 2835 - Abu Kurayb narrated to us, he said: Abu Mu'awiyah informed us, he said: Abu Malik al-Ashja'i, whose name is Sa'd ibn Tariq ibn Ashyam, informed us, from Rib'i ibn Hirash, from Hudhayfah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Among what people grasped of the speech of the first prophethood: If you feel no shame, do as you wish. And this hadith, they differed about it from Rib'i: Mansur said: from Rib'i from Abu Mas'ud; and Abu Malik said: from Rib'i from Hudhayfah."
"2839","2836 - Abu Kamil narrated to us, he said: Abu Awanah informed us, from Abu Malik, from Rib'i, from Hudhayfah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The earth was made for me a mosque and a purification. And this hadith, we know it is narrated from Hudhayfah only with this chain."
"2840","2837 - Ahmad ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Husayn ibn Kurdi and Ahmad ibn Aban al-Qurashi narrated to us, both said: Marwan ibn Mu'awiyah informed us, he said: Abu Malik informed us, from Rib'i, from Hudhayfah, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Allah created every maker and his making. And this speech, we know it is narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) only by this route with this chain; others than Marwan narrated it halted."
"2841","2838 - Abu Kurayb narrated to us, he said: Abu Mu'awiyah informed us, from Abu Malik, from Rib'i, from Hudhayfah, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Islam will wear out as the embroidery of a garment wears out. And this hadith, a group narrated it from Abu Malik from Rib'i from Hudhayfah halted; we know no one raised it except Abu Kurayb from Abu Mu'awiyah."
"2842","2839 - Abu Kamil narrated to us of it, he said: Abu Awanah informed us, from Abu Malik, from Rib'i, from Hudhayfah likewise, halted."
"2843","2840 - Ali ibn al-Mundhir narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Fudayl informed us, he said: Abu Malik informed us, from Abu Hazim, from Abu Hurayrah, and from Rib'i, from Hudhayfah, may Allah be pleased with him, both said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: People will be gathered - meaning on the Day of Resurrection - and they will come to Adam and say: O our father, open Paradise for us. He will say: Did anything expel you from Paradise except the sin of your father Adam? I am not the one for that; go to Ibrahim, the close friend of his Lord. Ibrahim will say: I am not the one for that; I was but a close friend from afar, afar. Go to the one whom Allah spoke to directly. They will come to Musa, and he will say: I am not the one for that; go to the word of Allah and His spirit, Isa. He will say: I am not the one for that; go to Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So they will come to Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he will intercede, and the Bridge will be laid; the first of you will pass like lightning. I said: By my father and mother - then like wind, and birds, and the running of men; and your Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) will be upon the Bridge saying: O Allah, save, save, until people cross, until a man comes who can do nothing but crawl; and on the sides of the Bridge are suspended hooks seizing whom they were commanded to seize: scratched yet saved, and toppled into the Fire. Then he said: By the One in whose hand is the soul of Abu Hurayrah, the bottom of Hell is seventy autumns deep. And this hadith, we know it is narrated from Hudhayfah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) only by this route; we know none transmitted it from Abu Malik except Ibn Fudayl, and others than Ibn Fudayl narrated it from Abu Malik halted."
"2844","2841 - Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Ibn Fudayl informed us, he said: Abu Malik informed us, from Rib'i, from Hudhayfah, and from Abu Hazim, from Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with them both, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: Allah led astray from Friday those before us - and he mentioned the hadith."
"2845","2842 - Ibrahim ibn Hani narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Mahdi informed us, he said: Uthman ibn Matar informed us, from Abu Malik, from Rib'i, from Hudhayfah, may Allah be pleased with him, that he said: O Messenger of Allah, inform us of the lifespans of your community. He said: Between fifty and sixty. They said: O Messenger of Allah, what of those of seventy? He said: Few of my community reach it; may Allah have mercy on those of seventy, and may Allah have mercy on those of eighty. And this speech, we know it is narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with this wording only from Hudhayfah with this chain; and this Uthman ibn Matar is a man of Basra, not strong."
"2846","2843 - Abu Kamil and al-Nadr ibn Tahir narrated to us, both said: al-Fudayl ibn Sulayman informed us, he said: Abu Malik informed us, from Rib'i, from Hudhayfah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: We are not inherited from; what we leave is charity. And this speech, we know it is narrated from Hudhayfah only by this route; none narrated it from Abu Malik except al-Fudayl ibn Sulayman."
"2847","2844 - Ali ibn al-Mundhir al-Kufi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Fudayl informed us, he said: Abu Malik informed us, from Rib'i, from Hudhayfah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I was sitting with Umar when his companions asked him about trials. He said: Which of you heard it? They said: We did. He said: Perhaps you mean a man's trial in his family, wealth and child. They said: Yes. He said: No, those are expiated by prayer, fasting and charity; but which of you heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) speak of the trials that surge like the waves of the sea? The people fell silent, so I said: I did. He said: You are - I think he said: bold. He said: I said: Trials are presented to hearts; any heart that rejects them, a white dot is marked in it, and any heart that absorbs them, a black dot is marked in it, until the heart becomes two hearts: a white heart like smooth rock, no trial harms it as long as the heavens and earth endure; and another black, overturned, recognizing no good and rejecting no evil except what it absorbed of its desire. And I narrated to him that between it and him is a locked door about to be broken. Umar said: Had it been opened it would be returned and locked. I said: No, rather it will be broken. And I narrated to him that that door is the killing of a man - or his death - a hadith without exaggerations."
"2848","2845 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn Habib narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Fudayl informed us, he said: Abu Malik al-Ashja'i informed us, from Rib'i ibn Hirash, from Hudhayfah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: We were favoured over people by three: the whole earth was made for us a mosque and a purification when we find no water; our rows were made like the rows of angels; and I was given these verses from the end of Surat al-Baqarah from a treasure-house under the Throne - none before me was given them, nor after me."
"2849","2846 - Raja ibn al-Jarud narrated to us, he said: Zakariyya ibn Adi informed us, he said: Ubayd Allah ibn Amr informed us, from Zayd ibn Abi Unaysah, from Zubayd, from Abu Burdah, from Rib'i ibn Hirash, from Hudhayfah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: Whoever wears a silk garment, Allah will clothe him in a garment of fire - not of your days, but of Allah's long days."
"2850","Kathir ibn Abi Kathir from Rib'i from Hudhayfah. 2847 - Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, he said: al-Dahhak ibn Makhlad informed us, he said: Kathir ibn Abi Kathir informed us, from Rib'i ibn Hirash, from Hudhayfah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"2851","2848 - And Ahmad ibn al-Miqdam informed us of it, he said: Muhammad ibn Bakr informed us, he said: Kathir ibn Abi Kathir informed us, from Rib'i, from Hudhayfah, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: No people walk to Allah's ruler to humiliate him except Allah humiliates them before the Day of Resurrection. And this speech, we know it is narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with this wording only from Hudhayfah's hadith with this chain."
"2852","Ubayd ibn al-Tufayl from Rib'i. 2849 - al-Qasim ibn Bishr ibn Ma'ruf narrated to us, he said: Qabisah ibn Uqbah informed us, he said: Ubayd ibn al-Tufayl informed us, from Rib'i ibn Hirash, from Hudhayfah, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: A time will come upon my community when they will wish for the Dajjal. It was said: Why, O Messenger of Allah? He said: He took his ears - or he said: He took his ear - and shook them, then said: Because of what they meet of trials - or a word like it. And this speech, we know it is narrated with this wording only from Hudhayfah with this chain; and this Ubayd ibn al-Tufayl is a well-known man of Kufa, a group narrated from him."
"2853","Nu'aym ibn Abi Hind from Rib'i from Hudhayfah. 2850 - Musarrif ibn Amr al-Kufi narrated to us, he said: Abu Usamah informed us, he said: al-Ajlah narrated to me, he said: Nu'aym ibn Abi Hind narrated to me, from Rib'i ibn Hirash, he said: I sat with Abu Mas'ud al-Ansari and Hudhayfah, and one of them said to the other: Narrate what you heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: No, rather you narrate. So one of them narrated and the other confirmed him. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: A man will be brought on the Day of Resurrection and Allah will say: Look into his deed. He will say: My Lord, I never did good except that I had wealth and I dealt with people through it; whoever was wealthy I eased for him, and whoever was insolvent I gave him respite until ease. Allah, blessed and exalted, will say: I am most deserving to ease, and He forgives him. The other said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say this."
"2854","2851 - Then the other said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: A man will be brought on the Day of Resurrection who had said to his family: When I die, burn me, then crush me, then face a stormy wind and scatter me. So Allah will gather him on the Day of Resurrection and say to him: Why did you do it? He will say: Out of fear of You. He said: So He forgives him. And the other said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say it."
"2855","2852 - Ali ibn Sa'id al-Masruqi narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Ya'la informed us, he said: al-Ajlah informed us, from Nu'aym ibn Abi Hind, from Rib'i ibn Hirash, he said: I sat with Hudhayfah ibn al-Yaman and Abu Mas'ud, and one of them said: Narrate what you heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: Rather you narrate. So one of them narrated and the other confirmed him. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: A man will be brought on the Day of Resurrection who had said to his family: When I die, burn me and crush me, then face a stormy wind and scatter me. He said: So Allah will gather him on the Day of Resurrection. He said: Why did you do this? He said: Out of fear of You. He said: So He forgave him. The other said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - meaning - say that."
"2856","2853 - Ibrahim ibn Isma'il ibn Yahya ibn Salamah ibn Kuhayl narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, from his father, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from Nu'aym ibn Abi Hind al-Ashja'i, from Rib'i ibn Hirash, that Hudhayfah and Abu Mas'ud - one of them narrated and the other confirmed him - he said: There was a man among the Children of Israel with much wealth; when death came to him he said to his family: Obey me in what I command you, or I will entrust this wealth of mine to others. When I die, take me and burn me, then grind me, then wait until a stormy windy day and scatter me in the wind. They did that with him, so Allah, blessed and exalted, gathered him - and he had never done any good - and his Lord said to him: Why did you do this? He said: Out of fear of You, my Lord. He said: So Allah's mercy reached him. And we know Salamah narrated from Nu'aym only this hadith."
"2857","2854 - Bishr ibn Adam narrated to us, he said: Hafs ibn Umar ibn al-Harith al-Namari informed us, he said: al-Hasan ibn Abi Ja'far informed us, from Muhammad ibn Juhadah, from Nu'aym ibn Abi Hind, from Rib'i, from Hudhayfah, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever has a day's fast sealed for him enters Paradise. And we know none narrated it from Nu'aym ibn Abi Hind except Muhammad ibn Juhadah, nor from Muhammad except al-Hasan ibn Abi Ja'far."
"2858","Mansur from Rib'i from Hudhayfah. 2855 - Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Jarir informed us, from Mansur, from Rib'i, from Hudhayfah, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: Do not precede the month until you complete the number or see the crescent; then fast, and do not break fast until you complete the number or see the crescent."
"2859","2856 - And Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna informed us of it, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi informed us, he said: al-Thawri informed us, from Mansur, from Rib'i, from a man among the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) likewise. And we know no one said in it from Hudhayfah except Jarir."
"2860","2857 - Umar ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-Asadi narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, he said: Qays informed us, from Mansur, from Rib'i, from Hudhayfah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade adorning with gold. And this hadith, we know no one narrated it from Mansur from Rib'i from Hudhayfah except Qays, nor from Qays except Muhammad ibn al-Hasan."
"2861","2858 - Ahmad ibn Sinan al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Harun informed us, he said: al-Awwam ibn Hawshab informed us, from Mansur, meaning Ibn al-Mu'tamir, from Rib'i ibn Hirash, he said: Hudhayfah said: Come near, O assembly of Mudar; by Allah, you will keep tempting and killing every believer, or Allah, and His angels, and the believers will strike you until you cannot protect the belly of a ravine. They said: Why did you put us forward when we are like that? He said: Among you is the master of Adam's children (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and among you are forerunners like the forerunners of horses."
"2862","2859 - Muhammad ibn Abi al-Bakhtari narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Adam informed us, he said: al-Mufaddal ibn Muhalhal informed us, from Mansur, from Rib'i, from Hudhayfah, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: I know best what is with the Dajjal: with him is a fire that does not burn, and cool water; whoever reaches him, let him close his eyes and enter his fire, for it is but cool water."
"2863","Abu Husayn from Abu Wa'il from Hudhayfah ibn al-Yaman. 2860 - Abd Allah ibn Sa'id al-Ashajj narrated to us, he said: Ishaq ibn Sulayman al-Razi informed us, from Abu Sinan, from Abu Husayn, from Abu Wa'il, from Hudhayfah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: We were commanded with the tooth-stick when we rose at night. And we know Abu Husayn narrated from Abu Wa'il from Hudhayfah only this hadith."
"2864","Mansur from Abu Wa'il from Hudhayfah. 2861 - Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Jarir, meaning Ibn Abd al-Hamid, informed us, from Mansur, from Abu Wa'il, from Hudhayfah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) rose at night, he would rub his mouth with the tooth-stick."
"2865","2862 - Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Jarir informed us, from Mansur, from Abu Wa'il, from Hudhayfah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood among us in a station and informed us of what will be until the Day of Resurrection. And this hadith has been narrated from Hudhayfah by other routes, and narrated from Abu Wa'il by other routes; we know none narrated it from Abu Wa'il more eminent than Mansur."
"2866","al-A'mash from Abu Wa'il from Hudhayfah. 2863 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Abu Mu'awiyah informed us, he said: al-A'mash informed us, from Shaqiq, from Hudhayfah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I was with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he came to a refuse heap of a people and urinated standing; I went to withdraw from him, but he called me until I was at his heels; then he performed ablution and wiped over his leather socks."
"2867","2864 - And Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna informed us of it, he said: Yahya ibn Sa'id informed us, he said: al-A'mash informed us, he said: Shaqiq informed us, from Hudhayfah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I was walking with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he mentioned likewise."
"2868","2865 - And Abd Allah ibn Sa'id informed us of it, he said: Abd Allah ibn Idris informed us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Wa'il, from Hudhayfah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to a refuse heap of a people and urinated standing; then he performed ablution and wiped over his leather socks. And this hadith has been narrated from Hudhayfah by other routes from Abu Wa'il from him; some of Abu Wa'il's companions said it from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah."
"2869","2866 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Abu Mu'awiyah informed us, he said: al-A'mash informed us, from Shaqiq, from Hudhayfah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Dajjal is blind in the left eye, curly-haired; with him are a paradise and a fire: his fire is paradise, and his paradise is fire."
"2870","2867 - Sa'id ibn Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Umawi and Ibrahim ibn Sa'id al-Jawhari narrated to us - the wording is Ibrahim's - from Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Umawi, he said: al-A'mash informed us, from Shaqiq ibn Salamah, from Hudhayfah ibn al-Yaman, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: With the Dajjal are a paradise and a fire, a mountain of bread, and a river of water; his fire is paradise and his paradise is fire; he is curly-haired, with the left eye effaced. And this speech, we know it is narrated with this wording from Hudhayfah only with this chain."
"2871","2868 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Abu Mu'awiyah informed us, from al-A'mash, from Shaqiq, from Hudhayfah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Count for me how many utter Islam. He said: So we wrote them and found them five hundred. We said: O Messenger of Allah, do you fear for us? He said: One of us would pray only secretly."
"2872","2869 - And al-Fadl ibn Sahl informed us, he said: al-Ahwas ibn Jawwab informed us, from Sulayman ibn Qarm, from al-A'mash, from Abu Wa'il, from Hudhayfah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Count for me how many utter Islam. So we counted them, we being between six hundred and seven hundred. We said: Do you fear for us? He said: You do not know. Then we were tried until a man would pray only concealed. And this hadith, we know it is narrated from Hudhayfah only with this chain; we know it was narrated from none other than Abu Hudhayfah."
"2873","2870 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Waki' ibn al-Jarrah informed us, he said: al-A'mash informed us, from Abu Wa'il, from Hudhayfah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The hypocrites among you today are more evil than the hypocrites at the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). We said: O Abu Abd Allah, how is that? He said: Those concealed their hypocrisy, while these proclaim it."
"2874","2871 - And Ahmad ibn Yazdad al-Kufi informed us, he said: Amr ibn Abd al-Ghaffar informed us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Wa'il, from Hudhayfah, likewise. And this hadith, we know it is narrated with this wording only from Hudhayfah; it was narrated from Abu Wa'il from Hudhayfah by other routes."
"2875","2872 - Abd al-Wahid ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Muslim informed us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Wa'il, from Hudhayfah."
"2876","2873 - And Yusuf ibn Musa informed us of it, he said: Jarir informed us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Wa'il, from Hudhayfah."
"2877","2874 - And Abu Musa informed us of it, he said: Abu Mu'awiyah informed us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Wa'il, from Hudhayfah - their wordings close together - he said: I was with Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, and he said: Which of you remembers the Messenger of Allah's (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) hadith about trial? He said: I said: I remember it as I heard it from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: You are bold. I said: A man's trial in himself, his family and his wealth is expiated by fasting, prayer, charity, commanding good and forbidding evil. Umar said: That is not what I mean; I mean that which surges like the sea's waves. He said: I said: O Commander of the Faithful, there is no harm for you in it; between you and it is a locked door. He said: Will the door be broken or opened? I said: Rather broken. He said: If broken, will it never be locked? I said: Yes. He said: So we feared to ask him. He said: So we said to Masruq: Ask him. He said: So we said: Did Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, know whom he meant? He said: Yes, as he knew that before tomorrow is tonight; I narrated to him a hadith without exaggerations. And this speech, more than one narrated it from Abu Wa'il from Hudhayfah."
"2878","2875 - Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Abu Yahya al-Himmani Abd al-Hamid ibn Abd al-Rahman informed us, he said: al-A'mash informed us, from Abu Wa'il, from Hudhayfah, may Allah be pleased with him, that he said: No one resembles the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) more in manner and guidance than Abd Allah ibn Mas'ud. And this hadith, we know it is narrated from al-A'mash from Abu Wa'il from Hudhayfah only from Abu Yahya al-Himmani's hadith."
"2879","2876 - And Sulayman ibn Ubayd Allah al-Ghaylani and al-Jarrah ibn Makhlad informed us - the wording is Sulayman's - both said: Abu Qutaybah informed us, he said: Shu'bah informed us, from Sulayman, from Abu Wa'il, from Hudhayfah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"2880","2877 - And al-Fadl ibn Sahl informed us of it, he said: Abu al-Nadr Hashim ibn al-Qasim informed us, he said: Muhammad ibn Talhah ibn Musarrif informed us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Wa'il, from Hudhayfah, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he forbade wearing silk and dibaj, and drinking in gold and silver vessels, and said: They are theirs in this world and yours in the Hereafter."
"2881","2878 - Ubayd Allah ibn Yusuf al-Thaqafi narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Abis informed us, he said: al-A'mash and others informed us, from Abu Wa'il, from Hudhayfah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade wearing silk and dibaj, and drinking in gold and silver vessels, and said: They are theirs in this world and ours in the Hereafter. And the hadith of Shu'bah from Sulayman from Abu Wa'il from Hudhayfah, we know none narrated it from Shu'bah except Abu Qutaybah; the hadith is known from Muhammad ibn Talhah's hadith, and Muhammad ibn Talhah followed Ali ibn Abis."
"2882","2879 - Ibrahim ibn Sa'id al-Jawhari narrated to us, he said: Abu Ahmad informed us, he said: Qays ibn al-Rabi' informed us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Wa'il, he said: I know it only from Hudhayfah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"2883","2880 - And al-Husayn ibn Ali ibn Ja'far al-Ahmar informed us of it, he said: Dawud ibn al-Rabi' informed us, he said: Qays informed us, from al-A'mash, from Shaqiq, from Hudhayfah, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Woe to the owner from the owned, and woe to the owned from the owner. And this hadith, we know none narrated it from al-A'mash from Abu Wa'il from Hudhayfah except Qays."
"2884","2881 - Muhammad ibn Ma'mar and Ahmad ibn Amr ibn Ubaydah al-Usfuri narrated to us, both said: Yahya ibn Kathir informed us, he said: Ibrahim ibn al-Mubarak informed us, from al-Qasim ibn Mutayyab, from al-A'mash, from Abu Wa'il, from Hudhayfah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Jibril came to me, in his palm like a mirror with a black spot in its middle. I said: O Jibril, what is this? He said: This is the world, its clarity and beauty. I said: What is this black spot? He said: This is Friday. I said: What is Friday? He said: A mighty day among your Lord's days. Then he mentioned its honour, merit and name in the Hereafter: when Allah places the people of Paradise in Paradise and the people of the Fire in the Fire, there is neither night nor day there - Allah knows the measure of those hours - and when Friday comes at the Friday time when the people of Friday go out to their Friday, a caller will call: O people of Paradise, go out to the Abode of Increase. So they will go out upon dunes of musk. Hudhayfah said: By Allah, it is whiter than your flour. When they sit and the people take their places, Allah will send upon them a wind called al-Muthirah, stirring upon them white musk, entering it into their garments and bringing it out of their pockets; the wind knows that perfume better than a wife of one of you if she were given the perfume of the world's people. And Allah says: Where are My servants who obeyed Me unseen and believed My messengers without seeing Me? Ask Me, for this is the Day of Increase. So they agree upon one word: We are pleased, so be pleased with us. And He returns to them in His speech to them: O people of Paradise, had I not been pleased with you I would not have housed you in My Paradise; this is the Day of Increase, so ask Me. So they agree upon one word: Show us Your face that we may look at it. He said: So Allah, blessed and exalted, will remove the veils and manifest Himself to them; His light will cover them - were Allah not to have decreed they shall not die, they would burn. Then it will be said to them: Return to your dwellings. So they will return, hidden from their wives and their wives hidden from them by His light that covered them; the light will keep settling until they return to their state - or to their dwellings they were in - and their wives will say to them: You left us in one form and returned to us in another? They will say: Our Lord manifested Himself to us, and we looked at what made us hidden from you. He said: So they will turn about in the musk of Paradise and its bliss every seven days, and that is the Day of Increase. And this hadith, we know it is narrated from Hudhayfah only by this route; we know none narrated it from al-A'mash except al-Qasim ibn Mutayyab, and none narrated it except Yahya ibn Kathir from Ibrahim ibn al-Mubarak. I heard Ahmad ibn Amr ibn Ubaydah say: I mentioned it to Ali ibn al-Madini, and he said to me: This is a strange hadith, I never heard it; and Ibrahim ibn al-Mubarak, he said to me, is known among the family of Abu Salabah, a famous people in Basra; it is narrated about Friday from Anas, Abd Allah ibn Amr, Hudhayfah and Samurah."
"2885","2882 - Ibrahim ibn Hani narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Yazid ibn Sinan informed us, he said: Yazid ibn Sinan, meaning his father, informed us, he said: Sulayman al-A'mash informed us, from Shaqiq, from Hudhayfah, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Allah is about to fill your hands with the non-Arabs, making them lions who do not flee; they will strike your necks and consume your spoils. And this speech, we know it is narrated from Hudhayfah only with this chain; we know none narrated it from al-A'mash except Yazid ibn Sinan."
"2886","2883 - al-Fadl ibn Sahl narrated to us, he said: al-Aswad ibn Amir informed us, he said: Sharik informed us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Wa'il, from Hudhayfah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood among us in a station and informed us of what will be until the Day of Resurrection."
"2887","2884 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna and Isma'il ibn Hafs narrated to us, both said: Muhammad ibn Ja'far informed us, he said: Shu'bah informed us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-A'mash, from Abu Wa'il, from Hudhayfah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The safeguarded among Muhammad's (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) Companions knew that Ibn Mas'ud is the nearest of them to Allah in means. And Abu Ishaq narrated from al-A'mash only this hadith."
"2888","2885 - Abd al-Wahid ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Muslim informed us, he said: al-A'mash informed us, from Abu Wa'il, from Hudhayfah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: Umar was called to a funeral, so he went out in it - or intending it - and I clung to him and said: Sit, O Commander of the Faithful, for he is of those. He said: I adjure you by Allah - am I of them? He said: No, and I will not clear anyone after you."
"2889","2886 - Muhammad ibn Mansur al-Tusi narrated to us, he said: al-Aswad ibn Amir informed us, he said: Sharik informed us, from al-A'mash, and Asim, and Husayn, from Abu Wa'il, from Hudhayfah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) rose at night, he would rub his mouth with the tooth-stick."
"2890","2887 - al-Fadl ibn Sahl narrated to us, he said: al-Aswad ibn Amir informed us, he said: Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash informed us, he said: Asim informed us, from Abu Wa'il, from Hudhayfah ibn al-Yaman, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: While I was walking with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a road of Medina, I heard him say: I am Muhammad, and Ahmad, and the Prophet of mercy, and the Gatherer, the Last in succession, and the Prophet of battles."
"2891","2888 - Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Karamah narrated to us, he said: Ubayd Allah ibn Musa informed us, he said: Isra'il informed us, from Asim, from Shaqiq, from Hudhayfah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Before the Hour are liars. And this hadith, we know it is narrated from Hudhayfah with this wording only with this chain; we know none narrated it except Ubayd Allah from Isra'il."
"2892","2889 - Muhammad ibn Ma'mar and Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Quta'i narrated to us, both said: Muhammad ibn Bakr al-Bursani informed us, he said: Imran al-Qattan informed us, from Asim, meaning Ibn Bahdalah, from Abu Wa'il: that Shabath ibn Rib'i prayed beside Hudhayfah and spat before him, so Hudhayfah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade this and said to me: When a man stands in prayer, Allah turns His face to him, so let him not turn away from Him until he turns away or breaks purity. And this hadith, we know none narrated it from Asim from Abu Wa'il raised except Imran al-Qattan; others narrated it halted."
"2893","2890 - Muhammad ibn Musa al-Qattan al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Harun informed us, he said: Sharik informed us, from Asim, from Abu Wa'il, from Hudhayfah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to a refuse heap of a people, urinated standing, performed ablution, and wiped over his leather socks. And this hadith, the companions of Asim narrate it from Asim from Abu Wa'il from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah."
"2894","2891 - And Fadalhah ibn al-Fadl al-Attar al-Kufi informed us of it, he said: Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash informed us, from Asim, from Abu Wa'il, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) likewise."
"2895","2892 - Muhammad ibn Musa al-Qattan narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Harun informed us, he said: Sharik informed us, from Asim, from Abu Wa'il, from Hudhayfah."
"2896","2893 - And Muhammad ibn Marzuq informed us of it, he said: Musa ibn Isma'il informed us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah informed us, from Asim, from Abu Wa'il, from Hudhayfah, he said: We were with Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, and he said: Which of you remembers the Messenger of Allah's (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) hadith about trial? I said: I do. He said: Give, may Allah bereave you of your father - how? I said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: A man's trial in himself, his family, his wealth and his child is expiated by fasting, prayer, charity, commanding good and forbidding evil. Umar said: That is not what I mean; I mean that which surges like the sea's waves. He said: There is no harm for you in it, O Commander of the Faithful; between you and it is a locked door. He said: Will that door be broken or opened? I said: Rather broken. He said: If broken, it will never be locked. And I narrated to him a hadith without exaggerations."
"2897","Husayn from Abu Wa'il from Hudhayfah. 2894 - al-Hasan ibn Qaza'ah narrated to us, he said: Husayn ibn Numayr informed us, from Husayn, meaning Ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Wa'il, from Hudhayfah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) rose at night, he would rub his mouth with the tooth-stick."
"2898","Abu al-Yaqzan from Abu Wa'il from Hudhayfah. 2895 - Abd Allah ibn Waddah al-Kufi narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn al-Yaman informed us, he said: Sharik informed us, from Abu al-Yaqzan, from Abu Wa'il, from Hudhayfah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: They said: O Messenger of Allah, will you not appoint a successor over us? He said: If I appoint a successor over you and you disobey my successor, punishment will descend upon you. They said: Will you not appoint Abu Bakr? He said: If you appoint him, you will find him weak in body, strong in Allah's cause. They said: Will you not appoint Umar? He said: If you appoint him, you will find him strong in body, strong in Allah's cause. They said: Will you not appoint Ali? He said: If you appoint him - and you will not - he will lead you upon the path, and you will find him guiding, guided. And this hadith, we know it is narrated from Hudhayfah only with this chain; Abu al-Yaqzan's name is Uthman ibn Umayr."
"2899","Wasil from Abu Wa'il from Hudhayfah. 2896 - Fitr ibn Hammad ibn Waqid narrated to us, he said: Mahdi ibn Maymun informed us, he said: Wasil informed us, from Abu Wa'il, from Hudhayfah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) met me while I was in major impurity and wanted to shake my hand, so I said: I am in major impurity. He said: The believer never becomes impure."
"2900","2897 - Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Adam informed us, he said: Mis'ar informed us, from Wasil, from Abu Wa'il, from Hudhayfah, likewise. And this hadith, more than one narrated it from Wasil from Abu Wa'il from Hudhayfah; we sufficed with those we named."
"2901","2898 - Fitr ibn Hammad narrated to us: Mahdi ibn Maymun informed us, from Wasil, from Abu Wail, from Hudhayfa (may Allah be pleased with him), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: ""No tale-bearer (nammam) will enter Paradise."" And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Abu Wail except Wasil, nor from Wasil except Mahdi; it is only known from the hadith of Ibrahim, from Hammam, from Hudhayfa."
"2902","2899 - Al-Fadl ibn Sahl narrated to us: Abu al-Nadr informed us: Mahdi ibn Maymun informed us, from Wasil, from Abu Wail, from Hudhayfa (may Allah be pleased with him): that he saw a man praying without properly establishing his bowing and prostration, so he said: ""For how long have you been praying this prayer?"" He said: For such-and-such long. He said: ""If you had died, you would have died upon other than the sunna of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."" And this hadith is only known from the hadith of al-Amash and Talha ibn Musarrif, from Zayd ibn Wahb, from Hudhayfa; and we do not know anyone who narrated it from Abu Wail, from Hudhayfa, except Wasil, and he is Wasil al-Ahdab, and he is trustworthy (thiqa). And there are three men named Wasil: Wasil al-Ahdab, from whom Shuba, al-Thawri, Misar, Mahdi ibn Maymun and others narrated, and he is a Kufan; and Wasil, the freed slave of Abu Uyayna, a Basran, from whom Hammad ibn Zayd, Mahdi ibn Maymun and others narrated, and he is not strong, though his hadith has been tolerated; and Wasil ibn al-Saib, who came upon them to Kufa and narrated from Ata and from Abu Sawra, the nephew of Abu Ayyub, hadiths in which he was not followed, and he is lenient (in hadith)."
"2903","2900 - Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us: Awn ibn Sallam informed us: Yahya ibn Salama ibn Kuhayl informed us, from his father, from Asim, from Abu Wail, from Hudhayfa (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: I said: O Abu Abd Allah, is hypocrisy today more, or was it in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: ""So he struck his forehead with his hand"" and said: ""Oh! Today it is open; they used to conceal it in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."" And we do not know that Salama ibn Kuhayl narrated, ascribed (marfu/musnad) from Asim, except this hadith."
"2904","Al-Hasan ibn Amr from Abu Wail from Hudhayfa 2901 - Ahmad ibn Dawud al-Kufi narrated to us: Amr ibn Abd al-Ghaffar informed us: al-Amash and al-Hasan ibn Amr informed us, from Abu Wail, from Hudhayfa (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: ""The hypocrites today, those among you, are worse than the hypocrites who were in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."" So we said: And how is that? He said: ""Those concealed their hypocrisy, while these declare it openly."" And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from al-Hasan ibn Amr except Amr ibn Abd al-Ghaffar."
"2905","Muslim al-Mulai from Abu Wail from Hudhayfa 2902 - Ubayd Allah ibn Yusuf narrated to us: Ali ibn Abis informed us: al-Amash and Muslim al-Mulai informed us, from Abu Wail, from Hudhayfa (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: ""The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade wearing silk and dibaj, and that we drink in vessels of gold and silver, and he said: 'They are for them in this world, and for you in the Hereafter.'"" And we do not know that Muslim narrated, from Abu Wail, from Hudhayfa, except this hadith."
"2906","Hakim ibn Jubayr from Abu Wail 2903 - Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Kufi narrated to us: Ali ibn Hakim informed us: Abd Allah ibn Bukayr informed us, from Hakim ibn Jubayr, from Abu Wail, who said: I was with Hudhayfa (may Allah be pleased with him) when Abd Allah ibn Masud and Abu Musa passed by, so he said: The one who most resembles the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), from the time he leaves his house until he returns to his family, is Abd Allah ibn Masud."
"2907","Zirr ibn Hubaysh from Hudhayfa; Adi ibn Thabit from Zirr 2904 - Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us: Jarir ibn Abd al-Hamid informed us, from al-Shaybani, from Adi ibn Thabit, from Zirr, from Hudhayfa (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""When one of you spits in the mosque, let him not spit to his right, but to his left or under his foot."""
"2908","2905 - Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us: Jarir informed us, from al-Shaybani, from Adi ibn Thabit, from Zirr ibn Hubaysh, from Hudhayfa (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever eats of this foul tree or foul vegetable, let him not come near our mosque."" And these two hadiths, we do not know them narrated from Hudhayfa except with this chain; and we do not know anyone who ascribed them from al-Shaybani except Jarir, while others besides Jarir narrated them as stopped (mawquf)."
"2909","2906 - Salama ibn Shabib narrated to us: Abd Allah ibn Jafar al-Raqqi informed us: Ubayd Allah ibn Amr informed us, from Zayd ibn Abi Unaysa, from Adi ibn Thabit, from Zirr, from Hudhayfa (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said on the Day of al-Ahzab: ""They diverted us from the middle prayer; may Allah fill their houses and graves with fire"" - meaning the Asr prayer. And this hadith was narrated by Asim, from Zirr, from Ali (may Allah be pleased with him), while Adi said: from Zirr, from Hudhayfa."
"2910","2907 - Al-Fadl ibn Sahl narrated to us: Abd al-Salam ibn Salih informed us: Talid ibn Sulayman informed us, from Abu al-Jahhaf, from Adi ibn Thabit, from Zirr ibn Hubaysh, from Hudhayfa (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: ""The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) met, on the night of al-Aqaba (at al-Aqaba), several men"" - meaning at al-Aqaba - ""he named them."" And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Adi, from Zirr, from Hudhayfa, except Abu al-Jahhaf."
"2911","Asim from Zirr from Hudhayfa 2908 - Hudba ibn Khalid narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salama informed us, from Asim, from Zirr, from Hudhayfa (may Allah be pleased with him): that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) met Jibril at the stones of al-Murri, and he said: ""I have been sent to an unlettered nation, and to one who has never read a book at all,"" so Jibril said: ""Allah commands you to recite the Quran upon one harf."" So Mikail said: ""Ask for more."" So he said: ""Recite upon two ahruf."" So Mikail said: ""Ask for more"" - until it reached seven ahruf. And this hadith was narrated by Abu Awana and Shayban, from Asim, from Zirr, from Ubayy ibn Kab, while Hammad ibn Salama said: from Asim, from Zirr, from Hudhayfa."
"2912","2909 - Khalid ibn Yusuf informed us of the hadith of Abu Awana: Abu Awana informed us, from Asim, from Zirr, from Ubayy ibn Kab, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with something like the hadith of Hudhayfa."
"2913","2910 - Ishaq ibn Sulayman al-Baghdadi, known as al-Tusi, narrated to us: Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash informed us, from Asim, from Zirr, from Hudhayfa (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: ""I took suhur with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then I went out for the Fajr prayer."" And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from Hudhayfa except with this chain."
"2914","2911 - Abd al-Warith ibn Abd al-Samad narrated to us: my father informed us: Hammad ibn Salama informed us, from Asim - meaning Ibn Bahdala - from Zirr, from Hudhayfa (may Allah be pleased with him): that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""What is between the two sides of my Hawd is what is between Ayla and Mudar, or more; its vessels are as many as - or like the number of - the stars of the sky, sweeter than honey, whiter in whiteness than milk, and more fragrant than the scent of musk; whoever drinks a drink from it will never thirst after it, ever."" And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from Hudhayfa except with this chain."
"2915","2912 - Ibrahim narrated to us: Ubayd Allah ibn Musa informed us: Israil informed us, from Asim, from Zirr, from Hudhayfa (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""I am Muhammad, and Ahmad, and I am al-Muqaffi, and al-Muhshir, and the Prophet of repentance."" And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from Hudhayfa except from the hadith of Asim; so Israil and Hammad ibn Salama narrated it, from Asim, from Zirr, from Hudhayfa, while Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated it, from Asim, from Abu Wail, from Hudhayfa. And this disagreement only came from the confusion of Asim, because he was not retentive."
"2916","2913 - Al-Hasan ibn Arafa narrated to us: Mubarak ibn Said informed us, from Mutarrif - meaning Ibn Tarif - from Asim - meaning Ibn Abi al-Nujud - from Zirr, from Hudhayfa (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: Umar said to us: Which of you narrates to us about the fitna as he heard it from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? So Hudhayfa said: I said: I. He said: ""Bring it, for you are indeed bold."" I said: O Commander of the Believers, the fitna of a man in his family, his wealth and his neighbor is expiated by fasting, prayer and charity. He said: ""It is not about this that I asked; rather I asked about that which surges as the sea surges."" He said: O Commander of the Believers, between you and it is a closed door. He said: ""Will it be broken or opened?"" I said: No, rather it will be broken. He said: ""That is more deserving of never being closed."" He said: I said to Hudhayfa: ""Does he know who the closed door is?"" He said: ""Yes, by Allah, he indeed knows, as one of you knows that before tomorrow is tonight."" I narrated to him a hadith that is not with obscurities. And this hadith was narrated by a group from Asim, from Abu Wail, from Hudhayfa; and we do not know anyone who narrated it from Asim, from Zirr, from Hudhayfa, except Mutarrif, nor anyone who narrated it from Mutarrif except Mubarak ibn Said, and we heard it only from al-Hasan ibn Arafa from him, and it was only with him; and Mutarrif did not ascribe from Asim except this hadith."
"2917","2914 - Ibrahim ibn Hani, Abd Allah ibn Abi Thumama al-Ansari, and Muhammad ibn Umar ibn Hayyaj narrated to us, saying: Qudama ibn Zaida ibn Qudama informed us: my father narrated to me, from Asim, from Zirr, from Hudhayfa (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood and called the people, saying: ""Come to me."" So they came to him and sat, and he said: ""This is the messenger of the Lord of the worlds, Jibril; he breathed into my heart that no soul will die until it completes its provision, even if it is delayed for it. So fear Allah and seek gracefully, and let not the delay of provision carry you to take it through disobedience of Allah, for what is with Allah is not attained except through obeying Him."" And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from Hudhayfa except from this way, with this chain."
"2918","2915 - Ahmad ibn Ishaq al-Ahwazi narrated to us: Abu Ahmad informed us: Shayban informed us, from Asim, from Zirr, who said: Hudhayfa (may Allah be pleased with him) said: Did the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) not pray in Bayt al-Maqdis? So I said: Yes indeed. So Hudhayfa said: What is your name? I said: Zirr. So Hudhayfa said: Recite {Glory to He who took His servant by night from al-Masjid al-Haram to al-Masjid al-Aqsa} the verse; do you find that he prayed? Had he prayed in it, prayer in it would have been prescribed upon you as tawaf of the House was prescribed upon you. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought a beast, long-backed and extended, called al-Buraq; its stride is as far as the sight reaches. He said: ""So we did not leave its back - I and Jibril, upon them both be peace - meaning the back of the beast, or the back of al-Buraq - until we saw Paradise and Hell."""
"2919","Yazid al-Taymi - and he is Ibn Sharik - from Hudhayfa 2916 - Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us: Jarir informed us, from al-Amash, from Ibrahim al-Taymi, from his father, from Hudhayfa (may Allah be pleased with him): that the people dispersed from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the night of al-Ahzab, and none remained with him but a few men, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to me while I was asleep and said: ""Go to the camp of al-Ahzab and see."" So I said: O Messenger of Allah, by He who sent you with the truth, I only rose to you out of shyness from the cold - or he said: from the severity of the cold. So he said: ""Go."" So I went until I came to their camp, and I found Abu Sufyan kindling a fire, warming his back, among a group around him, while al-Ahzab had dispersed from him. So I came until I sat among them, and Abu Sufyan sensed that one not of them had entered among them, so he said: Let each man of you take the hand of his companion. So I struck with my hand upon the one on my right and took his hand, then I struck with my hand upon the one on my left and took his hand. So I remained a little while, then I stood and came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was praying, so he gestured to me to draw near; so I drew near him until he sent to me of the garment that was upon him to warm me. When he finished his prayer he said: O son of al-Yaman, sit; what is the news of the people? So I said: O Messenger of Allah, the people dispersed from Abu Sufyan, and none remained but a group kindling a fire, and Allah poured upon them of the cold like that which He poured upon us. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cast his garment upon me, and I slept. Then he said: ""Rise, O sleepy one (Nawman)."""
"2920","2917 - Ishaq ibn Shahin al-Wasiti informed us: Khalid ibn Abd Allah informed us, from Abu Sad - meaning Said ibn al-Marzuban - from Ibrahim al-Taymi, from his father, from Hudhayfa, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with something like it or close to it. And these words, we do not know anyone who narrated them except Hudhayfa, and it has been narrated from Hudhayfa from another way; as for the hadith of Abu Sad, we do not know anyone who narrated it except Khalid and Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash."
"2921","Simak ibn Hudhayfa from Hudhayfa 2918 - Al-Hasan ibn Ali ibn Affan al-Kufi narrated to us: al-Hasan ibn Atiyya informed us: Qatari - meaning al-Khashshab - informed us: Simak ibn Hudhayfa ibn al-Yaman informed us, from his father Hudhayfa (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: I was riding behind the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: ""O Hudhayfa, do you know what is the right of Allah upon the servants?"" I said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: ""That they worship Him and associate nothing with Him."" Then he traveled on and said: ""O Hudhayfa."" I said: At your service, O Messenger of Allah. He said: ""Do you know what is the right of the servants upon Allah, blessed and exalted, when they do that?"" I said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: ""That He forgive them."""
"2922","2919 - Al-Hasan ibn Affan narrated to us: al-Hasan ibn Atiyya informed us: Qatari informed us, from Simak ibn Hudhayfa, from Hudhayfa (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while al-Abbas was sitting on his right and Fatima (may Allah be pleased with her) on his left, and he said: O Fatima, daughter of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), do good for Allah, for I will not avail you anything from Allah on the Day of Resurrection - he said: meaning that three times - then he said: ""O Abbas ibn Abd al-Muttalib, O uncle of the Messenger of Allah, do good for Allah, for I will not avail you on the Day of Resurrection anything from Allah"" - he said it three times - then he said: O Hudhayfa, draw near. So I drew near. Then he said: ""O Hudhayfa, whoever testifies that there is no god but Allah and that I am the Messenger of Allah"" - and I think he said: ""and believes in what I have come with, except that Allah has forbidden the Fire upon him and Paradise has become obligatory for him; and whoever fasts Ramadan seeking the face of Allah and the abode of the Hereafter, Allah seals it for him and forbids the Fire upon him; and whoever gives charity seeking thereby the face of Allah, blessed and exalted, and the abode of the Hereafter; and whoever performs hajj to the House of Allah, blessed and exalted, seeking the face of Allah, blessed and exalted, and the abode of the Hereafter - Allah seals it with it and forbids the Fire upon him, and Paradise becomes obligatory for him."" I said: O Messenger of Allah, shall I keep this secret or proclaim it? He said: ""Proclaim it."" And these two hadiths, we do not know them narrated from Hudhayfa except with this chain; and we do not know Hudhayfa to have a son called Simak except in this hadith."
"2923","Sila ibn Zufar from Hudhayfa; al-Shabi from Sila 2920 - Ziyad ibn Ayyub narrated to us: Hushaym informed us, from Mujalid, from al-Shabi, from Sila ibn Zufar: that Hudhayfa said: ""Accustom yourselves to patience, for tribulation is about to descend upon you, yet no tribulation will strike you more severe than what struck us with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."" And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Mujalid with this chain, connected, except Hushaym."
"2924","2921 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us: Hafs ibn Ghiyath informed us, from Ibn Abi Layla, from al-Shabi, from Sila, from Hudhayfa (may Allah be pleased with him): that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say in his bowing: ""Glory to my Lord, the Mighty, and with His praise, three times; and in his prostration: Glory to my Lord, the Most High, and with His praise, three times."" And this hadith was narrated by Hafs, who said in it at one time ""and with His praise, three times,"" and omitted at one time ""and with His praise""; and I think it came from the poor memory of Ibn Abi Layla. Al-Mustawrid narrated it from Sila, from Hudhayfa, and he did not say: ""and with His praise."""
"2925","2922 - Ibrahim ibn Said al-Jawhari narrated to us: Abu Usama informed us, from Mujalid, from al-Shabi, from Sila, from Hudhayfa (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: I said: ""How did you recognize the hypocrites?"" He said: I was with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) one night, and he named them."
"2926","Habib ibn Abi Thabit from Sila from Hudhayfa 2923 - Ahmad ibn Yahya and Salih ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Said al-Qattan narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Imran ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Layla informed us: my father narrated to me, from his father, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Sila, from Hudhayfa (may Allah be pleased with him): that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say in his bowing: ""Glory to my Lord, the Mighty, three times; and in his prostration: Glory to my Lord, the Most High, three times."""
"2927","2924 - Ahmad ibn Yahya and Salih ibn Muhammad narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Imran informed us: my father narrated to me, from his father, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Sila, from Hudhayfa (may Allah be pleased with him): that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed at the eclipse of the sun; so he stood and said takbir, then recited, then bowed as he had recited, then rose as he had bowed, then bowed as he had recited, then rose as he had bowed; so he did that four bowings before prostrating two prostrations, then he stood for the second (raka) and did the like of that, and he did not recite between the bowings. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from Hudhayfa except with this chain; and we do not know Habib narrated from Sila except these two hadiths."
"2928","Abu Ishaq from Sila from Hudhayfa 2925 - Abu Musa narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Jafar informed us: Shuba informed us, from Abu Ishaq, from Sila ibn Zufar, from Hudhayfa (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The people of Najran came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Send to us a trustworthy man. So he said: ""I shall surely send to you a truly trustworthy man."" So the people competed, and he sent Abu Ubayda ibn al-Jarrah (may Allah be pleased with him). And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from Hudhayfa except with this chain."
"2929","2926 - Abu Musa narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Jafar informed us: Shuba informed us, from Abu Ishaq, from Sila, from Hudhayfa (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: People will be gathered on one plain, and no soul will speak; so the first - I think he said - to speak will be Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he will say: ""At Your service, and blessed to serve You; good is in Your hands, and evil is not to You; guided is he whom You guide; Your servant is before You, by You and to You; there is no refuge nor escape from You except to You; blessed and exalted are You; glory to You, Lord of the House."" So this is His saying {That your Lord may raise you to a praised station}. And this hadith, thus Shuba narrated it, from Abu Ishaq, from Sila, from Hudhayfa; while others besides Shuba narrated it from Abu Ishaq, from other than Sila, from Hudhayfa."
"2930","2927 - Muhammad ibn Said ibn Yazid ibn Ibrahim al-Tustari narrated to us: Yaqub ibn Ishaq al-Hadrami informed us: Yazid ibn Ata informed us: Abu Ishaq informed us, from Sila, from Hudhayfa (may Allah be pleased with him), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: ""Islam is eight shares: Islam is a share, prayer is a share, zakat is a share, hajj to the House is a share, fasting is a share, enjoining good is a share, forbidding evil is a share, and jihad in the path of Allah is a share; and disappointed is he who has no share."""
"2931","2928 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna informed us: Muhammad ibn Jafar informed us: Shuba informed us, from Abu Ishaq, from Sila ibn Zufar, from Hudhayfa (may Allah be pleased with him): that he said: Islam is eight shares, then he mentioned the like of it but did not ascribe it (to the Prophet). And this hadith, we do not know anyone who ascribed it except Yazid ibn Ata, from Abu Ishaq."
"2932","2929 - Salama ibn Shabib narrated to us: Amr ibn Uthman informed us: Musa ibn Ayan informed us, from Layth, from Abu Ishaq, from Sila, from Hudhayfa (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Indeed, slandering a chaste woman demolishes the deeds of a hundred years."" And this hadith, we do not know anyone who ascribed it except Layth, nor from Layth except Musa ibn Ayan; and a group narrated it, from Abu Ishaq, from Sila, from Hudhayfa, stopped (mawquf)."
"2933","2930 - Muhammad ibn Mamar narrated to us: Rawh ibn Ubada informed us: Hammad ibn Salama informed us, from al-Hajjaj - meaning Ibn Artah - from Abu Ishaq, from Sila, from Hudhayfa (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The polytheists seized me and my father while we were heading to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day of Badr, and they said: Where are you heading? We said: To Medina. He said: You intend Muhammad. So they made us give the covenant of Allah and His pact that we would not fight with him and would turn back to Medina; so we gave them what they wanted and they let us go. Then we came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and informed him of the news, and he said: ""Fulfill for them their covenant, and we seek Allah's help against them."" So that is what prevented us from witnessing Badr. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Abu Ishaq, from Sila, from Hudhayfa, except al-Hajjaj."
"2934","2931 - Muhammad ibn Miskin narrated to us: Yahya ibn Hassan informed us: Hammad ibn Shuayb informed us, from Abu Ishaq, from Sila, from Hudhayfa (may Allah be pleased with him): that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say in his bowing: ""Glory to my Lord, the Mighty, three times; and in his prostration: Glory to my Lord, the Most High, three times."" And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Abu Ishaq, from Sila, from Hudhayfa, except Hammad ibn Shuayb."
"2935","2932 - Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad ibn Mamul narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Kathir al-Mulai informed us: Abu Sinan informed us, from Abu Ishaq, from Sila, from Hudhayfa (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: ""The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded us to inspect the eye and the ear (of sacrificial animals)."" And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from Sila, from Hudhayfa, except with this chain; and it is narrated from Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) from more than one way."
"2936","2933 - Mamar ibn Sahl narrated to us: Amir ibn Mudrik informed us: Muhammad ibn Ubayd Allah informed us, from Abu Ishaq, from Sila, from Hudhayfa (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever separates from the community by a handspan has separated from Islam."" And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Abu Ishaq, from Sila, from Hudhayfa, raised (marfu), except Muhammad ibn Ubayd Allah; and Muhammad ibn Ubayd Allah is lenient in hadith, though Shuba and others narrated from him."
"2937","The shaykhs from Sila from Hudhayfa 2934 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Jafar informed us: Shuba informed us, from Amr ibn Murra, from Abu Hamza, from a man of Abs, from Hudhayfa (may Allah be pleased with him): that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say between the two prostrations: ""O Allah, forgive me,"" repeating it many times. He said: And when he raised his head he would say: ""Glory to the Owner of dominion, might, pride and greatness."""
"2938","2935 - Nasr ibn Ali informed us: Yahya ibn Zakariyya ibn Abi Zaida informed us, from al-Ala ibn al-Musayyab, from Amr ibn Murra, from Talha ibn Yazid, from Hudhayfa, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with something like it. And al-Ala ibn al-Musayyab did not say in his hadith ""from a man of Banu Abs""; rather he left it unconnected (mursal), and the man of Banu Abs is thought to be Sila."
"2939","Said ibn al-Musayyab from Hudhayfa 2936 - Muhammad ibn Mamar narrated to us: Muslim ibn Ibrahim informed us: Hammad ibn Salama informed us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Said ibn al-Musayyab, from Hudhayfa (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: ""The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave me the choice between emigration (hijra) and support (nusra), so I chose emigration."" And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it except Hudhayfa from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); and we do not know for it any chain other than this chain, and we only preserve it from the hadith of Muslim, from Hammad."
"2940","Ata ibn Yasar from Hudhayfa 2937 - Ibrahim ibn Hani narrated to us: Ali ibn Abd al-Hamid informed us: Abu Mashar informed us, from Umar, freed slave of Ghufra, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Hudhayfa (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""For every nation there are Magians, and the Magians of this nation are those who say there is no decree (qadar); if they fall ill do not visit them, and if they die do not attend them; and they are the party (shia) of the Dajjal, and it is due upon Allah, blessed and exalted, to gather them with him."" And these words have been narrated from Hudhayfa from other than this way; and we do not know anyone who connected it and named the man between Umar ibn Abd Allah, freed slave of Ghufra, and Hudhayfa, except Abu Mashar; others besides Abu Mashar only narrate it from Umar, from a man, from Hudhayfa."
"2941","Al-Mustazill ibn Husayn from Hudhayfa 2938 - Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Kufi narrated to us: al-Hasan ibn al-Husayn informed us: Qays - meaning Ibn al-Rabi - informed us, from Shabib ibn Gharqada, from al-Mustazill ibn Husayn, from Hudhayfa (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""All of you are the children of Adam, and Adam was created from dust; a people who boast of their forefathers shall surely cease, or they shall be more insignificant to Allah than the dung beetle."" And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from Hudhayfa except from this way, with this chain."
"2942","Qays ibn Abi Hazim from Hudhayfa 2939 - Abda ibn Abd Allah al-Qasmali narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Bishr informed us: Ismail - meaning Ibn Abi Khalid - informed us, from Qays, from Hudhayfa (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: ""The people used to ask the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about good, while I used to ask him about evil."" And we do not know Ismail narrated, from Qays, from Hudhayfa, except this hadith."
"2943","Zayd ibn Yuthay from Hudhayfa 2940 - Ishaq ibn al-Dayf narrated to us: al-Nadr ibn Shumayl informed us: Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq informed us, from his father, from Zayd ibn Yuthay, from Hudhayfa (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Abu Bakr: ""If you saw with Umm Ruman a man, what would you do with him?"" He said: I would, by Allah, do evil with him. He said: ""And you, O Umar?"" He said: I would, by Allah, kill him; I would say: may Allah curse the most incapable, for he is wicked. He said: ""So there was revealed {And those who accuse their wives and have no witnesses but themselves}."" And this hadith, we do not know anyone who ascribed it except al-Nadr ibn Shumayl, from Yunus."
"2944","2941 - Abd Allah ibn Ishaq al-Attar informed us: Abu Asim informed us, from Sufyan, from Abu Ishaq, from Zayd ibn Yuthay - and he did not say from Hudhayfa - from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with something like it."
"2945","Amr ibn Shurahbil from Hudhayfa 2942 - Musa ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Masruqi narrated to us: Abu Yahya al-Himmani Abd al-Hamid ibn Abd al-Rahman informed us: al-Hasan ibn Abi al-Hasan al-Bajali informed us, from Talha ibn Musarrif, from Abu Ammar, from Amr ibn Shurahbil, from Hudhayfa (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Sheep are blessing, camels are honor for their people, horses have good in their forelocks until the Day of Resurrection; and your servant is your brother, so do good to him, and if you find him overpowered then help him."" And these words, we do not know them narrated from Hudhayfa except with this chain; and I think al-Hasan ibn Abi al-Hasan al-Bajali is al-Hasan ibn Umara."
"2946","Bilal ibn Yahya al-Absi from Hudhayfa 2943 - Ibrahim ibn Hani narrated to us: Ubayd Allah ibn Musa informed us: Yusuf ibn Suhayb informed us, from Musa ibn Abi al-Mukhtar, from Bilal ibn Yahya, from Hudhayfa (may Allah be pleased with him): that the people dispersed from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the night of al-Ahzab, and none remained with him but twelve men. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to me while I was crouching from sleep and said: O son of al-Yaman, rise and go to the camp of al-Ahzab and see their condition. I said: O Messenger of Allah, by He who sent you with the truth, I only rose to you out of shyness from the cold. He said: ""Go, O son of al-Yaman; no harm upon you from cold nor heat until you return to me."" So I went until I came to their camp, and I found Abu Sufyan kindling a fire among a group around him, while al-Ahzab had dispersed from him. So I came until I sat among them, and Abu Sufyan sensed that one not of them had entered among them, so he said: Let each man of you take the hand of his companion. He said: So I struck with my hand upon the one on my right and took his hand, then I struck my hand upon the one on my left and took his hand. He said: So I remained among them a little while, then I stood and came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was standing praying; so he gestured to me to draw near, so I drew near, then he gestured to me to draw near, so I drew near, until he sent upon me of the garment that was upon him to warm me. When he finished his prayer he said: ""O son of al-Yaman, sit; what is the news of the people?"" I said: O Messenger of Allah, the people dispersed from Abu Sufyan, and none remained but a group kindling a fire, and Allah, blessed and exalted, poured upon them of the cold like that which He poured upon us; but we hope from Allah what they do not hope. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from Bilal ibn Yahya, from Hudhayfa, except with this chain."
"2947","2944 - Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Kufi narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Ubayd informed us, from Yusuf ibn Suhayb, from Musa ibn Abi al-Mukhtar, from Bilal ibn Yahya, from Hudhayfa (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: No tents after tents that were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), warding off from them what they ward off from these tents; nor does a people intend them with evil except that Allah brings upon them what distracts them from them. Abu Bakr said: meaning Kufa. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from Bilal ibn Yahya, from Hudhayfa, except with this chain."
"2948","2945 - Ahmad ibn Yahya narrated to us: Ubayd Allah ibn Musa informed us: Sad ibn Aws informed us, from Bilal ibn Yahya, who said: When Uthman (may Allah be pleased with him) was killed, Hudhayfa came, and it was said: O Abu Abd Allah, this man has been killed and the people have differed, so what do you say? So he said: Prop me up. So they propped him against the chest of a man, and he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""Abu al-Yaqzan is upon the fitra; Abu al-Yaqzan is upon the fitra; he will not leave it until he dies or old age touches him."" And these words, we do not know them narrated from Hudhayfa except with this chain."
"2949","2946 - Ahmad ibn Yahya narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Maymun informed us: Said ibn Hakim informed us, from Muslim ibn Habib, from Bilal - meaning al-Absi - from Hudhayfa (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""How good is moderation in wealth, and how good is moderation in poverty, and how good is moderation in worship."" And this hadith, we do not know it narrated with this wording except from the hadith of Hudhayfa."
"2950","Abd Allah ibn Salama from Hudhayfa 2947 - Ibrahim ibn Ziyad al-Saigh narrated to us: Yahya ibn Adam informed us: Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash informed us, from al-Amash, from Amr ibn Murra, from Abd Allah ibn Salima, from Hudhayfa (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: I was with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the night of al-Aqaba, with Ammar leading him and I driving him, when mounts appeared aiming at the Messenger of Allah, so Ammar (may Allah be pleased with him) struck their faces; and there were masked men, twelve men. When they passed, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""What did the people intend?"" I said: They intended to make the mount of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) shy away. He said: ""Do you know them?"" I said: Yes. And these words and the like have been narrated from Hudhayfa from other than this way; and we do not know Abd Allah ibn Salama narrated from Hudhayfa an ascribed hadith other than this hadith."
"2951","Habba al-Urani from Hudhayfa 2948 - Ali ibn al-Mundhir narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Fudayl informed us: Muslim - meaning Ibn Abd Allah al-Awar - informed us, from Habba, who said: Hudhayfa and Abu Masud gathered, and one of them said to his companion: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The rebellious party (al-fia al-baghiya) will kill Ammar,"" and the other affirmed him. And these words, we do not know them narrated from Hudhayfa from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except from this way."
"2952","Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla from Hudhayfa 2949 - Muhammad ibn Mamar narrated to us: Wahb ibn Jarir informed us: my father informed us, from al-Amash, from Mujahid, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Hudhayfa (may Allah be pleased with him): that he asked a dihqan (village chief) for drink, so he brought him in a silver vessel, so he struck his face with it and said: Do you know why I did this with it? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade us to eat in gold and silver, and to wear silk and dibaj, for they are for them in this world and for us in the Hereafter. And this hadith was narrated by more than one from Mujahid, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Hudhayfa. So al-Amash, Ibn Awn and Ibn Abi Najih narrated it from Mujahid, from Abd al-Rahman; and it was narrated from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla from more than one way: al-Hakam, Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad and Abu Farwa narrated it."
"2953","2950 - As for the hadith of Ibn Awn: Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us from Ibn Abi Adi, from Ibn Awn, from Mujahid, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Hudhayfa, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"2954","2951 - As for the hadith of Ibn Abi Najih: Ibrahim ibn Said al-Jawhari narrated it to us: Sufyan informed us, from Ibn Abi Najih, from Mujahid, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Hudhayfa, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"2955","2952 - Ibrahim ibn Said said: And Sufyan ibn Uyayna informed us, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Hudhayfa, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): that he forbade drinking in vessels of gold and silver, and wearing silk and dibaj, and he said: ""They are for them in this world and for us in the Hereafter."" They are close in the wording of this hadith."
"2956","2953 - Muhammad ibn Umar ibn Hayyaj narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Ubayd informed us: Dawud ibn Yazid informed us, from al-Hakam, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade drinking in vessels of gold and silver."
"2957","Hammam ibn al-Harith from Hudhayfa 2954 - Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us: Jarir informed us, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from Hammam, from Hudhayfa (may Allah be pleased with him), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: ""No qattat will enter Paradise"" - meaning a tale-bearer (nammam). And this hadith was narrated by Mansur and al-Amash, from Ibrahim, from Hammam, from Hudhayfa."
"2958","2955 - Al-Fadl ibn Sahl narrated to us: Ubayd Allah ibn Musa informed us: Israil informed us, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from Hammam, from Hudhayfa (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) met me while I was junub, and he wanted to shake my hand, so I said: I am junub. So he said: ""The believer does not become impure."" And this hadith was narrated by more than one from the hadith of Mansur, from Ibrahim, from Hudhayfa; and we did not hear it from the hadith of Mansur, from Ibrahim, from Hammam, from Hudhayfa, except from al-Fadl ibn Sahl."
"2959","2956 - Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Hanan informed us: Baqiyya ibn al-Walid informed us: Ibrahim ibn Muhammad al-Fazari informed us: al-Amash informed us, from Ibrahim, from Hammam, from Hudhayfa (may Allah be pleased with him): that he passed by people in the mosque and said: O company of reciters (qurra), follow the path; for by Allah, if you follow it you have indeed preceded a far precedence, and if you take right and left you have indeed gone astray a far error."
"2960","Abu Mijlaz from Hudhayfa 2957 - Ahmad ibn Abda narrated to us: Yazid ibn Zuray informed us: Said - meaning Ibn Abi Aruba - informed us, from Qatada, from Abu Mijlaz: that Hudhayfa (may Allah be pleased with him) saw a man sitting in the middle of the circle, so he said: As for this, he is cursed upon the tongue of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - or he said: cursed upon the tongue of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) is whoever sits in the middle of the circle. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated except from Hudhayfa with this chain."
"2961","2958 - Ibrahim ibn Said al-Jawhari narrated to us: Abu Ahmad informed us, from Mandal - meaning Ibn Ali - from al-Amash, from al-Hakam, from Abu Mijlaz, from Hudhayfa (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) shook my hand while I was junub. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from al-Amash except Mandal; and we do not know al-Hakam ascribed, from Abu Mijlaz, from Hudhayfa, except this hadith."
"2962","Subay ibn Khalid from Hudhayfa 2959 - Abu Kamil narrated to us: Abu Awana informed us, from Qatada, from Nasr ibn Asim, from Subay ibn Khalid. 2960 - And Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna informed us of it: Yahya ibn Hammad and Abu al-Walid informed us, saying: Abu Awana informed us, from Qatada, from Nasr ibn Asim, from Subay ibn Khalid, who said: I went out to Kufa at the time Tustar was conquered, to bring mules from it; so I entered the mosque and there was a group of men, whom you would recognize when you saw them that they were men of Hijaz; among them was a man. I said: Who is this? He said: So the people gestured to me with their eyes and said: Do you not know this? This is Hudhayfa, the companion of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So he said: The people used to ask the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about good, and I used to ask him about evil. So I said: O Messenger of Allah, do you see this good that Allah has given us - will there be evil after it as there was before it? He said: ""Yes."" I said: O Messenger of Allah, then what is protection from that? He said: ""The sword."" I said: And is there any remainder for the sword? He said: ""Yes."" I said: Then what? He said: A truce upon smoke (dakhan), and a community upon division. So if there is on that day a caliph of Allah, blessed and exalted, who strikes your back and takes your wealth, then listen and obey; otherwise die while biting onto the root of a tree. He said: I said: Then what? He said: ""Then the Dajjal will emerge, with him a river and a fire; so whoever falls into his fire, his reward becomes obligatory and his burden is removed; and whoever falls into his river, his burden becomes obligatory and his reward is removed."" He said: I said: Then what? He said: ""Then it is the establishment of the Hour."" And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Qatada more complete than Abu Awana."
"2963","2961 - Ibrahim ibn al-Mustamirr narrated to us: Said ibn Amir informed us: Abu Amir al-Khazzaz informed us, from Humayd ibn Hilal, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Qurt, from Hudhayfa - or from a man, from Hudhayfa - with something like it."
"2964","Abu Idris from Hudhayfa 2962 - Ahmad ibn al-Miqdam narrated to us: al-Walid ibn Muslim informed us: Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid ibn Jabir informed us, from Busr ibn Ubayd Allah, from Abu Idris al-Khawlani, from Hudhayfa ibn al-Yaman (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The people used to ask the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about good, and I used to ask him about evil, fearing it would reach me. So I said: O Messenger of Allah, we were in ignorance and evil, then Allah, blessed and exalted, brought this good; so is there after this good any evil? He said: ""Yes: fitna and evil."" I said: Then is there after that evil any good? He said: ""Yes: a truce upon smoke."" I said: And what is its smoke? He said: ""You will be guided by other than guidance from them."" I said: Then is there after that good any evil? He said: ""Yes: callers at the gates of Hell; whoever answers them they cast him into it."" I said: O Messenger of Allah, describe them to us. He said: ""They speak with our tongues."" I said: O Messenger of Allah, then what do you command me if I reach it? - meaning that time. He said: ""Stick to the community of the people and their imam."" I said: Then if they have no community? He said: ""Then be patient, even if you bite onto a tree, until death reaches you while you are like that."""
"2965","Abu Ubayda ibn Hudhayfa from his father 2963 - Abu Musa narrated to us: Wahb ibn Jarir informed us: Hisham ibn Hassan informed us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Ubayda ibn Hudhayfa, from his father (may Allah be pleased with him), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: ""Whoever establishes in Islam a good sunna and it is acted upon after him, he will have its reward and the reward of whoever acts upon it, without decreasing anything from their rewards; and whoever establishes in Islam an evil sunna and it is acted upon after him, upon him is its burden and the burden of whoever acts, without decreasing anything from their burdens."""
"2966","2964 - Ayyub ibn Sulayman al-Baghdadi informed us: Ali ibn Asim informed us: Khalid al-Hadhdha and Hisham informed us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Ubayda ibn Hudhayfa, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with something like it. And this hadith was narrated by Abd al-Warith, from Ayyub, from Ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayra; and the hadith of Hudhayfa is more authentic than the hadith of Abu Hurayra."
"2967","2965 - Yusuf ibn Hammad al-Mani and Muhammad ibn Marzuq informed us, saying: Abd al-Ala ibn Abd al-Ala informed us: Hisham ibn Hassan informed us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Ubayda ibn Hudhayfa, from his father (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The verse of kalala was revealed to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was on one of his journeys. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stopped, and there was Hudhayfa, with the head of Hudhayfa's she-camel at the waist-wrapper (izar) of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); so he taught it to him. Then Hudhayfa looked and there was Umar ibn al-Khattab, so he taught it to him. When it was the caliphate of Umar (may Allah be pleased with him), Umar looked into kalala and called Hudhayfa and asked him about it. So Hudhayfa said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) indeed taught it to me, and I taught it to you as he taught me; and by Allah, I am indeed truthful, and by Allah, I will never add to you upon that anything, ever. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it except Hudhayfa; and we do not know for it a path from Hudhayfa except this path, nor anyone who narrated it from Hisham except Abd al-Ala."
"2968","2966 - Muhammad ibn Marzuq narrated to us: Abd al-Aziz ibn al-Khattab informed us: Ali ibn Ghurab informed us: Hisham ibn Hassan informed us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Ubayda ibn Hudhayfa, from his father (may Allah be pleased with him): that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever imitates a people is of them."" And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from Hudhayfa, ascribed, except from this way; and others besides Ali ibn Ghurab narrated it from Hisham, from Muhammad, from Abu Ubayda, from his father, stopped (mawquf)."
"2969","2967 - Muhammad ibn Mamar narrated to us: Wahb ibn Jarir informed us: Shuba informed us: Yazid Abu Khalid informed us, from Abu Ubayda ibn Hudhayfa, from his father (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever sells a house or real estate and does not place its price into its like, it will not be blessed for him in it"" - or as he said."
"2970","Thalaba ibn Zahdam from Hudhayfa 2968 - Amr ibn Ali narrated to us: Yahya ibn Said informed us: Sufyan informed us, from Ashath ibn Abi al-Shatha, from al-Aswad ibn Hilal, from Thalaba ibn Zahdam, who said: We were with Hudhayfa in Tabaristan, when Said ibn al-Asi said: ""Which of you prayed with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the prayer of fear?"" So Hudhayfa said: I. So he prayed with these a raka and with these a raka, and they did not make up - meaning none of the two groups made up - as if they sufficed with a raka each."
"2971","Mutarrif from Hudhayfa 2969 - Abbad ibn Yaqub narrated to us: Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Quddus informed us, from al-Amash, from Mutarrif, from Hudhayfa (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The excellence of knowledge is more beloved to me than the excellence of worship, and the best of your religion is piety (wara)."" And these words, we do not know them narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except from this way; rather these words are only known as the words of Mutarrif. And we do not know anyone who narrated it from al-Amash except Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Quddus, and we heard it only from Abbad ibn Yaqub."
"2972","Ubayd Abu al-Mughira from Hudhayfa 2970 - Nasr ibn Ali narrated to us: Abu Ahmad informed us: Israil informed us, from Abu Ishaq, from Ubayd Abi al-Mughira, from Hudhayfa (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: There was in my tongue sharpness against my family, and it would not go beyond them to others; so I mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: ""Where are you with regard to seeking forgiveness? I seek Allah's forgiveness, blessed and exalted, a hundred times a day."" He said: So I mentioned that to Abu Burda, and he narrated to me from Abu Musa, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with something like it. And this hadith was narrated by a group from Abu Ishaq, from Ubayd, from Hudhayfa."
"2973","2971 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Jafar informed us: Shuba informed us: I heard Abu Ishaq say: I heard al-Walid Abu al-Mughira - or al-Mughira Abu al-Walid - narrating that Hudhayfa said: O Messenger of Allah, I am sharp of tongue, and most of that is against my family. So he said: ""Where are you with regard to seeking forgiveness? I seek Allah's forgiveness, blessed and exalted, a hundred times a day."""
"2974","2972 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us: Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi informed us: Sufyan informed us, from Abu Ishaq, from Ubayd Abi al-Mughira, from Hudhayfa; and he mentioned from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) something like it."
"2975","Muslim ibn Nadhir from Hudhayfa 2973 - Muhammad ibn Musa al-Harashi narrated to us: Ziyad ibn Abd Allah informed us, from al-Amash, from Abu Ishaq, from Muslim ibn Nudhayr, from Hudhayfa, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"2976","2974 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna informed us: Muhammad ibn Jafar informed us: Shuba informed us, from Abu Ishaq, from Muslim ibn Nudhayr, from Hudhayfa - and the wording is the wording of Shuba - who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took hold of the muscle of my leg - or his leg - and said: ""The right place of the izar is here; if you refuse, then here; if you refuse, then the izar has no right in the ankles"" - or ""the ankles have no right in the izar."" And this hadith was narrated by more than one from Abu Ishaq, from Muslim, from Hudhayfa; so we sufficed with those we named."
"2977","2975 - Abu al-Hasan Muhammad ibn Ayyub al-Raqqi informed us: Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Amr ibn Abd al-Khaliq al-Bazzar informed us, dictating: Muhammad ibn Mamar informed us: Abu Asim informed us, from Ibn Jurayj: Abu al-Zubayr informed me that he heard Jabir ibn Abd Allah (may Allah be pleased with him) say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""I am your forerunner (farat) before you; if you do not find me, then I am at the Hawd; and the Hawd is what is between Ayla to Mecca; and there shall come peoples, men and women, with vessels, then they shall not taste anything of it."" And this hadith is only known from the hadith of al-Hajjaj ibn Muhammad, from Ibn Jurayj, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir."
"2978","Musnad of Abu Musa (may Allah be pleased with him); first hadith of Abu Musa 2976 - Muhammad ibn Ismail ibn Samura narrated to us: Asbat ibn Muhammad informed us, from Mutarrif, from Amir, from Abu Burda, from Abu Musa (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever had a slave girl and raised her and did good to her, then freed her and married her, he has two rewards."""
"2979","2977 - Al-Muammal ibn Hisham narrated to us: Ismail ibn Ibrahim informed us: Mamar informed us, from Firas, from al-Shabi, from Abu Burda, from Abu Musa (may Allah be pleased with him): that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Any man who had a slave girl and disciplined her, doing well in her discipline, and taught her, doing well in her teaching, then freed her and married her, he has two rewards; and any slave who fulfills the right of Allah upon him and the right of his masters, he has two rewards; and any man of the People of the Book who believed in his prophet, then became Muslim and believed in Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he has two rewards."""
"2980","2978 - Yahya ibn Hakim informed us of it: Musa ibn Masud informed us: Sufyan informed us, from Salih ibn Salih, from al-Shabi, from Abu Burda, from Abu Musa, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with something like it. And these words, we do not know anyone who narrated them from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with this wording except Abu Musa al-Ashari."
"2981","2979 - Fadala ibn al-Fadl al-Kufi narrated to us: Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash informed us, from Abu Husayn, from Abu Burda, from Abu Musa (may Allah be pleased with him), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: ""Any man who had a slave girl with him and disciplined her, doing well in her discipline, and taught her, then freed her and married her, he has two rewards."""
"2982","2980 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us: Abd al-Ala informed us, from Dawud - meaning Ibn Abi Hind - from Abu Nadra, from Abu Said al-Khudri, who said: ""Abu Musa sought permission from Umar three times, but he did not permit him, so he left. Then Umar met him and said: What turned you back? He said: I sought permission three times but was not permitted, so I returned; and I sought the permission that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded us: if we are permitted we enter, otherwise we return. So he said: You shall surely bring me proof for this, or I shall do to you (such-and-such). He said: So Abu Musa went until he came to the gathering of his people and informed them. So they said: None shall stand with you except the youngest of us; rise, O Abu Said. So he stood with him to Umar and informed him, so he let him go."""
"2983","2981 - Ahmad ibn Abda and Yahya ibn Hakim narrated to us; Ahmad said: Sufyan informed us, while Yahya said: Sufyan ibn Uyayna informed us, from Yazid ibn Khusayfa, from Busr ibn Said, from Abu Said al-Khudri, who said: Abu Musa al-Ashari came to us and said to us: Umar commanded me to bring him proof, because I came to him and sought permission three times but was not permitted, so I returned; and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever seeks permission three times and is not permitted, let him return."" So Umar said: You shall surely bring me proof for this, or I shall hurt you. So I came to you to stand with me. So Ubayy ibn Kab said: None shall stand with you except the youngest of the people. So I was the youngest of the people, and I stood with him."
"2984","2982 - Amr ibn Ali narrated to us: Yazid ibn Zuray informed us: Said - meaning Ibn Abi Aruba - informed us, from Qatada, from Anas, from Abu Musa al-Ashari, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"2985","2983 - Amr ibn Ali informed us of it: Yahya ibn Said informed us, from Shuba, from Qatada, from Anas, from Abu Musa, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"2986","2984 - Abu Kamil and Abd al-Wahid ibn Ghiyath informed us, saying: Abu Awana informed us, from Qatada, from Anas, from Abu Musa, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"2987","2985 - Amr ibn Ali informed us: Abu Dawud informed us: Hammam informed us, from Qatada, from Anas, from Abu Musa, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); and their wordings are close. He said: ""The example of the believer who recites the Quran is like the citron: sweet its scent, sweet its taste. And the example of the believer who does not recite the Quran is like a fruit: sweet its taste, with no scent. And the example of the hypocrite - and Said said in his hadith: the example of the wicked (fajir) - who recites the Quran is like basil: sweet its scent, bitter its taste. And the example of the hypocrite - and Said said: the wicked - who does not recite the Quran is like colocynth: vile its taste, vile its scent."""
"2988","2986 - Al-Fadl ibn Sahl narrated to us: Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr informed us: Abu Bakr al-Nahshali informed us, from Ziyad ibn Ilaqa, from Qutba ibn Malik, from Abu Musa (may Allah be pleased with him), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: ""The perishing of my nation is by stabbing (tan) and plague (taun)."" They said: O Messenger of Allah, we know stabbing; so what is plague? He said: ""The piercing of your enemies from the jinn; and in each is martyrdom."" Thus Abu Bakr al-Nahshali narrated it from Ziyad, from Qutba, from Abu Musa; while Shuba differed from him in its chain. Abu Bakr said:"
"2989","2987 - So Yahya ibn Hakim narrated to us: Abd al-Rahman ibn Uthman Abu Bahr al-Bakrawi informed us: Shuba informed us, from Ziyad ibn Ilaqa: a man of my people informed me: I heard Abu Musa narrating from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with something like it. Abu Bakr said: And this hadith was narrated by al-Hajjaj ibn Artah, from Ziyad ibn Ilaqa, differing from Shuba and differing from Abu Bakr al-Nahshali."
"2990","2988 - Yahya ibn Habib ibn Arabi narrated to us: al-Mutamir ibn Sulayman informed us: al-Hajjaj ibn Artah informed us, from Ziyad ibn Ilaqa, from Kurdus, from Abu Musa (may Allah be pleased with him), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: ""The perishing of my nation is by stabbing and plague."" They said: O Messenger of Allah, we know stabbing; so what is plague? He said: ""The piercing of your enemies from the jinn; and in each is martyrdom."" Thus al-Hajjaj narrated it from Ziyad; while Saad ibn Sulayman narrated it from Ziyad ibn Ilaqa, differing from the group in its chain."
"2991","2989 - Ahmad ibn Amr ibn Ubayda al-Usfuri narrated to us: Sahl ibn Hammad Abu Attab informed us: Saad ibn Sulayman informed us, from Ziyad ibn Ilaqa, from Yazid ibn al-Harith, from Abu Musa, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with something like it."
"2992","2990 - Ahmad ibn Abda narrated to us: Hammad ibn Zayd informed us, from Asim - meaning Ibn Sulayman - from Abu Uthman al-Nahdi, from Abu Musa al-Ashari (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a raid, and we raised our voices. So he drew near us and said: O people, be gentle with yourselves; for you do not call upon one deaf nor absent. You only call upon One All-Hearing, All-Seeing; and He whom you call is nearer to one of you than the neck of his mount. Then he said: O Abd Allah ibn Qays, shall I not teach you a word that is of the treasures of Paradise: there is no power nor strength except with Allah. And this hadith was narrated from Abu Uthman, from Abu Musa, by Sulayman al-Taymi, Khalid al-Hadhdha, Uthman ibn Ghiyath and Abu Tamima."
"2993","As for the hadith of Sulayman al-Taymi: Yahya ibn Hakim narrated it to us 2991 - saying: Yahya ibn Said informed us, from Sulayman al-Taymi, from Abu Uthman al-Nahdi, from Abu Musa, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"2994","2992 - And Yahya ibn Hakim informed us of it: Abd al-Wahhab informed us: Khalid al-Hadhdha informed us, from Abu Uthman, from Abu Musa, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"2995","2993 - And Muammal ibn Hisham informed us: Ismail ibn Ibrahim informed us, from al-Jurayri, from Abu Tamima, from Abu Uthman, from Abu Musa. Abu Bakr said: And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith from al-Jurayri, from Abu Tamima, from Abu Uthman, from Abu Musa, except Ismail ibn Ibrahim."
"2996","2994 - And Yahya ibn Hakim informed us: Abu Bahr al-Bakrawi informed us: Uthman ibn Ghiyath informed us, from Abu Uthman, from Abu Musa; and the wording in these hadiths and these chains is the wording of Khalid al-Hadhdha, from Abu Uthman, from Abu Musa (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: We were on a raid with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and we would not ascend an elevation nor rise upon an elevation, nor descend a valley - or he said: descend into a valley - except that we raised our voices with takbir. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) drew near us and said: O people, be gentle with yourselves; for you do not call upon one deaf nor absent. You only call upon One All-Hearing, All-Seeing. He whom you call is nearer to one of you than the neck of his mount. Then he said: O Abd Allah ibn Qays, shall I not teach you a word that is of the treasures of Paradise: there is no power nor strength except with Allah."
"2997","2995 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna ibn Ubayd narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Jafar informed us. He said: Shuba informed us. 2996 - And Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna informed us of it: Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi informed us: Shuba and al-Thawri informed us, both from Qays ibn Muslim, from Tariq ibn Shihab, from Abu Musa."
"2998","2997 - And Yahya ibn Hakim informed us of it: Muhammad ibn Abi Adi informed us, from Shuba, from Qays ibn Muslim, from Tariq ibn Shihab, from Abu Musa (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: I came from Yemen while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was at al-Batha. So he said: ""Did you perform hajj?"" I said: Yes. He said: ""How did you say?"" I said: Labbayk with an ihram like the ihram of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So he said: You did well; come to the House and circumambulate it, then run between al-Safa and al-Marwa, then release (from ihram). He said: So I came to the House and circumambulated it and (ran) between al-Safa and al-Marwa."
"2999","2998 - Bishr ibn Khalid al-Askari and Hawthara ibn Muhammad narrated to us, saying: Abu Usama informed us: Abu al-Umays informed us, from Qays ibn Muslim, from Tariq ibn Shihab, from Abu Musa al-Ashari (may Allah be pleased with him): that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded fasting Ashura - or he said: he used to fast it. Abu Bakr said: And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Qays ibn Muslim, from Tariq ibn Shihab, from Abu Musa, except Abu al-Umays."
"3000","2999 - Bishr ibn Adam ibn Bint Azhar al-Samman narrated to us: Zayd ibn al-Hubab informed us: Muhammad ibn Jabir informed us, from Qays ibn Muslim, from Tariq ibn Shihab, from Abu Musa (may Allah be pleased with him), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: ""Allah, blessed and exalted, did not send down any disease except that it has a cure. So upon you is cow's milk, for it pastures from every tree."" And this hadith was narrated by Shuba; so some of them narrated it from Shuba, from al-Rukayn ibn al-Rabi, from Qays ibn Muslim, from Tariq ibn Shihab, from Abd Allah ibn Masud; and some companions of Shuba narrated it from Shuba, from al-Rukayn ibn al-Rabi, from Qays, from Tariq ibn Shihab, from Abd Allah. And al-Thawri and al-Masudi narrated it from Qays ibn Muslim, from Tariq ibn Shihab, from Abd Allah. As for whoever narrated it from Shuba, from al-Rukayn ibn al-Rabi, from Qays ibn Muslim, from Tariq ibn Shihab:"
